INSERT INTO `paper_questions` VALUES (5850,'4da6b5cb',1814,'The chemical formula of water is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','H₂O'),(5851,'4da6b5cb',1815,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5852,'4da6b5cb',1816,'The SI unit of force is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(5853,'4da6b5cb',1817,'The basic unit of heredity is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(5854,'4da6b5cb',1818,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapour is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Transpiration'),(5855,'4da6b5cb',1819,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll.  It involves the conversion of carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen using light energy.'),(5856,'4da6b5cb',1820,'State Newton\'s third law of motion and give an example.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Newton\'s third law states that for every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.  Example: When you walk, you push backward on the ground, and the ground pushes forward on you, propelling you forward.'),(5857,'4da6b5cb',1821,'Explain the difference between a conductor and an insulator.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Conductors allow electric current to flow easily through them due to the presence of free electrons. Insulators resist the flow of electric current because they have very few free electrons.'),(5858,'4da6b5cb',1822,'Explain the concept of refraction of light.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to a change in the speed of light.'),(5859,'4da6b5cb',1823,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.  Include a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The right atrium receives deoxygenated blood from the body, and the right ventricle pumps it to the lungs. The left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lungs, and the left ventricle pumps it to the rest of the body.  A diagram showing the chambers, valves, and major blood vessels should be included.'),(5860,'4da6b5cb',1824,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox, and neutralization reactions. Each type should be explained with suitable chemical equations and examples.'),(5861,'4da6b5cb',1825,'Explain the process of digestion in the human body.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The answer should explain the process of digestion starting from the mouth, including mechanical and chemical digestion in the stomach and small intestine, absorption of nutrients, and the role of various digestive enzymes and organs.'),(5862,'4da6b5cb',1826,'Explain the working principle of an electric generator.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','An electric generator works on the principle of electromagnetic induction. When a coil of wire rotates in a magnetic field, an electric current is induced in the coil.  The answer should explain the role of the armature, magnets, slip rings, and brushes.'),(5863,'4da6b5cb',1827,'Match the following:\nColumn A\n1.  Acid Rain\n2.  Ozone layer\n3.  Global warming\n4.  Deforestation\nA.  Loss of forests\nB.  Increased CO2 levels\nC.  Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides\nD.  UV radiation protection','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-B, 4-A'),(5864,'4da6b5cb',1828,'A farmer noticed that his crop yield was decreasing year after year.  He suspected a deficiency of certain nutrients in the soil.  He conducted a soil test and found that the soil was lacking in nitrogen and phosphorus. \n(a) Explain the importance of nitrogen and phosphorus for plant growth. \n(b) Suggest methods to improve the nitrogen and phosphorus content of the soil. \n(c) What are the consequences of nutrient deficiency in plants?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is essential for chlorophyll synthesis and protein formation. Phosphorus is important for root development, flowering, and fruit formation.  (b) Methods to improve soil nutrient content include using nitrogenous and phosphatic fertilizers, crop rotation, and using organic manure. (c) Nutrient deficiencies can lead to stunted growth, reduced yield, chlorosis (yellowing of leaves), and eventually plant death.'),(5865,'4da6b5cb',1817,'The basic unit of heredity is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(5866,'4da6b5cb',1819,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll.  It involves the conversion of carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen using light energy.'),(5867,'4da6b5cb',1826,'Explain the working principle of an electric generator.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','An electric generator works on the principle of electromagnetic induction. When a coil of wire rotates in a magnetic field, an electric current is induced in the coil.  The answer should explain the role of the armature, magnets, slip rings, and brushes.'),(5868,'4da6b5cb',1824,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox, and neutralization reactions. Each type should be explained with suitable chemical equations and examples.'),(5869,'71e9de08',1829,'The process of converting a solid directly into gas is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Sublimation'),(5870,'71e9de08',1830,'The focal length of a concave mirror is always _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','negative'),(5871,'71e9de08',1831,'The unit of power is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(5872,'71e9de08',1832,'The process by which plants make their own food is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5873,'71e9de08',1833,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s chemical composition remains the same.  Examples include melting ice, tearing paper.  A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition, resulting in the formation of a new substance. Examples include burning wood, rusting iron.'),(5874,'71e9de08',1834,'State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Limitations include its non-applicability to non-ohmic conductors (like diodes) and its breakdown at high temperatures or voltages.'),(5875,'71e9de08',1835,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Respiration is the process of exchanging gases between an organism and its environment. In humans, it involves taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. This process occurs through the lungs, where oxygen from the inhaled air diffuses into the bloodstream and carbon dioxide from the blood diffuses into the air to be exhaled.'),(5876,'71e9de08',1836,'What are the different types of lenses and their uses?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex (converging) and concave (diverging). Convex lenses are used in magnifying glasses, cameras, and eyeglasses for farsightedness. Concave lenses are used in eyeglasses for nearsightedness and telescopes.'),(5877,'71e9de08',1837,'Describe the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the balanced chemical equation and factors affecting the rate of photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll. The balanced chemical equation is 6CO2 + 6H2O + Sunlight → C6H12O6 + 6O2. Factors affecting the rate include light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, temperature, and water availability.'),(5878,'71e9de08',1838,'Explain the structure and functioning of the human heart. Draw a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The right atrium receives deoxygenated blood from the body, which is pumped to the right ventricle and then to the lungs for oxygenation. The left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lungs, which is pumped to the left ventricle and then to the rest of the body.  (Diagram should be included)'),(5879,'71e9de08',1839,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into various types, including combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox (oxidation-reduction), and neutralization reactions.  Each type should be explained with examples like the formation of water (combination), decomposition of calcium carbonate (decomposition), iron reacting with copper sulfate (displacement), etc.'),(5880,'71e9de08',1840,'Explain the Mendelian laws of inheritance with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Mendelian laws of inheritance include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment. The law of segregation states that during gamete formation, the alleles for each gene segregate from each other so that each gamete carries only one allele for each gene. The law of independent assortment states that during gamete formation, the segregation of the alleles for one gene occurs independently of the segregation of alleles for other genes. Examples should be given using monohybrid and dihybrid crosses.'),(5881,'71e9de08',1841,'Match the following:','Matching','Medium',4,'null','A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3'),(5882,'71e9de08',1842,'A farmer observes that his crop yield is decreasing year after year. He suspects that the soil is lacking in essential nutrients.  Discuss the possible reasons for decreased crop yield, the role of fertilizers, and sustainable agricultural practices he can adopt to improve soil health and crop production.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','Possible reasons include nutrient depletion, soil erosion, pest infestation, and water scarcity. Fertilizers replenish essential nutrients, but overuse can lead to environmental problems. Sustainable practices include crop rotation, intercropping, using organic fertilizers, and water conservation techniques.'),(5883,'71e9de08',1815,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5884,'71e9de08',1814,'The chemical formula of water is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','H₂O'),(5885,'71e9de08',1833,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s chemical composition remains the same.  Examples include melting ice, tearing paper.  A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition, resulting in the formation of a new substance. Examples include burning wood, rusting iron.'),(5886,'71e9de08',1837,'Describe the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the balanced chemical equation and factors affecting the rate of photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll. The balanced chemical equation is 6CO2 + 6H2O + Sunlight → C6H12O6 + 6O2. Factors affecting the rate include light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, temperature, and water availability.'),(5887,'71e9de08',1839,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into various types, including combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox (oxidation-reduction), and neutralization reactions.  Each type should be explained with examples like the formation of water (combination), decomposition of calcium carbonate (decomposition), iron reacting with copper sulfate (displacement), etc.'),(5888,'f64db2dc',1843,'The SI unit of electric current is ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Ampere'),(5889,'f64db2dc',1844,'The focal length of a concave mirror is always ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','negative'),(5890,'f64db2dc',1845,'The process of converting nitrogen gas into nitrogenous compounds is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Nitrogen fixation'),(5891,'f64db2dc',1846,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(5892,'f64db2dc',1847,'The unit of power is ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(5893,'f64db2dc',1848,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of water vapor is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Transpiration'),(5894,'f64db2dc',1849,'Explain the difference between a physical and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(5895,'f64db2dc',1850,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression. Draw a circuit diagram to verify Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR. (A circuit diagram showing a battery, resistor, ammeter, and voltmeter connected in series should be included).'),(5896,'f64db2dc',1851,'Differentiate between mitosis and meiosis. Mention the significance of each.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Mitosis is a type of cell division that produces two identical daughter cells, while meiosis produces four genetically different haploid cells. Mitosis is for growth and repair; meiosis is for sexual reproduction.'),(5897,'f64db2dc',1852,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light. Explain the phenomenon with a diagram.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to change in speed. (A suitable diagram showing the refraction of light from air to water or glass should be included.)'),(5898,'f64db2dc',1853,'Describe the process of photosynthesis. Explain its significance in the ecosystem.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It involves the use of carbon dioxide and water in the presence of chlorophyll and sunlight. The products are glucose and oxygen. Photosynthesis is crucial for the ecosystem as it forms the base of most food chains and produces oxygen.'),(5899,'f64db2dc',1854,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.  Include a labelled diagram.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','(A detailed description of the heart\'s structure, including atria, ventricles, valves, and blood vessels. Explanation of the double circulation system and its significance is needed. A labeled diagram showing the four chambers and major blood vessels is essential)'),(5900,'f64db2dc',1855,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection. Provide suitable examples.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','(The answer should explain the concepts of variation, inheritance, overproduction, struggle for existence, and survival of the fittest. Examples like Darwin\'s finches or the peppered moth should be included.)'),(5901,'f64db2dc',1856,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','(The answer should describe various types of chemical reactions such as combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions with suitable examples for each.)'),(5902,'f64db2dc',1857,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:','Matching','Medium',4,'null','A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4'),(5903,'f64db2dc',1858,'A student conducted an experiment to study the effect of different fertilizers on plant growth.  Three different fertilizers (A, B, C) were used on three separate plants of the same species, grown under identical conditions. After a month, the height of the plants was measured. Plant with fertilizer A grew 10 cm, B grew 15 cm, and C grew 8cm.  Analyze the results and answer the following questions: a) Which fertilizer was most effective?  b) What are the possible sources of error in this experiment?  c) How could the experiment be improved? ','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','a) Fertilizer B was the most effective. b) Possible errors include variations in soil composition, amount of sunlight received, or water quantity. c) Improvements could include using more plants per fertilizer type, controlled environmental conditions, precise measurement tools, and statistical analysis of the results.'),(5904,'f64db2dc',1834,'State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Limitations include its non-applicability to non-ohmic conductors (like diodes) and its breakdown at high temperatures or voltages.'),(5905,'f64db2dc',1824,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox, and neutralization reactions. Each type should be explained with suitable chemical equations and examples.'),(5906,'f64db2dc',1837,'Describe the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the balanced chemical equation and factors affecting the rate of photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll. The balanced chemical equation is 6CO2 + 6H2O + Sunlight → C6H12O6 + 6O2. Factors affecting the rate include light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, temperature, and water availability.'),(5907,'a22c1fbf',1859,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5908,'a22c1fbf',1860,'The SI unit of force is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(5909,'a22c1fbf',1861,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(5910,'a22c1fbf',1862,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(5911,'a22c1fbf',1863,'The resistance of a wire is directly proportional to its ______________ and inversely proportional to its ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',2,'null','length, cross-sectional area'),(5912,'a22c1fbf',1864,'The nucleus of an atom contains ______________ and ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',2,'null','protons, neutrons'),(5913,'a22c1fbf',1865,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but not its chemical composition.  A chemical change involves the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(5914,'a22c1fbf',1866,'What is the role of ozone in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ozone in the stratosphere absorbs harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(5915,'a22c1fbf',1867,'State Ohm\'s Law.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across it, provided the temperature remains constant.'),(5916,'a22c1fbf',1868,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to a change in speed.'),(5917,'a22c1fbf',1869,'Explain the process of binary fission.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Binary fission is a type of asexual reproduction in which a single parent cell divides into two identical daughter cells.'),(5918,'a22c1fbf',1870,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','The human respiratory system consists of the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs.  Its function is to take in oxygen and expel carbon dioxide.'),(5919,'a22c1fbf',1871,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Different types include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples of each should be provided.'),(5920,'a22c1fbf',1872,'Explain the working principle of an electric generator.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','An electric generator works on the principle of electromagnetic induction. When a coil rotates in a magnetic field, an electric current is induced in the coil.'),(5921,'a22c1fbf',1873,'Discuss the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Air, water, and soil pollution should be discussed, including their sources and harmful effects.'),(5922,'a22c1fbf',1874,'Explain the process of photosynthesis and its significance.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It\'s essential for the food chain and oxygen production.'),(5923,'a22c1fbf',1875,'Describe the structure and functions of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','The nervous system includes the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system.  Explain its role in coordinating body functions.'),(5924,'a22c1fbf',1876,'Match the following terms with their definitions:','Matching','Medium',5,'null','Correct matching of terms and definitions should be provided.  This would require a table of terms and definitions.'),(5925,'a22c1fbf',1877,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. The leaves are yellowing, and the plants are stunted.  He suspects a nutrient deficiency.  Discuss the possible causes of this problem and suggest solutions.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','The answer should include a discussion of nutrient deficiencies (e.g., nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium), soil testing, and appropriate fertilizer application.'),(5926,'30f9f8de',1848,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of water vapor is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Transpiration'),(5927,'30f9f8de',1846,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(5928,'30f9f8de',1815,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5929,'30f9f8de',1830,'The focal length of a concave mirror is always _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','negative'),(5930,'30f9f8de',1816,'The SI unit of force is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(5931,'30f9f8de',1817,'The basic unit of heredity is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(5932,'30f9f8de',1820,'State Newton\'s third law of motion and give an example.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Newton\'s third law states that for every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.  Example: When you walk, you push backward on the ground, and the ground pushes forward on you, propelling you forward.'),(5933,'30f9f8de',1836,'What are the different types of lenses and their uses?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex (converging) and concave (diverging). Convex lenses are used in magnifying glasses, cameras, and eyeglasses for farsightedness. Concave lenses are used in eyeglasses for nearsightedness and telescopes.'),(5934,'30f9f8de',1834,'State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Limitations include its non-applicability to non-ohmic conductors (like diodes) and its breakdown at high temperatures or voltages.'),(5935,'30f9f8de',1852,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light. Explain the phenomenon with a diagram.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to change in speed. (A suitable diagram showing the refraction of light from air to water or glass should be included.)'),(5936,'30f9f8de',1835,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Respiration is the process of exchanging gases between an organism and its environment. In humans, it involves taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. This process occurs through the lungs, where oxygen from the inhaled air diffuses into the bloodstream and carbon dioxide from the blood diffuses into the air to be exhaled.'),(5937,'30f9f8de',1823,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.  Include a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The right atrium receives deoxygenated blood from the body, and the right ventricle pumps it to the lungs. The left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lungs, and the left ventricle pumps it to the rest of the body.  A diagram showing the chambers, valves, and major blood vessels should be included.'),(5938,'30f9f8de',1838,'Explain the structure and functioning of the human heart. Draw a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The right atrium receives deoxygenated blood from the body, which is pumped to the right ventricle and then to the lungs for oxygenation. The left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lungs, which is pumped to the left ventricle and then to the rest of the body.  (Diagram should be included)'),(5939,'30f9f8de',1825,'Explain the process of digestion in the human body.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The answer should explain the process of digestion starting from the mouth, including mechanical and chemical digestion in the stomach and small intestine, absorption of nutrients, and the role of various digestive enzymes and organs.'),(5940,'30f9f8de',1824,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox, and neutralization reactions. Each type should be explained with suitable chemical equations and examples.'),(5941,'30f9f8de',1853,'Describe the process of photosynthesis. Explain its significance in the ecosystem.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It involves the use of carbon dioxide and water in the presence of chlorophyll and sunlight. The products are glucose and oxygen. Photosynthesis is crucial for the ecosystem as it forms the base of most food chains and produces oxygen.'),(5942,'30f9f8de',1840,'Explain the Mendelian laws of inheritance with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Mendelian laws of inheritance include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment. The law of segregation states that during gamete formation, the alleles for each gene segregate from each other so that each gamete carries only one allele for each gene. The law of independent assortment states that during gamete formation, the segregation of the alleles for one gene occurs independently of the segregation of alleles for other genes. Examples should be given using monohybrid and dihybrid crosses.'),(5943,'30f9f8de',1841,'Match the following:','Matching','Medium',4,'null','A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3'),(5944,'30f9f8de',1828,'A farmer noticed that his crop yield was decreasing year after year.  He suspected a deficiency of certain nutrients in the soil.  He conducted a soil test and found that the soil was lacking in nitrogen and phosphorus. \n(a) Explain the importance of nitrogen and phosphorus for plant growth. \n(b) Suggest methods to improve the nitrogen and phosphorus content of the soil. \n(c) What are the consequences of nutrient deficiency in plants?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is essential for chlorophyll synthesis and protein formation. Phosphorus is important for root development, flowering, and fruit formation.  (b) Methods to improve soil nutrient content include using nitrogenous and phosphatic fertilizers, crop rotation, and using organic manure. (c) Nutrient deficiencies can lead to stunted growth, reduced yield, chlorosis (yellowing of leaves), and eventually plant death.'),(5945,'6092c434',1895,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transpiration\"]','D'),(5946,'6092c434',1896,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(5947,'6092c434',1897,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon Dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(5948,'6092c434',1898,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Zero\", \"Infinity\", \"10cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(5949,'6092c434',1899,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\"]','D'),(5950,'6092c434',1900,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5951,'6092c434',1901,'The force of attraction between the earth and an object is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravity'),(5952,'6092c434',1902,'The unit of power is the _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(5953,'6092c434',1903,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(5954,'6092c434',1904,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(5955,'6092c434',1905,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Not provided'),(5956,'6092c434',1906,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Not provided'),(5957,'6092c434',1907,'What is the role of ozone in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Not provided'),(5958,'6092c434',1908,'Describe the structure of an atom.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Not provided'),(5959,'6092c434',1909,'Explain the concept of electric potential.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Not provided'),(5960,'6092c434',1910,'What are the different types of asexual reproduction?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Not provided'),(5961,'6092c434',1911,'Explain the process of digestion in humans.  Include a labelled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Not provided'),(5962,'6092c434',1912,'Describe the various types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Not provided'),(5963,'6092c434',1913,'Explain Ohm\'s Law and its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Not provided'),(5964,'6092c434',1914,'Discuss the different types of lenses and their uses.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Not provided'),(5965,'6092c434',1915,'Explain the carbon cycle and its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Not provided'),(5966,'6092c434',1916,'Match the following terms with their definitions:','Matching','Medium',5,'null','Not provided'),(5967,'6092c434',1917,'A farmer noticed that his crops were not growing well despite regular watering and fertilization. He suspected a problem with the soil.  Discuss the various factors that could affect soil health and suggest solutions the farmer could implement to improve crop growth.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','Not provided'),(5968,'ac1ba3a9',1918,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(5969,'ac1ba3a9',1919,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(5970,'ac1ba3a9',1920,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(5971,'ac1ba3a9',1921,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(5972,'ac1ba3a9',1922,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(5973,'ac1ba3a9',1923,'What is the pH of a neutral solution?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"0\", \"7\", \"14\", \"3\"]','B'),(5974,'ac1ba3a9',1924,'The process by which plants make their own food is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(5975,'ac1ba3a9',1925,'The SI unit of force is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(5976,'ac1ba3a9',1926,'The process of converting a gas into a liquid is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Condensation'),(5977,'ac1ba3a9',1927,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(5978,'ac1ba3a9',1928,'The basic unit of heredity is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(5979,'ac1ba3a9',1929,'The nucleus of an atom contains ______________ and ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','protons, neutrons'),(5980,'ac1ba3a9',1930,'The process of asexual reproduction in which a new organism develops from an outgrowth or bud is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','budding'),(5981,'ac1ba3a9',1931,'The bending of light as it passes from one medium to another is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','refraction'),(5982,'ac1ba3a9',1932,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in the form or state of matter, while a chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of the substance.'),(5983,'ac1ba3a9',1933,'What is the role of ozone in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ozone layer absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun.'),(5984,'ac1ba3a9',1934,'Define the terms \'acid\' and \'base\'. Give one example of each.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Acids are substances that release hydrogen ions (H+) when dissolved in water. Bases are substances that release hydroxide ions (OH-) when dissolved in water. Example of acid: HCl (Hydrochloric acid). Example of base: NaOH (Sodium hydroxide).'),(5985,'ac1ba3a9',1935,'What is Newton\'s third law of motion? Give an example.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.  Example: When you walk, you push backward on the ground, and the ground pushes you forward.'),(5986,'ac1ba3a9',1936,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide.  It involves the intake of air into the lungs, the exchange of gases between the lungs and the blood, and the transport of oxygen to the body\'s cells.'),(5987,'ac1ba3a9',1937,'What are the different types of blood groups?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The main blood groups are A, B, AB, and O.'),(5988,'ac1ba3a9',1938,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood from the body and the lungs, and the ventricles pump blood to the body and the lungs. The heart valves ensure that blood flows in one direction.'),(5989,'ac1ba3a9',1939,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(5990,'ac1ba3a9',1940,'Explain the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Pollution can be air, water, or land pollution. Air pollution can cause respiratory problems, water pollution can contaminate drinking water, and land pollution can harm soil and wildlife.  The effects include climate change, acid rain, depletion of the ozone layer, and loss of biodiversity.'),(5991,'ac1ba3a9',1941,'Describe the structure and function of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The human nervous system is composed of the brain, spinal cord, and nerves. It controls and coordinates all bodily functions.  The brain receives and processes information from the senses, and the spinal cord relays information between the brain and the rest of the body.'),(5992,'ac1ba3a9',1942,'Explain the laws of reflection of light.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The laws of reflection state that: (1) The angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection. (2) The incident ray, the reflected ray, and the normal at the point of incidence all lie in the same plane.'),(5993,'ac1ba3a9',1943,'Explain Mendel\'s laws of inheritance.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Mendel\'s laws of inheritance describe how traits are passed from parents to offspring.  The law of segregation states that each parent contributes one allele for each gene to its offspring. The law of independent assortment states that different genes are inherited independently of each other.'),(5994,'ac1ba3a9',1944,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Force\n2.  Energy\n3.  Power\n4.  Pressure\n\nColumn B\nA.  Joule\nB.  Newton\nC.  Pascal\nD.  Watt','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-D, 4-C'),(5995,'ac1ba3a9',1945,'A farmer notices that his crops are not growing well. He suspects a lack of essential nutrients in the soil. He conducts a soil test and finds that the soil is deficient in nitrogen. \n\n(a) What is the importance of nitrogen for plant growth?\n(b) What are some ways to improve the nitrogen content of the soil?\n(c) What are the potential negative impacts of using excessive nitrogen fertilizers?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is a crucial component of chlorophyll and proteins, essential for plant growth and development. (b) Ways to improve nitrogen content include using nitrogen-rich fertilizers, crop rotation, using cover crops, and composting organic matter. (c) Excessive nitrogen fertilizers can lead to water pollution (eutrophication), soil acidification, and harm beneficial soil microorganisms.'),(5996,'28ab80e7',1919,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(5997,'ca027cc1',1897,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon Dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(5998,'28ab80e7',1896,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(5999,'28ab80e7',1895,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transpiration\"]','D'),(6000,'ca027cc1',1922,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6001,'28ab80e7',1923,'What is the pH of a neutral solution?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"0\", \"7\", \"14\", \"3\"]','B'),(6002,'ca027cc1',1919,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6003,'28ab80e7',1922,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6004,'ca027cc1',1895,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transpiration\"]','D'),(6005,'ca027cc1',1921,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6006,'28ab80e7',1899,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\"]','D'),(6007,'ca027cc1',1814,'The chemical formula of water is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','H₂O'),(6008,'28ab80e7',1931,'The bending of light as it passes from one medium to another is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','refraction'),(6009,'ca027cc1',1844,'The focal length of a concave mirror is always ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','negative'),(6010,'28ab80e7',1904,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6011,'ca027cc1',1927,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6012,'28ab80e7',1861,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6013,'28ab80e7',1815,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6014,'ca027cc1',1862,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6015,'28ab80e7',1930,'The process of asexual reproduction in which a new organism develops from an outgrowth or bud is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','budding'),(6016,'ca027cc1',1816,'The SI unit of force is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6017,'28ab80e7',1924,'The process by which plants make their own food is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6018,'ca027cc1',1830,'The focal length of a concave mirror is always _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','negative'),(6019,'28ab80e7',1860,'The SI unit of force is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6020,'28ab80e7',1848,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of water vapor is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6021,'ca027cc1',1850,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression. Draw a circuit diagram to verify Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR. (A circuit diagram showing a battery, resistor, ammeter, and voltmeter connected in series should be included).'),(6022,'28ab80e7',1821,'Explain the difference between a conductor and an insulator.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Conductors allow electric current to flow easily through them due to the presence of free electrons. Insulators resist the flow of electric current because they have very few free electrons.'),(6023,'28ab80e7',1833,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s chemical composition remains the same.  Examples include melting ice, tearing paper.  A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition, resulting in the formation of a new substance. Examples include burning wood, rusting iron.'),(6024,'ca027cc1',1849,'Explain the difference between a physical and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6025,'28ab80e7',1822,'Explain the concept of refraction of light.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to a change in the speed of light.'),(6026,'ca027cc1',1836,'What are the different types of lenses and their uses?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex (converging) and concave (diverging). Convex lenses are used in magnifying glasses, cameras, and eyeglasses for farsightedness. Concave lenses are used in eyeglasses for nearsightedness and telescopes.'),(6027,'28ab80e7',1820,'State Newton\'s third law of motion and give an example.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Newton\'s third law states that for every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.  Example: When you walk, you push backward on the ground, and the ground pushes forward on you, propelling you forward.'),(6028,'ca027cc1',1833,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s chemical composition remains the same.  Examples include melting ice, tearing paper.  A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition, resulting in the formation of a new substance. Examples include burning wood, rusting iron.'),(6029,'28ab80e7',1852,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light. Explain the phenomenon with a diagram.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to change in speed. (A suitable diagram showing the refraction of light from air to water or glass should be included.)'),(6030,'ca027cc1',1821,'Explain the difference between a conductor and an insulator.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Conductors allow electric current to flow easily through them due to the presence of free electrons. Insulators resist the flow of electric current because they have very few free electrons.'),(6031,'28ab80e7',1835,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Respiration is the process of exchanging gases between an organism and its environment. In humans, it involves taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. This process occurs through the lungs, where oxygen from the inhaled air diffuses into the bloodstream and carbon dioxide from the blood diffuses into the air to be exhaled.'),(6032,'ca027cc1',1837,'Describe the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the balanced chemical equation and factors affecting the rate of photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll. The balanced chemical equation is 6CO2 + 6H2O + Sunlight → C6H12O6 + 6O2. Factors affecting the rate include light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, temperature, and water availability.'),(6033,'28ab80e7',1856,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','(The answer should describe various types of chemical reactions such as combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions with suitable examples for each.)'),(6034,'ca027cc1',1856,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','(The answer should describe various types of chemical reactions such as combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions with suitable examples for each.)'),(6035,'28ab80e7',1840,'Explain the Mendelian laws of inheritance with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Mendelian laws of inheritance include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment. The law of segregation states that during gamete formation, the alleles for each gene segregate from each other so that each gamete carries only one allele for each gene. The law of independent assortment states that during gamete formation, the segregation of the alleles for one gene occurs independently of the segregation of alleles for other genes. Examples should be given using monohybrid and dihybrid crosses.'),(6036,'ca027cc1',1855,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection. Provide suitable examples.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','(The answer should explain the concepts of variation, inheritance, overproduction, struggle for existence, and survival of the fittest. Examples like Darwin\'s finches or the peppered moth should be included.)'),(6037,'28ab80e7',1826,'Explain the working principle of an electric generator.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','An electric generator works on the principle of electromagnetic induction. When a coil of wire rotates in a magnetic field, an electric current is induced in the coil.  The answer should explain the role of the armature, magnets, slip rings, and brushes.'),(6038,'ca027cc1',1839,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into various types, including combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox (oxidation-reduction), and neutralization reactions.  Each type should be explained with examples like the formation of water (combination), decomposition of calcium carbonate (decomposition), iron reacting with copper sulfate (displacement), etc.'),(6039,'28ab80e7',1855,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection. Provide suitable examples.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','(The answer should explain the concepts of variation, inheritance, overproduction, struggle for existence, and survival of the fittest. Examples like Darwin\'s finches or the peppered moth should be included.)'),(6040,'28ab80e7',1853,'Describe the process of photosynthesis. Explain its significance in the ecosystem.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It involves the use of carbon dioxide and water in the presence of chlorophyll and sunlight. The products are glucose and oxygen. Photosynthesis is crucial for the ecosystem as it forms the base of most food chains and produces oxygen.'),(6041,'ca027cc1',1825,'Explain the process of digestion in the human body.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The answer should explain the process of digestion starting from the mouth, including mechanical and chemical digestion in the stomach and small intestine, absorption of nutrients, and the role of various digestive enzymes and organs.'),(6042,'28ab80e7',1839,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into various types, including combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox (oxidation-reduction), and neutralization reactions.  Each type should be explained with examples like the formation of water (combination), decomposition of calcium carbonate (decomposition), iron reacting with copper sulfate (displacement), etc.'),(6043,'28ab80e7',1827,'Match the following:\nColumn A\n1.  Acid Rain\n2.  Ozone layer\n3.  Global warming\n4.  Deforestation\nA.  Loss of forests\nB.  Increased CO2 levels\nC.  Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides\nD.  UV radiation protection','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-B, 4-A'),(6044,'ca027cc1',1827,'Match the following:\nColumn A\n1.  Acid Rain\n2.  Ozone layer\n3.  Global warming\n4.  Deforestation\nA.  Loss of forests\nB.  Increased CO2 levels\nC.  Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides\nD.  UV radiation protection','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-B, 4-A'),(6045,'ca027cc1',1945,'A farmer notices that his crops are not growing well. He suspects a lack of essential nutrients in the soil. He conducts a soil test and finds that the soil is deficient in nitrogen. \n\n(a) What is the importance of nitrogen for plant growth?\n(b) What are some ways to improve the nitrogen content of the soil?\n(c) What are the potential negative impacts of using excessive nitrogen fertilizers?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is a crucial component of chlorophyll and proteins, essential for plant growth and development. (b) Ways to improve nitrogen content include using nitrogen-rich fertilizers, crop rotation, using cover crops, and composting organic matter. (c) Excessive nitrogen fertilizers can lead to water pollution (eutrophication), soil acidification, and harm beneficial soil microorganisms.'),(6046,'28ab80e7',1917,'A farmer noticed that his crops were not growing well despite regular watering and fertilization. He suspected a problem with the soil.  Discuss the various factors that could affect soil health and suggest solutions the farmer could implement to improve crop growth.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','Not provided'),(6047,'6e0ae149',1946,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6048,'6e0ae149',1947,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6049,'6e0ae149',1948,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6050,'6e0ae149',1949,'Which gas is mainly responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6051,'6e0ae149',1950,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Zero\", \"Infinity\", \"10 cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(6052,'6e0ae149',1951,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6053,'6e0ae149',1952,'The SI unit of force is the _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6054,'6e0ae149',1953,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6055,'6e0ae149',1954,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of water vapor is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6056,'6e0ae149',1955,'The nucleus of an atom contains _________ and _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','protons, neutrons'),(6057,'6e0ae149',1956,'The resistance of a conductor is directly proportional to its _________ and inversely proportional to its _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','length, cross-sectional area'),(6058,'6e0ae149',1957,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition, while a chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(6059,'6e0ae149',1958,'What are the main components of blood?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Red blood cells, white blood cells, platelets, and plasma.'),(6060,'6e0ae149',1959,'State Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.'),(6061,'6e0ae149',1960,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Reflection is the bouncing back of light from a surface, while refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.'),(6062,'6e0ae149',1961,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves the intake of air into the lungs, diffusion of oxygen into the blood, transport of oxygen to cells, cellular respiration, and the release of carbon dioxide.'),(6063,'6e0ae149',1962,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each.'),(6064,'6e0ae149',1963,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The structure and function of each chamber should be detailed, along with the role of valves.'),(6065,'6e0ae149',1964,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  What are its importance?','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce glucose and oxygen. The equation and steps should be described, along with its importance for life on Earth (oxygen production, food source).'),(6066,'6e0ae149',1965,'Explain the different types of lenses and their uses.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Convex and concave lenses should be described, along with their properties (converging/diverging) and applications (eyeglasses, telescopes, microscopes).'),(6067,'6e0ae149',1966,'Discuss the various methods of preventing pollution of air and water.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Air and water pollution prevention methods should be discussed, including using renewable energy sources, proper waste management, industrial regulations, and public awareness campaigns.'),(6068,'6e0ae149',1967,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Sodium Chloride\n2.  Hydrochloric Acid\n3.  Sodium Hydroxide\n4.  Carbon Dioxide\n\nColumn B\nA. Acid\nB. Base\nC. Salt\nD. Oxide','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B, 4-D'),(6069,'6e0ae149',1968,'A student performs an experiment to study the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction.  They mix two chemicals at different temperatures and observe the time taken for the reaction to complete.  At lower temperatures, the reaction takes longer. At higher temperatures, it is faster. \n\n(a) Explain why the rate of reaction changes with temperature. \n(b)  What is the term used to describe the increase in the rate of reaction with temperature?\n(c)  What is the effect of temperature on the kinetic energy of molecules?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) At higher temperatures, molecules have higher kinetic energy, leading to more frequent and energetic collisions, increasing the rate of reaction. (b) Activation energy. (c) Increased kinetic energy with increased temperature.'),(6070,'f5570c0c',1969,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6071,'f5570c0c',1970,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6072,'f5570c0c',1971,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6073,'f5570c0c',1972,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6074,'f5570c0c',1973,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6075,'f5570c0c',1974,'What is the name of the process by which plants make their food?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Excretion\"]','B'),(6076,'f5570c0c',1975,'The SI unit of force is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6077,'f5570c0c',1976,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6078,'f5570c0c',1977,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6079,'f5570c0c',1978,'The basic unit of heredity is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(6080,'f5570c0c',1979,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6081,'f5570c0c',1980,'The resistance of a conductor is inversely proportional to its _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cross-sectional area'),(6082,'f5570c0c',1981,'The force of attraction between two bodies due to their masses is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gravitation'),(6083,'f5570c0c',1982,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in which no new substance is formed, while a chemical change involves the formation of a new substance.'),(6084,'f5570c0c',1983,'What are the different types of reproduction?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The two main types of reproduction are asexual and sexual reproduction.'),(6085,'f5570c0c',1984,'State Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature remains constant.'),(6086,'f5570c0c',1985,'What is the role of decomposers in an ecosystem?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Decomposers break down dead organic matter, releasing nutrients back into the ecosystem.'),(6087,'f5570c0c',1986,'Explain the concept of inertia.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Inertia is the tendency of an object to resist changes in its state of motion.'),(6088,'f5570c0c',1987,'What are the different states of matter?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three common states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas.'),(6089,'f5570c0c',1988,'Describe the process of photosynthesis in detail.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll.  It involves the conversion of light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The process takes place in chloroplasts and requires carbon dioxide, water, and sunlight.  Oxygen is released as a byproduct.'),(6090,'f5570c0c',1989,'Explain Newton\'s three laws of motion with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Newton\'s three laws of motion are: 1. Law of Inertia: An object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.  2. F=ma (Force equals mass times acceleration): The acceleration of an object is directly proportional to the net force acting on the object and inversely proportional to its mass. 3. For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6091,'f5570c0c',1990,'Discuss the structure and functions of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs.  Its main function is gas exchange: taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide.'),(6092,'f5570c0c',1991,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6093,'f5570c0c',1992,'Explain the process of digestion in humans.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The digestive system breaks down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream.  The process involves mechanical and chemical digestion, and several organs play important roles.'),(6094,'f5570c0c',1993,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The heart\'s function is to circulate blood, carrying oxygen and nutrients to the body\'s tissues and removing waste products.'),(6095,'f5570c0c',1994,'Explain the concept of electric current and potential difference.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Electric current is the flow of electric charge, while potential difference is the driving force that causes this flow.  They are related by Ohm\'s law.'),(6096,'f5570c0c',1995,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Transpiration\n4.  Excretion\n\nColumn B\nA. Removal of waste products\nB. Release of energy from food\nC. Water loss from leaves\nD. Making food using sunlight','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-B, 3-C, 4-A'),(6097,'f5570c0c',1996,'A student is conducting an experiment to investigate the effect of different fertilizers on plant growth.  Three groups of plants are grown under identical conditions, except for the type of fertilizer used.  Group A receives fertilizer X, Group B receives fertilizer Y, and Group C receives no fertilizer (control). After several weeks, the height and overall health of the plants are measured.\n\n(a) What is the independent variable in this experiment?\n(b) What is the dependent variable?\n(c) What is the purpose of Group C (control group)?\n(d) What are some possible sources of error in this experiment?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Type of fertilizer\n(b) Plant height and health\n(c) To provide a baseline for comparison\n(d) Differences in sunlight, water, soil quality, and initial plant size.'),(6098,'c2530c63',1997,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6099,'c2530c63',1998,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6100,'c2530c63',1999,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6101,'c2530c63',2000,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6102,'c2530c63',2001,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Cylindrical lens\", \"None of these\"]','B'),(6103,'c2530c63',2002,'What is the functional unit of the kidney?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Nephron\", \"Neuron\", \"Hepatocyte\", \"Osteocyte\"]','A'),(6104,'c2530c63',2003,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6105,'c2530c63',2004,'The force of attraction between the earth and an object is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravity'),(6106,'c2530c63',2005,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6107,'c2530c63',2006,'The basic unit of heredity is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(6108,'c2530c63',2007,'The process by which plants lose water vapor is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration'),(6109,'c2530c63',2008,'The SI unit of force is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6110,'c2530c63',2009,'The process of breaking down complex food molecules into simpler ones is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','digestion'),(6111,'c2530c63',2010,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but not its chemical composition, while a chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties.'),(6112,'c2530c63',2011,'What are the two types of lenses and how do they differ?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Convex lenses converge light rays, while concave lenses diverge light rays.  Convex lenses are thicker in the middle, concave lenses are thinner.'),(6113,'c2530c63',2012,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another. Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface.'),(6114,'c2530c63',2013,'What is the role of the nervous system in coordinating body functions?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The nervous system receives, processes, and transmits information, coordinating various body functions and responses to stimuli.'),(6115,'c2530c63',2014,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves inhalation, gas exchange in the lungs, and exhalation.'),(6116,'c2530c63',2015,'State two differences between mitosis and meiosis.','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','Mitosis produces two identical diploid daughter cells, while meiosis produces four genetically different haploid daughter cells. Mitosis occurs in somatic cells, while meiosis occurs in germ cells.'),(6117,'c2530c63',2016,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ with four chambers (two atria and two ventricles). It pumps blood throughout the body, carrying oxygen and nutrients to tissues and removing waste products.'),(6118,'c2530c63',2017,'Explain the process of photosynthesis, including the reactants, products, and importance.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy.  Reactants are carbon dioxide and water; products are glucose and oxygen. It\'s crucial for producing food and releasing oxygen.'),(6119,'c2530c63',2018,'Explain the different types of blood groups and the concept of blood transfusion.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Blood groups (A, B, AB, O) are determined by antigens on red blood cells.  Blood transfusions require matching blood types to avoid agglutination (clumping).'),(6120,'c2530c63',2019,'Describe the structure and function of the human eye.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human eye is a complex organ that allows us to see.  It contains various structures such as the cornea, lens, iris, retina, etc. which work together to form images.'),(6121,'c2530c63',2020,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants reproduce through asexual reproduction (vegetative propagation, budding, etc.) and sexual reproduction (pollination, fertilization, seed formation).'),(6122,'c2530c63',2021,'Explain Newton\'s three laws of motion with examples.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Newton\'s laws describe the relationship between force and motion: 1. Inertia: a body at rest stays at rest unless acted upon; 2. F=ma; 3. Action-reaction.'),(6123,'c2530c63',2022,'Explain the concept of evolution and the evidence that supports it.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Evolution is the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time.  Evidence includes fossil records, comparative anatomy, embryology, and molecular biology.'),(6124,'c2530c63',2023,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Ohm\'s Law\n2.  Power\n3.  Energy\n4.  Current\n\nColumn B\nA.  Joules\nB.  Watts\nC.  Amperes\nD.  V=IR','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-B, 3-A, 4-C'),(6125,'c2530c63',2024,'A student observes that a plant kept in a dark room for a week wilts and its leaves turn yellow. When the plant is moved to a sunny location, it recovers over a few days.\n\n(a) Explain why the plant wilted in the dark room.\n(b) Explain the role of sunlight in the recovery of the plant.\n(c) What is the significance of this observation related to a specific biological process?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) The plant wilted due to lack of photosynthesis; it couldn\'t produce glucose for energy.\n(b) Sunlight is essential for photosynthesis; the plant recovers by producing glucose and restoring water balance.\n(c) It demonstrates the importance of light for photosynthesis.'),(6126,'0ec3880f',2025,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6127,'0ec3880f',2026,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6128,'0ec3880f',2027,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6129,'0ec3880f',2028,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6130,'0ec3880f',2029,'Which process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Digestion\", \"Transpiration\"]','B'),(6131,'0ec3880f',2030,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"0\", \"Infinite\", \"10 cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(6132,'0ec3880f',2031,'The process of converting light energy into electrical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','photovoltaic effect'),(6133,'0ec3880f',2032,'The SI unit of force is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6134,'0ec3880f',2033,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6135,'0ec3880f',2034,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration'),(6136,'0ec3880f',2035,'The resistance of a conductor is directly proportional to its _______________ and inversely proportional to its _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','length, area of cross-section'),(6137,'0ec3880f',2036,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(6138,'0ec3880f',2037,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface. Refraction is the bending of light when it passes from one medium to another.'),(6139,'0ec3880f',2038,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s physical properties change but not its chemical composition.  A chemical change is a change in which new substances are formed.'),(6140,'0ec3880f',2039,'What is the role of ozone in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ozone layer in the stratosphere absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6141,'0ec3880f',2040,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  V = IR'),(6142,'0ec3880f',2041,'Explain the process of respiration in plants.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Plants take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide during respiration, releasing energy from glucose.'),(6143,'0ec3880f',2042,'Describe the structure of a neuron.','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','A neuron consists of a cell body (soma), dendrites, and an axon. Dendrites receive signals, the cell body processes them, and the axon transmits signals to other neurons.'),(6144,'0ec3880f',2043,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox, and neutralization reactions.  Examples should be provided for each.'),(6145,'0ec3880f',2044,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs. It facilitates gas exchange between the body and the environment.'),(6146,'0ec3880f',2045,'Explain the concept of heredity and variation with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Heredity is the passing of traits from parents to offspring. Variation is the differences in characteristics among individuals of the same species. Examples should be given to illustrate both concepts.'),(6147,'0ec3880f',2046,'Explain the different types of lenses and their applications.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Convex and concave lenses, their properties, and applications in spectacles, cameras, and microscopes should be described.'),(6148,'0ec3880f',2047,'Explain the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','A detailed description of the process, including the light-dependent and light-independent reactions, and its importance in providing food and oxygen.'),(6149,'0ec3880f',2048,'Explain the working of an electric motor and its applications.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The principle of electromagnetic induction, the components of an electric motor, and its various applications in fans, pumps, etc. should be discussed.'),(6150,'0ec3880f',2049,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\'s First Law\n2.  Newton\'s Second Law\n3.  Newton\'s Third Law\n\nColumn B\nA.  Force = mass × acceleration\nB.  For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction\nC.  An object at rest stays at rest, an object in motion stays in motion.','Matching','Medium',3,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B'),(6151,'0ec3880f',2050,'A student observed that a plant kept in a dark room for several days wilted and eventually died.  However, a similar plant kept in sunlight remained healthy.\n\n(a) Explain why the plant in the dark room died.\n(b) What process is essential for the survival of the plant in sunlight?\n(c) Name the green pigment involved in this process.','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) The plant died because it could not perform photosynthesis in the absence of sunlight. (b) Photosynthesis. (c) Chlorophyll.'),(6152,'c8b56ed7',2051,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6153,'c8b56ed7',2052,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6154,'c8b56ed7',2053,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6155,'c8b56ed7',2054,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6156,'c8b56ed7',2055,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6157,'c8b56ed7',2056,'What is the name of the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fermentation\"]','B'),(6158,'c8b56ed7',2057,'The process of converting light energy into electrical energy is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','photovoltaic'),(6159,'c8b56ed7',2058,'The basic unit of heredity is called a ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6160,'c8b56ed7',2059,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6161,'c8b56ed7',2060,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cohesion'),(6162,'c8b56ed7',2061,'The process by which the nucleus of an atom breaks down is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','nuclear fission'),(6163,'c8b56ed7',2062,'The SI unit of power is the ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','watt'),(6164,'c8b56ed7',2063,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6165,'c8b56ed7',2064,'What are the three states of matter? Briefly describe each.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a definite shape and volume, liquids have a definite volume but take the shape of their container, and gases have neither a definite shape nor volume.'),(6166,'c8b56ed7',2065,'Define Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6167,'c8b56ed7',2066,'What is the role of chlorophyll in photosynthesis?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light energy, which is then used to power the process of photosynthesis.'),(6168,'c8b56ed7',2067,'Explain the difference between a conductor and an insulator.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A conductor allows electricity to flow easily through it, while an insulator resists the flow of electricity.'),(6169,'c8b56ed7',2068,'What is the function of the human respiratory system?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The respiratory system is responsible for taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide.'),(6170,'c8b56ed7',2069,'Describe the process of digestion in humans, mentioning the different organs involved and their functions.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Digestion begins in the mouth with mechanical breakdown (chewing) and chemical breakdown (saliva).  The food then travels down the esophagus to the stomach, where it\'s mixed with gastric juices.  The small intestine is where most nutrient absorption occurs, aided by enzymes and bile from the liver and pancreas. Finally, undigested material moves to the large intestine for water absorption and elimination.'),(6171,'c8b56ed7',2070,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The heart is a muscular organ with four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  It pumps blood throughout the body, delivering oxygen and nutrients. The right side pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs, and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.'),(6172,'c8b56ed7',2071,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants reproduce both sexually (involving the fusion of gametes) and asexually (without fusion of gametes).  Sexual reproduction involves flowers and the production of seeds. Asexual reproduction methods include vegetative propagation (from stems, roots, or leaves).'),(6173,'c8b56ed7',2072,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples: Combination (2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O), Decomposition (2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂), Displacement (Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu), Double Displacement (AgNO₃ + NaCl → AgCl + NaNO₃), Redox (Zn + Cu²⁺ → Zn²⁺ + Cu).'),(6174,'c8b56ed7',2073,'Explain the concept of evolution and natural selection.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Evolution is the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time. Natural selection is the mechanism by which this change occurs. Organisms with traits better suited to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on those advantageous traits to their offspring.'),(6175,'c8b56ed7',2074,'Discuss the impact of human activities on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Human activities, such as deforestation, pollution, and overconsumption of resources, have significant negative impacts on the environment, leading to climate change, loss of biodiversity, and resource depletion. Sustainable practices are needed to mitigate these effects.'),(6176,'c8b56ed7',2075,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Charles Darwin\n3. Albert Einstein\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Theory of Evolution\nC. Laws of Inheritance','Matching','Medium',3,'null','1-C, 2-B, 3-A'),(6177,'c8b56ed7',2076,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. He notices yellowing leaves and stunted growth.  He suspects a nutrient deficiency in the soil.\n\n(a) What nutrient deficiency is likely causing this problem?\n(b) What are the sources of this nutrient?\n(c) How can the farmer address this nutrient deficiency?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a)  Nitrogen deficiency is a likely cause of yellowing leaves and stunted growth.\n(b) Sources of nitrogen include nitrogen-rich fertilizers (urea, ammonium nitrate), organic matter (compost, manure), and nitrogen-fixing bacteria in the soil.\n(c) The farmer can address this by applying nitrogen-rich fertilizers, incorporating organic matter into the soil, or promoting the growth of nitrogen-fixing bacteria through crop rotation or other sustainable practices.'),(6178,'3fb19461',2077,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6179,'3fb19461',2078,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6180,'3fb19461',2079,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6181,'3fb19461',2080,'What is the formula for calculating the speed of an object?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Distance × Time\", \"Distance / Time\", \"Time / Distance\", \"Distance + Time\"]','B'),(6182,'3fb19461',2081,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Plano-convex lens\", \"Plano-concave lens\"]','B'),(6183,'3fb19461',2082,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called __________.  The basic unit of heredity is a __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis, gene'),(6184,'3fb19461',2083,'Acids turn blue litmus paper __________, while bases turn red litmus paper __________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red, blue'),(6185,'3fb19461',2084,'The force of attraction between the earth and an object is called __________. The process of rusting is an example of __________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gravity, oxidation'),(6186,'3fb19461',2085,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called __________.  The unit of power is the __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration, watt'),(6187,'3fb19461',2086,'The resistance of a conductor is directly proportional to its __________ and inversely proportional to its __________.  Newton\'s second law states that force is equal to mass times __________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','length, area, acceleration'),(6188,'3fb19461',2087,'The nucleus of an atom contains __________ and __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','protons, neutrons'),(6189,'3fb19461',2088,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in which no new substance is formed, while a chemical change involves the formation of new substances. Examples: Physical - melting ice; Chemical - burning wood.'),(6190,'3fb19461',2089,'What are the three states of matter? Explain the properties of each state.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a fixed shape and volume. Liquids have a fixed volume but take the shape of their container. Gases have neither fixed shape nor fixed volume.'),(6191,'3fb19461',2090,'What is the function of the digestive system?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The digestive system breaks down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream and used by the body.'),(6192,'3fb19461',2091,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to create glucose (food) and oxygen.'),(6193,'3fb19461',2092,'State Ohm\'s Law and explain its significance.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ohm\'s Law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across it, provided the temperature remains constant.  It is significant because it allows us to predict and control the flow of electricity in circuits.'),(6194,'3fb19461',2093,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.  Include a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The atria receive blood, and the ventricles pump blood out.  (Diagram should be included showing atria, ventricles, valves, etc.)'),(6195,'3fb19461',2094,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants. Give examples of each type.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Plants can reproduce sexually (involving the fusion of gametes) and asexually (without the fusion of gametes). Sexual reproduction involves flowers and seeds, while asexual reproduction can occur through various methods such as vegetative propagation (e.g., runners, bulbs, tubers), budding, and fragmentation.'),(6196,'3fb19461',2095,'Explain the process of respiration in humans, including the equations involved.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Respiration is the process by which cells break down glucose to release energy in the form of ATP. This occurs through several steps: glycolysis, the Krebs cycle, and the electron transport chain. The overall equation is C6H12O6 + 6O2 → 6CO2 + 6H2O + Energy (ATP).'),(6197,'3fb19461',2096,'Explain the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Different types of pollution include air pollution (caused by emissions from vehicles and industries), water pollution (caused by sewage and industrial waste), and land pollution (caused by improper waste disposal). These have detrimental effects on human health, ecosystems, and climate change.'),(6198,'3fb19461',2097,'Explain the concept of evolution and the evidence that supports it.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Evolution is the gradual change in the heritable characteristics of biological populations over successive generations.  Evidence includes fossil records, comparative anatomy, molecular biology (DNA similarities), and biogeography.'),(6199,'3fb19461',2098,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples of each type.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into different types such as combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions. Each type involves a specific change in the arrangement of atoms and molecules. Examples of each reaction type should be provided.'),(6200,'3fb19461',2099,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Excretion\n4.  Transpiration\n\nColumn B\nA. Removal of waste products\nB. Release of water vapor from leaves\nC. Conversion of light energy into chemical energy\nD. Release of energy from food','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6201,'3fb19461',2100,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. The leaves are yellowing, and the plants are stunted.  He suspects a nutrient deficiency.  He tests the soil and finds it lacks nitrogen. \n\n(a) Explain why nitrogen is essential for plant growth.\n(b) Suggest a method to improve the nitrogen content of the soil. \n(c) What are the potential environmental consequences of overuse of nitrogen fertilizers?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is a crucial component of chlorophyll, which is essential for photosynthesis. It is also a component of amino acids and proteins needed for plant growth. (b) Nitrogen-fixing bacteria, crop rotation, and the use of organic fertilizers or nitrogen fertilizers in appropriate amounts can improve soil nitrogen content. (c) Overuse of nitrogen fertilizers can lead to eutrophication of water bodies, harming aquatic life.  It can also contribute to greenhouse gas emissions and air pollution.'),(6202,'b92eb250',2101,'Which of the following is a good conductor of electricity?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Wood\", \"Rubber\", \"Copper\", \"Plastic\"]','C'),(6203,'b92eb250',2102,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6204,'b92eb250',2103,'Which process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Digestion\", \"Combustion\"]','B'),(6205,'b92eb250',2104,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\"]','C'),(6206,'b92eb250',2105,'Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Melting ice\", \"Boiling water\", \"Burning wood\", \"Cutting paper\"]','C'),(6207,'b92eb250',2106,'The process of converting a solid directly into a gas is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Sublimation'),(6208,'b92eb250',2107,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Cohesion'),(6209,'b92eb250',2108,'The unit of electric current is the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Ampere'),(6210,'b92eb250',2109,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6211,'b92eb250',2110,'The process by which plants make their own food is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6212,'b92eb250',2111,'The basic unit of heredity is the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(6213,'b92eb250',2112,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6214,'b92eb250',2113,'What are the three states of matter? Describe their properties.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a definite shape and volume, liquids have a definite volume but take the shape of their container, and gases have neither a definite shape nor volume.'),(6215,'b92eb250',2114,'Define Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6216,'b92eb250',2115,'What is the function of the digestive system?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The digestive system breaks down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream and used by the body for energy and growth.'),(6217,'b92eb250',2116,'Explain the process of respiration.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process by which living organisms release energy from food molecules.  It involves breaking down glucose in the presence of oxygen to produce ATP (energy), carbon dioxide, and water.'),(6218,'b92eb250',2117,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The atria receive blood, while the ventricles pump blood out.  The heart has valves that prevent backflow of blood.'),(6219,'b92eb250',2118,'Explain the process of photosynthesis in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  It involves using carbon dioxide and water, in the presence of sunlight and chlorophyll, to produce glucose and oxygen.'),(6220,'b92eb250',2119,'State and explain Ohm\'s law. Give its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Applications include calculating resistance, current, or voltage in circuits.'),(6221,'b92eb250',2120,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into several types: combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6222,'b92eb250',2121,'Describe the structure and function of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The human nervous system consists of the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system (nerves). The brain is the control center, the spinal cord relays messages, and nerves transmit signals throughout the body.'),(6223,'b92eb250',2122,'Explain the concept of evolution and natural selection.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Evolution is the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time. Natural selection is the process by which organisms better adapted to their environment tend to survive and produce more offspring.'),(6224,'b92eb250',2123,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Oxygen\n2.  Carbon Dioxide\n3.  Nitrogen\n4.  Water\n\nColumn B\nA.  78% of the atmosphere\nB.  Used in respiration\n C.  Product of respiration\nD.  Used in photosynthesis','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-C, 3-A, 4-D'),(6225,'b92eb250',2124,'A student conducts an experiment to study the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction.  He observes that the reaction proceeds faster at higher temperatures.  Explain this observation in terms of kinetic energy of molecules and collision theory.','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','At higher temperatures, molecules possess greater kinetic energy, leading to more frequent and forceful collisions.  This increases the chance of successful collisions with sufficient activation energy to initiate the reaction, thus increasing the rate of reaction.'),(6226,'45c5791c',2125,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6227,'45c5791c',2126,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6228,'45c5791c',2127,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6229,'45c5791c',2128,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6230,'45c5791c',2129,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6231,'45c5791c',2130,'The process by which plants make their own food is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6232,'45c5791c',2131,'The force of attraction between two objects due to their masses is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravity'),(6233,'45c5791c',2132,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(6234,'45c5791c',2133,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6235,'45c5791c',2134,'The process of converting a gas into a liquid is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Condensation'),(6236,'45c5791c',2135,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(6237,'45c5791c',2136,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change is a change in the form or appearance of a substance, without changing its chemical composition.  A chemical change involves the formation of new substances with different chemical properties.'),(6238,'45c5791c',2137,'What is the role of chlorophyll in photosynthesis?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light energy from the sun, which is then used to drive the process of photosynthesis.'),(6239,'45c5791c',2138,'State two uses of acids and two uses of bases.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Acids:  In batteries, food preservation. Bases: In soaps, detergents.'),(6240,'45c5791c',2139,'Explain the concept of Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6241,'45c5791c',2140,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.'),(6242,'45c5791c',2141,'Describe the structure and functions of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood from the body and the lungs, while the ventricles pump blood to the body and the lungs. The heart has valves that prevent the backflow of blood.'),(6243,'45c5791c',2142,'Explain the process of respiration in humans, including the chemical equation involved.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Respiration is the process of releasing energy from food. It involves the intake of oxygen and the release of carbon dioxide. The chemical equation for aerobic respiration is: C6H12O6 + 6O2 → 6CO2 + 6H2O + Energy.'),(6244,'45c5791c',2143,'Explain the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Pollution can be air, water, soil, noise or light pollution.  The effects can include respiratory problems, waterborne diseases, damage to ecosystems, hearing loss, and disruption of natural cycles.'),(6245,'45c5791c',2144,'Describe the process of electrolysis of water.  Include the chemical equation and observations.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Electrolysis of water involves passing an electric current through water, causing it to decompose into hydrogen and oxygen gas.  The chemical equation is 2H2O → 2H2 + O2.  Observations include the production of hydrogen gas at the cathode and oxygen gas at the anode.'),(6246,'45c5791c',2145,'Explain the different types of asexual reproduction in organisms, providing examples for each type.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Asexual reproduction involves a single parent. Examples include binary fission (Amoeba), budding (Hydra), fragmentation (Spirogyra), vegetative propagation (potato).'),(6247,'45c5791c',2146,'Explain the structure and function of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The nervous system consists of the brain, spinal cord, and nerves. It receives, processes, and transmits information throughout the body. The brain is the control center, the spinal cord relays messages, and nerves carry signals.'),(6248,'45c5791c',2147,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  HCl\n2. NaOH\n3.  NaCl\n4. H2SO4\n\nColumn B\nA.  Common salt\nB.  Sulphuric acid\nC.  Hydrochloric acid\nD.  Sodium hydroxide','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6249,'45c5791c',2148,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well despite regular watering and fertilization. He notices that the leaves are yellowing and the plants are stunted.  He suspects a nutrient deficiency. \n\n(a) What nutrient deficiency might be the cause of these symptoms?\n(b) What is the role of this nutrient in plant growth?\n(c) Suggest a solution to address this deficiency.','Case Study','Medium',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen deficiency\n(b) Nitrogen is essential for chlorophyll synthesis, protein synthesis, and overall plant growth.\n(c) Apply nitrogen-rich fertilizers or use nitrogen-fixing bacteria.'),(6250,'ae636582',2149,'Which of the following is a good conductor of electricity?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Wood\", \"Rubber\", \"Copper\", \"Plastic\"]','C'),(6251,'ae636582',2150,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6252,'ae636582',2151,'Which process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Digestion\", \"Excretion\"]','B'),(6253,'ae636582',2152,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\"]','C'),(6254,'ae636582',2153,'Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Melting ice\", \"Boiling water\", \"Burning wood\", \"Cutting paper\"]','C'),(6255,'ae636582',2154,'The process of converting sugar into alcohol is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','fermentation'),(6256,'ae636582',2155,'The basic unit of heredity is called a ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6257,'ae636582',2156,'The force of attraction between two objects due to their masses is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gravity'),(6258,'ae636582',2157,'The process of adding a base to an acid until it is neutralized is called ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','neutralization'),(6259,'ae636582',2158,'The outermost layer of the Earth is called the ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','crust'),(6260,'ae636582',2159,'The SI unit of electric current is ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','ampere'),(6261,'ae636582',2160,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change is a change in the form or state of matter without changing its chemical composition. A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of matter, forming new substances.'),(6262,'ae636582',2161,'What are the three states of matter? Describe their properties.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a definite shape and volume. Liquids have a definite volume but take the shape of their container. Gases have neither a definite shape nor volume.'),(6263,'ae636582',2162,'Define Newton\'s first law of motion.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Newton\'s first law of motion, also known as the law of inertia, states that an object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.'),(6264,'ae636582',2163,'What is the role of chlorophyll in photosynthesis?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light energy, which is then used to drive the process of photosynthesis.'),(6265,'ae636582',2164,'Explain the difference between renewable and non-renewable resources.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Renewable resources are naturally replenished over a relatively short period, such as solar energy, wind energy, and biomass. Non-renewable resources are finite and cannot be replenished at a rate that matches their consumption, such as fossil fuels and minerals.'),(6266,'ae636582',2165,'Explain the process of digestion in the human body, including the organs involved and the enzymes secreted.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Digestion begins in the mouth with mechanical and chemical breakdown. The stomach continues the process with churning and acid secretion. The small intestine absorbs nutrients with the help of enzymes and bile. The large intestine absorbs water, and undigested materials are eliminated.'),(6267,'ae636582',2166,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The right side pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs, and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.'),(6268,'ae636582',2167,'Explain the process of respiration, both aerobic and anaerobic.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Aerobic respiration requires oxygen and produces a large amount of energy. Anaerobic respiration does not require oxygen and produces less energy.'),(6269,'ae636582',2168,'Explain Ohm\'s law and its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the voltage across it and inversely proportional to its resistance. It\'s used to calculate voltage, current, or resistance in circuits.'),(6270,'ae636582',2169,'Explain the structure and function of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The nervous system consists of the brain, spinal cord, and nerves. It controls and coordinates bodily functions through electrical and chemical signals.'),(6271,'ae636582',2170,'Discuss the importance of conservation of natural resources.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Conservation is crucial for maintaining ecological balance, supporting biodiversity, and ensuring the availability of resources for future generations.'),(6272,'ae636582',2171,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1. Carbon dioxide\n2. Oxygen\n3. Nitrogen\n4. Water\n\nColumn B\nA. Essential for respiration\nB. Main component of air\nC. Greenhouse gas\nD. Universal solvent','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B, 4-D'),(6273,'ae636582',2172,'A student is conducting an experiment to study the effect of different fertilizers on the growth of plants. He uses three different fertilizers (A, B, C) and a control group with no fertilizer. After a month, he observes that plants with fertilizer A are taller and healthier than those with fertilizers B and C. Plants in the control group show the least growth.  \n\n(a) What is the independent variable in this experiment?\n(b) What is the dependent variable in this experiment?\n(c) What is the control group in this experiment?\n(d) What conclusion can be drawn from this experiment?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Type of fertilizer\n(b) Plant growth (height and health)\n(c) Plants with no fertilizer\n(d) Fertilizer A is the most effective in promoting plant growth.'),(6274,'27b7950e',2173,'Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6275,'27b7950e',2174,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6276,'27b7950e',2175,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6277,'27b7950e',2176,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6278,'27b7950e',2177,'Which type of mirror is used in a car\'s side mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Plane mirror\", \"Concave mirror\", \"Convex mirror\", \"None of the above\"]','C'),(6279,'27b7950e',2178,'The process by which plants make their own food is called __________.  The green pigment in plants is called __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis, Chlorophyll'),(6280,'27b7950e',2179,'The SI unit of force is __________, while the SI unit of energy is __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton, Joule'),(6281,'27b7950e',2180,'The process of converting solid directly into gas is called __________, while the reverse process is called __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Sublimation, Deposition'),(6282,'27b7950e',2181,'Acids turn blue litmus paper __________, while bases turn red litmus paper __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Red, Blue'),(6283,'27b7950e',2182,'The basic unit of heredity is called a __________, and they are located on __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene, Chromosomes'),(6284,'27b7950e',2183,'The process of cell division that results in two identical daughter cells is called __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Mitosis'),(6285,'27b7950e',2184,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Physical changes alter the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). Chemical changes result in the formation of new substances with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6286,'27b7950e',2185,'What is the role of enzymes in digestion?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Enzymes are biological catalysts that speed up chemical reactions in digestion, breaking down complex molecules into simpler ones.'),(6287,'27b7950e',2186,'Describe the structure of an atom.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Atoms consist of a nucleus containing protons and neutrons, surrounded by orbiting electrons.'),(6288,'27b7950e',2187,'State Ohm\'s Law and write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across it, provided the temperature remains constant.  V = IR'),(6289,'27b7950e',2188,'What is the difference between renewable and non-renewable resources?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Renewable resources can be replenished naturally (e.g., solar energy), while non-renewable resources are finite and deplete with use (e.g., fossil fuels).'),(6290,'27b7950e',2189,'Explain the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the reactants, products, and the role of chlorophyll.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  Reactants are carbon dioxide and water.  Products are glucose and oxygen. Chlorophyll is a pigment that absorbs light energy to drive the reaction.'),(6291,'27b7950e',2190,'Describe the different types of reproduction in plants with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants can reproduce sexually (involving fusion of gametes) and asexually (without fusion of gametes). Sexual reproduction involves flowers and seeds (e.g., flowering plants), while asexual reproduction methods include vegetative propagation (e.g., tubers, bulbs) and spore formation (e.g., ferns).'),(6292,'27b7950e',2191,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Various types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, neutralization, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6293,'27b7950e',2192,'Explain the working of the human respiratory system with a neat diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','The respiratory system involves the intake of oxygen and the expulsion of carbon dioxide.  It includes the nasal cavity, trachea, bronchi, lungs, and alveoli.  A labelled diagram should be included to show the pathway of air.'),(6294,'27b7950e',2193,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers (two atria and two ventricles), valves to regulate blood flow, and blood vessels (arteries, veins, capillaries).'),(6295,'27b7950e',2194,'Explain the concept of evolution with examples and evidences.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Evolution refers to the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time.  Examples include Darwin\'s finches and peppered moths. Evidences include fossil records, comparative anatomy, embryology, and molecular biology.'),(6296,'27b7950e',2195,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Acid rain\n2.  Ozone layer\n3.  Global warming\n4.  Deforestation\n\nColumn B\nA.  Increased CO2 levels\nB.  Loss of forest cover\nC.  Damage to plants and buildings\nD.  Protection from UV radiation','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6297,'27b7950e',2196,'A farmer noticed that his crops were not growing well. He observed that the soil was dry and lacked nutrients. He decided to use fertilizers and irrigation to improve the condition of his soil.  \n(a) What are the advantages of using fertilizers? \n(b) What are the disadvantages of excessive use of fertilizers? \n(c) What are the advantages of irrigation? \n(d) What are the disadvantages of excessive irrigation?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Fertilizers provide essential nutrients for plant growth. (b) Excessive use leads to soil pollution and water contamination. (c) Irrigation ensures adequate water supply for crop growth. (d) Excessive irrigation can lead to waterlogging and salinization.'),(6298,'9393f92c',2197,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6299,'9393f92c',2198,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6300,'9393f92c',2199,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Combination reaction\", \"Decomposition reaction\", \"Displacement reaction\", \"Reflection\"]','D'),(6301,'9393f92c',2200,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Zero\", \"Infinity\", \"10 cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(6302,'9393f92c',2201,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6303,'9393f92c',2202,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6304,'9393f92c',2203,'The unit of power is the _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(6305,'9393f92c',2204,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6306,'9393f92c',2205,'The process of separating components of a mixture based on their boiling points is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Distillation'),(6307,'9393f92c',2206,'The resistance of a conductor is inversely proportional to its _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cross-sectional area'),(6308,'9393f92c',2207,'The image formed by a concave mirror can be _______ or _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','real, virtual'),(6309,'9393f92c',2208,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s physical properties change but its chemical composition remains the same. A chemical change is a change in which the substance\'s chemical composition changes, forming a new substance.'),(6310,'9393f92c',2209,'State Ohm\'s law. Write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR'),(6311,'9393f92c',2210,'What is the role of chlorophyll in photosynthesis?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Chlorophyll is a green pigment found in plants that absorbs sunlight, which is essential for photosynthesis. It traps light energy and converts it into chemical energy.'),(6312,'9393f92c',2211,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface. Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.'),(6313,'9393f92c',2212,'Explain the process of neutralization reaction.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Neutralization is a chemical reaction between an acid and a base, producing salt and water.  It involves the combination of H+ ions from the acid and OH- ions from the base to form water.'),(6314,'9393f92c',2213,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Combination reaction (e.g., formation of water from hydrogen and oxygen), decomposition reaction (e.g., decomposition of calcium carbonate), displacement reaction (e.g., reaction between iron and copper sulphate), double displacement reaction (e.g., reaction between sodium chloride and silver nitrate), redox reaction (e.g., reaction between magnesium and oxygen).'),(6315,'9393f92c',2214,'Explain the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, bronchioles, and alveoli. It facilitates the intake of oxygen and the removal of carbon dioxide from the body through the process of breathing.'),(6316,'9393f92c',2215,'Explain the process of electrolysis of water.  What are the products formed?','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Electrolysis of water involves passing an electric current through water, breaking it down into its constituent elements: hydrogen and oxygen.  Hydrogen gas is produced at the cathode (negative electrode), and oxygen gas is produced at the anode (positive electrode).'),(6317,'9393f92c',2216,'Describe the different types of mirrors and their uses.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plane mirrors (used in dressing tables), concave mirrors (used in telescopes and headlights), convex mirrors (used as rear-view mirrors in vehicles).'),(6318,'9393f92c',2217,'Explain the working principle of a simple electric motor.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','A simple electric motor works based on the principle of electromagnetic induction.  A current-carrying coil placed in a magnetic field experiences a torque, causing it to rotate.'),(6319,'9393f92c',2218,'Describe the different types of lenses and their uses.  Draw ray diagrams for image formation by a convex lens.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Convex lenses (used in magnifying glasses and cameras), concave lenses (used in correcting myopia). Ray diagrams should show image formation for different object positions (beyond 2F, at 2F, between F and 2F, at F, and between F and the lens).'),(6320,'9393f92c',2219,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Sulphuric acid\n2.  Hydrochloric acid\n3.  Sodium hydroxide\n4.  Calcium oxide\n\nColumn B\nA.  Base\nB.  Acid\nC.  Alkali\nD.  Basic oxide','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-B, 3-C, 4-D'),(6321,'9393f92c',2220,'A student is conducting an experiment to study the effect of different liquids on the growth of plants.  Three plants of the same species and size are selected. Plant A is watered with plain water, Plant B with a solution of diluted fertilizer, and Plant C with a solution of salt water.  After a week, the height of each plant is measured.\n\n(a) What is the independent variable in this experiment?\n(b) What is the dependent variable in this experiment?\n(c) What are the controlled variables in this experiment?\n(d) What can you conclude about the effect of different liquids on plant growth based on this experiment?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) The type of liquid used to water the plants. \n(b) The height of the plants after a week. \n(c) The species and size of the plants, the amount of light and sunlight, the type of soil, the amount of water given.\n(d) The conclusion will depend on the measured heights, but generally it is expected that Plant B (with diluted fertilizer) will show the most growth, Plant A (with plain water) will show moderate growth, and Plant C (with salt water) might show stunted growth or die.'),(6322,'6ba91f64',2221,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6323,'6ba91f64',2222,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6324,'6ba91f64',2223,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6325,'6ba91f64',2224,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6326,'6ba91f64',2225,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6327,'6ba91f64',2226,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6328,'6ba91f64',2227,'The force of attraction between two bodies due to their masses is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitational force'),(6329,'6ba91f64',2228,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(6330,'6ba91f64',2229,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6331,'6ba91f64',2230,'The process of separating different components of a mixture based on their boiling points is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Distillation'),(6332,'6ba91f64',2231,'The outermost shell of an atom is called the _________ shell.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','valence'),(6333,'6ba91f64',2232,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but does not change its chemical composition, while a chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties.'),(6334,'6ba91f64',2233,'What is the role of enzymes in digestion?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Enzymes act as biological catalysts, speeding up the breakdown of complex food molecules into simpler, absorbable substances.'),(6335,'6ba91f64',2234,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature remains constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR'),(6336,'6ba91f64',2235,'Describe the structure of an atom.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','An atom consists of a central nucleus containing protons and neutrons, surrounded by orbiting electrons.'),(6337,'6ba91f64',2236,'What are the advantages and disadvantages of using fossil fuels?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Advantages: readily available, high energy density. Disadvantages: non-renewable, pollute the environment, contribute to climate change.'),(6338,'6ba91f64',2237,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a balanced chemical equation. Mention its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2. It\'s important because it produces food for plants and releases oxygen, essential for most life on Earth.'),(6339,'6ba91f64',2238,'Describe the different types of reproduction in plants. Give examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants reproduce through sexual reproduction (involving the fusion of gametes, e.g., flowering plants) and asexual reproduction (without gamete fusion, e.g., vegetative propagation in potato).'),(6340,'6ba91f64',2239,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Examples include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Specific examples of each reaction type should be provided.'),(6341,'6ba91f64',2240,'Explain the working principle of an electric motor. Draw a labelled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','An electric motor works on the principle of electromagnetic induction.  A detailed explanation of the interaction between magnetic fields and current-carrying conductors, resulting in rotational motion, is required. A labelled diagram should be included.'),(6342,'6ba91f64',2241,'Describe the different types of lenses and their uses. Explain how a human eye works.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Convex and concave lenses, and their uses in correcting vision problems and optical instruments.  The human eye\'s structure and its function in forming images on the retina should be described.'),(6343,'6ba91f64',2242,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection. Give examples.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Natural selection explains how species adapt and evolve over time through variations, inheritance, and differential survival and reproduction.  Examples like Darwin\'s finches or antibiotic resistance in bacteria should be provided.'),(6344,'6ba91f64',2243,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\'s Law of Gravitation\n2.  Archimedes\' Principle\n3.  Ohm\'s Law\n4.  Boyle\'s Law\n\nColumn B\nA.  Relates pressure and volume of a gas\nB.  Deals with the force of attraction between objects\nC.  Relates current, voltage, and resistance\nD.  Deals with the buoyant force on a body immersed in a fluid','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-D, 3-C, 4-A'),(6345,'6ba91f64',2244,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well despite sufficient watering.  Upon investigation, it is found that the soil lacks essential nutrients. \n(a)  What is the term for the deficiency of essential nutrients in the soil?\n(b)  How can this deficiency be addressed?\n(c)  What are some important nutrients required for healthy plant growth?\n(d)  What are the consequences of nutrient deficiency in plants?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Soil nutrient deficiency\n(b) By using fertilizers and other soil amendments to replenish the lacking nutrients.\n(c) Nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium, etc.\n(d) Stunted growth, reduced yield, susceptibility to diseases.'),(6346,'17e713cc',2245,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6347,'17e713cc',2246,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6348,'17e713cc',2247,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6349,'17e713cc',2248,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6350,'17e713cc',2249,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Zero\", \"Infinity\", \"10 cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(6351,'17e713cc',2250,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6352,'17e713cc',2251,'The force of attraction between any two objects is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravity'),(6353,'17e713cc',2252,'The unit of power is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(6354,'17e713cc',2253,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6355,'17e713cc',2254,'The process of rusting is an example of _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','oxidation'),(6356,'17e713cc',2255,'The basic unit of heredity is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(6357,'17e713cc',2256,'The splitting of nucleus into two or more nuclei is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Nuclear fission'),(6358,'17e713cc',2257,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in the form or appearance of a substance, without changing its chemical composition. A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of a substance, resulting in the formation of new substances.'),(6359,'17e713cc',2258,'What is the role of enzymes in digestion?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Enzymes are biological catalysts that speed up the rate of chemical reactions in digestion. They break down complex food molecules into simpler molecules that can be absorbed by the body.'),(6360,'17e713cc',2259,'State Ohm\'s law. Write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR'),(6361,'17e713cc',2260,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\'.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface. Refraction is the bending of light when it passes from one medium to another.'),(6362,'17e713cc',2261,'What are the advantages of using solar energy?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Solar energy is a renewable, clean, and sustainable source of energy. It reduces dependence on fossil fuels, lowers carbon emissions, and can be used in remote areas.'),(6363,'17e713cc',2262,'Explain the process of fertilization in flowering plants.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Fertilization in flowering plants involves the fusion of male gametes (pollen) with female gametes (ovules) to form a zygote, which develops into a seed.'),(6364,'17e713cc',2263,'What are the different types of blood groups?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The main blood groups are A, B, AB, and O.'),(6365,'17e713cc',2264,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a labeled diagram.  Mention the factors affecting photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  [Diagram showing chloroplast, sunlight, CO2, H2O, glucose, O2]. Factors affecting photosynthesis include light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, temperature, and water availability.'),(6366,'17e713cc',2265,'Describe the structure and functions of the human respiratory system with a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','[Diagram showing lungs, bronchi, trachea, diaphragm etc.].  The respiratory system facilitates the intake of oxygen and the removal of carbon dioxide from the body.  Air enters through the nose and mouth, passes through the trachea, bronchi, and bronchioles, reaching the alveoli where gas exchange takes place.'),(6367,'17e713cc',2266,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Plants reproduce through asexual and sexual reproduction. Asexual reproduction involves the production of offspring from a single parent, without the fusion of gametes (e.g., vegetative propagation). Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of male and female gametes to form a zygote, resulting in offspring with a combination of genetic material from both parents.'),(6368,'17e713cc',2267,'Explain the working of a simple electric motor with a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','[Diagram of a simple electric motor showing magnets, coil, commutator, brushes].  An electric motor converts electrical energy into mechanical energy. When current flows through a coil placed in a magnetic field, it experiences a force causing it to rotate. The commutator ensures continuous rotation.'),(6369,'17e713cc',2268,'Discuss the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into various types, including combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox reactions, etc.  Examples of each type should be given.'),(6370,'17e713cc',2269,'Explain the concept of evolution and natural selection. Give examples.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Evolution is the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time. Natural selection is the process by which organisms better adapted to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on their advantageous traits to their offspring. Examples of natural selection should be provided.'),(6371,'17e713cc',2270,'Explain the different types of lenses and their uses. Draw ray diagrams to show image formation by convex and concave lenses.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Lenses are classified as convex (converging) and concave (diverging) lenses.  Convex lenses converge light rays, while concave lenses diverge light rays.  Ray diagrams should be drawn for image formation in both lenses for different object positions.'),(6372,'17e713cc',2271,'Explain the structure and function of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The human nervous system consists of the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system (nerves). The nervous system controls and coordinates bodily functions through the transmission of nerve impulses.'),(6373,'17e713cc',2272,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\'s First Law\n2.  Newton\'s Second Law\n3.  Newton\'s Third Law\n4.  Inertia\n\nColumn B\nA.  F = ma\nB.  For every action, there\'s an equal and opposite reaction\nC.  An object at rest stays at rest unless acted upon by an external force\nD.  Tendency of an object to resist changes in motion','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B, 4-D'),(6374,'17e713cc',2273,'A student is conducting an experiment to study the effect of different fertilizers on the growth of plants. He uses three different fertilizers (A, B, C) and a control group (no fertilizer). After 30 days, he measures the height of the plants. The results are as follows:\n\nFertilizer A: Average height = 15 cm\nFertilizer B: Average height = 20 cm\nFertilizer C: Average height = 10 cm\nControl Group: Average height = 5 cm\n\n(a) Which fertilizer is most effective?\n(b) What is the role of the control group in this experiment?\n(c) What are some other factors that could affect plant growth besides fertilizers?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Fertilizer B is most effective. (b) The control group provides a baseline for comparison, allowing the student to determine the effect of the fertilizers. (c) Other factors that could affect plant growth include sunlight, water, temperature, soil quality, and pests.'),(6375,'db650d29',2274,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6376,'db650d29',2275,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6377,'db650d29',2276,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6378,'db650d29',2277,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(6379,'db650d29',2278,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6380,'db650d29',2279,'The process of converting solar energy into electrical energy is called _____________ .  The SI unit of force is the _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',2,'null','photovoltaic effect, newton'),(6381,'db650d29',2280,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _____________ and bases turn red litmus paper _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',2,'null','red, blue'),(6382,'db650d29',2281,'The process by which plants make their own food is called _____________ .  The smallest unit of an element is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',2,'null','photosynthesis, atom'),(6383,'db650d29',2282,'The force of attraction between two objects due to their masses is called _____________ . The resistance to the flow of current is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',2,'null','gravitation, resistance'),(6384,'db650d29',2283,'The outermost shell of an atom is called the _____________ shell.  The process of separating components of a mixture is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',2,'null','valence, separation'),(6385,'db650d29',2284,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition.  A chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(6386,'db650d29',2285,'What are the different states of matter? Briefly describe each state.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a fixed shape and volume. Liquids have a fixed volume but take the shape of their container. Gases have neither a fixed shape nor volume.'),(6387,'db650d29',2286,'Define Newton\'s first law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Newton\'s first law of motion, also known as the law of inertia, states that an object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.'),(6388,'db650d29',2287,'What is the difference between speed and velocity?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Speed is the rate of change of distance, while velocity is the rate of change of displacement.  Velocity includes both speed and direction.'),(6389,'db650d29',2288,'Explain the concept of biodiversity.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Biodiversity refers to the variety of life on Earth at all its levels, from genes to ecosystems, and can encompass the evolutionary, ecological, and cultural processes that sustain it.'),(6390,'db650d29',2289,'Describe the structure and functions of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','The respiratory system consists of the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs.  Air enters through the nose, passes through the pharynx and larynx, and into the trachea.  The trachea branches into two bronchi, which lead to the lungs.  In the lungs, gas exchange occurs in the alveoli, where oxygen is absorbed into the blood and carbon dioxide is released.'),(6391,'db650d29',2290,'Explain the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  It involves the absorption of carbon dioxide and water, using light energy to produce glucose and oxygen.  Photosynthesis is essential for all life on Earth because it provides the basis of most food chains and produces the oxygen we breathe.'),(6392,'db650d29',2291,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Plants reproduce through both asexual and sexual reproduction. Asexual reproduction involves the production of offspring from a single parent, without the fusion of gametes.  Examples include vegetative propagation, budding, and fragmentation.  Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of male and female gametes, leading to the formation of seeds.  This process may involve self-pollination or cross-pollination.'),(6393,'db650d29',2292,'Describe the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Pollution can be classified into various types, including air, water, soil, noise, and light pollution. Air pollution leads to respiratory problems and acid rain. Water pollution contaminates water sources, harming aquatic life and human health. Soil pollution reduces soil fertility and can contaminate food crops. Noise pollution affects hearing and causes stress. Light pollution disrupts ecosystems and astronomy.'),(6394,'db650d29',2293,'Explain Ohm\'s law and its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Mathematically, V = IR, where V is the potential difference, I is the current, and R is the resistance.  Applications include designing electrical circuits, calculating resistance, and understanding current flow.'),(6395,'db650d29',2294,'Discuss the importance of conservation of natural resources.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Conservation of natural resources is crucial for maintaining ecological balance, supporting biodiversity, and ensuring sustainable development.  It involves responsible use and management of resources like water, forests, minerals, and energy to prevent depletion and environmental degradation.  Sustainable practices, including recycling, reducing consumption, and renewable energy sources, are vital for long-term sustainability.'),(6396,'db650d29',2295,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Transpiration\n4.  Germination\n\nColumn B\nA.  Loss of water vapor from plants\nB.  Process of seed development into seedling\nC.  Process of making food in plants\nD.  Process of releasing energy from food','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6397,'db650d29',2296,'A farmer noticed that his crop yield was significantly lower than usual this year.  He suspected a problem with the soil.  Upon testing, it was found that the soil lacked essential nutrients. \n\n(a) What is the importance of soil nutrients for plant growth?\n(b) Suggest some methods the farmer could use to improve the soil\'s nutrient content.\n(c) What are the long-term consequences of neglecting soil health?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Soil nutrients are essential for plant growth, providing the necessary building blocks for various plant processes.  (b) Methods include using organic fertilizers, crop rotation, and cover cropping. (c) Long-term consequences include decreased crop yields, soil erosion, and land degradation.'),(6398,'db650d29',2003,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6399,'c285cc48',2297,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transformation\"]','D'),(6400,'c285cc48',2298,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6401,'c285cc48',2299,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\", \"Nuclear Energy\"]','C'),(6402,'c285cc48',2300,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ohm\", \"Ampere\", \"Watt\"]','C'),(6403,'c285cc48',2301,'Which process is responsible for the upward movement of water and minerals in plants?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Transpiration\", \"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Fermentation\"]','A'),(6404,'c285cc48',2302,'The basic unit of heredity is the ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6405,'c285cc48',2303,'The process of converting solar energy into chemical energy is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','photosynthesis'),(6406,'c285cc48',2304,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6407,'c285cc48',2305,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cohesion'),(6408,'c285cc48',2306,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration'),(6409,'c285cc48',2307,'The SI unit of force is the ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','newton'),(6410,'c285cc48',2308,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance without changing its chemical composition, while a chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(6411,'c285cc48',2309,'What are the main components of blood?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Red blood cells, white blood cells, platelets, and plasma.'),(6412,'c285cc48',2310,'State the law of conservation of mass.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The law of conservation of mass states that mass is neither created nor destroyed in a chemical reaction; it only changes form.'),(6413,'c285cc48',2311,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to a change in speed.'),(6414,'c285cc48',2312,'What is the role of ozone layer in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The ozone layer absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6415,'c285cc48',2313,'Describe the process of photosynthesis in detail, including the reactants, products, and the role of chlorophyll.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  Chlorophyll is the green pigment that absorbs light energy. The process takes place in chloroplasts and involves two main stages: the light-dependent reactions and the light-independent reactions (Calvin cycle). The reactants are carbon dioxide and water, and the products are glucose (a sugar) and oxygen. Chlorophyll plays a crucial role in capturing light energy, which drives the entire process.'),(6416,'c285cc48',2314,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination (synthesis), decomposition, displacement (single and double), and redox (oxidation-reduction) reactions. Examples would include formation of water (combination), decomposition of calcium carbonate, reaction of zinc with hydrochloric acid (displacement), and rusting of iron (redox).'),(6417,'c285cc48',2315,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The right atrium receives deoxygenated blood from the body and pumps it to the right ventricle, which pumps it to the lungs. The left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lungs and pumps it to the left ventricle, which pumps it to the rest of the body. Valves ensure blood flows in one direction.'),(6418,'c285cc48',2316,'Describe the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Pollution can be categorized into air, water, and soil pollution. Air pollution is caused by emissions from vehicles and industries, leading to respiratory problems and acid rain. Water pollution results from industrial and agricultural waste, harming aquatic life and contaminating drinking water. Soil pollution comes from industrial waste and pesticides, affecting plant growth and human health. Each form has widespread environmental and health consequences.'),(6419,'c285cc48',2317,'Explain the concept of evolution and natural selection.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Evolution is the change in the heritable characteristics of biological populations over successive generations.  Natural selection is the mechanism by which this occurs.  Organisms with traits better suited to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing those advantageous traits to their offspring. Over time, this leads to the adaptation and diversification of species.'),(6420,'c285cc48',2318,'Explain Newton\'s three laws of motion with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Newton\'s first law (inertia): An object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.  Second law (F=ma): The acceleration of an object is directly proportional to the net force acting on it and inversely proportional to its mass. Third law (action-reaction): For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6421,'c285cc48',2319,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Albert Einstein\n3. Marie Curie\n4. Charles Darwin\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Principles of Inheritance\nC. Theory of Evolution\nD. Discovery of Radium','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-D, 4-C'),(6422,'c285cc48',2320,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. The leaves are yellowing, and the plants are stunted.  He suspects a nutrient deficiency.  He carries out a soil test and finds it deficient in nitrogen. \n(a) What is the role of nitrogen in plant growth? \n(b) What are the symptoms of nitrogen deficiency in plants? \n(c) Suggest a suitable remedy for this problem.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is crucial for chlorophyll synthesis and protein formation in plants, essential for growth. (b) Nitrogen deficiency shows up as chlorosis (yellowing) of leaves, stunted growth, and reduced yields. (c) The farmer should apply nitrogen-rich fertilizers like urea or ammonium nitrate to his soil.'),(6423,'72fadb67',2321,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6424,'72fadb67',2322,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6425,'72fadb67',2323,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Nuclear energy\", \"Hydro energy\"]','C'),(6426,'72fadb67',2324,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6427,'72fadb67',2325,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6428,'72fadb67',2326,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called __________.  Plants use __________ to perform this process.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis, chlorophyll'),(6429,'72fadb67',2327,'The basic unit of heredity is the __________.  These are located on __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene, chromosomes'),(6430,'72fadb67',2328,'Acids turn blue litmus paper __________, while bases turn red litmus paper __________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red, blue'),(6431,'72fadb67',2329,'The force of attraction between the earth and an object is called __________. Its unit is __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gravity, Newton'),(6432,'72fadb67',2330,'The process by which a solid directly changes into a gas is called __________. The reverse process is called __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','sublimation, deposition'),(6433,'72fadb67',2331,'The process of separating different components of a mixture based on their boiling points is called __________.  A common example of this is __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','distillation, separating components of crude oil'),(6434,'72fadb67',2332,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Physical changes alter the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). Chemical changes involve the formation of new substances with different chemical properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6435,'72fadb67',2333,'What are the three states of matter? Explain the characteristics of each.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have definite shape and volume; liquids have definite volume but take the shape of their container; gases have neither definite shape nor volume.'),(6436,'72fadb67',2334,'Describe the process of osmosis.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Osmosis is the movement of water molecules across a selectively permeable membrane from a region of high water concentration (low solute concentration) to a region of low water concentration (high solute concentration).'),(6437,'72fadb67',2335,'Explain the concept of Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6438,'72fadb67',2336,'What is an ecosystem? Give an example.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','An ecosystem is a community of living organisms (plants, animals, microorganisms) in conjunction with the nonliving components of their environment (air, water, soil) interacting as a system. Example: A forest ecosystem.'),(6439,'72fadb67',2337,'Explain the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the reactants, products, and the importance of photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  Reactants are carbon dioxide and water; products are glucose (a sugar) and oxygen.  It\'s crucial for providing food and oxygen for most life on Earth.'),(6440,'72fadb67',2338,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs. It\'s responsible for taking in oxygen and expelling carbon dioxide, essential for cellular respiration.'),(6441,'72fadb67',2339,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants reproduce through sexual reproduction (involving fusion of gametes) and asexual reproduction (without fusion of gametes). Asexual methods include vegetative propagation (e.g., runners, bulbs) while sexual reproduction involves pollination and fertilization.'),(6442,'72fadb67',2340,'Explain the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Types of pollution include air, water, and soil pollution. Air pollution can cause respiratory problems, acid rain, and climate change. Water pollution contaminates drinking water sources and harms aquatic life. Soil pollution degrades soil fertility and affects plant growth.'),(6443,'72fadb67',2341,'Explain Ohm\'s law and its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current through a conductor between two points is directly proportional to the voltage across the two points, provided the temperature remains constant.  Applications include designing electrical circuits and calculating resistance.'),(6444,'72fadb67',2342,'Describe the structure and functions of the human digestive system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The digestive system consists of the mouth, esophagus, stomach, small intestine, large intestine, rectum, and anus. It\'s responsible for breaking down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream to provide energy and nutrients.'),(6445,'72fadb67',2343,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Electric current\n2.  Resistance\n3.  Potential difference\n4.  Power\n\nColumn B\nA.  Volt\nB.  Watt\n C.  Ampere\nD.  Ohm','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6446,'72fadb67',2344,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well.  The leaves are yellowing, and the plants are stunted. He suspects a nutrient deficiency in the soil.  What are the possible reasons for this? What tests could be done to determine the cause? What measures can be taken to improve crop yield?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','Possible reasons include nitrogen deficiency (leading to yellowing leaves), phosphorus deficiency (affecting growth), or potassium deficiency (causing weak stems). Soil testing can determine nutrient levels. Measures to improve yield include using fertilizers, improving soil drainage, or crop rotation.'),(6447,'1c810dc9',2345,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6448,'1c810dc9',2346,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6449,'1c810dc9',2347,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Nuclear energy\", \"Hydro energy\"]','C'),(6450,'1c810dc9',2348,'What is the process by which plants make their food?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Excretion\"]','B'),(6451,'1c810dc9',2349,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6452,'1c810dc9',2350,'The basic unit of heredity is a _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6453,'1c810dc9',2351,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','photosynthesis'),(6454,'1c810dc9',2352,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6455,'1c810dc9',2353,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cohesion'),(6456,'1c810dc9',2354,'The unit of power is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','watt'),(6457,'1c810dc9',2355,'The process of splitting of a heavy nucleus into lighter nuclei is called _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','nuclear fission'),(6458,'1c810dc9',2356,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in which no new substance is formed, only the physical properties change. A chemical change is a change in which a new substance is formed with different properties.'),(6459,'1c810dc9',2357,'Define the term \'Biodiversity\'.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Biodiversity refers to the variety of life on Earth at all its levels, from genes to ecosystems, and the ecological and evolutionary processes that sustain it.'),(6460,'1c810dc9',2358,'What are the main components of blood?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The main components of blood are plasma, red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets.'),(6461,'1c810dc9',2359,'State Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current through a conductor between two points is directly proportional to the voltage across the two points, provided the temperature remains constant.'),(6462,'1c810dc9',2360,'Explain the concept of reflection of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it hits a surface.  The angle of incidence (incoming light) equals the angle of reflection (outgoing light).'),(6463,'1c810dc9',2361,'Describe the process of digestion in the human body. Include the major organs involved and their functions.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Digestion begins in the mouth with mechanical and chemical breakdown of food. The esophagus transports food to the stomach, where it\'s mixed with gastric juices. The small intestine is the major site of nutrient absorption, aided by enzymes from the pancreas and bile from the liver. The large intestine absorbs water and forms feces, which are eliminated from the body.'),(6464,'1c810dc9',2362,'Explain the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, trachea, bronchi, and lungs. Air enters through the nose and travels to the lungs via the trachea and bronchi. Gas exchange (oxygen and carbon dioxide) occurs in the alveoli within the lungs.'),(6465,'1c810dc9',2363,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Plants reproduce both sexually (involving gametes) and asexually (without gametes). Sexual reproduction involves pollination, fertilization, and seed formation. Asexual reproduction methods include vegetative propagation (e.g., budding, runners).'),(6466,'1c810dc9',2364,'Describe the structure and functions of a neuron.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Neurons are the fundamental units of the nervous system. They have a cell body (soma), dendrites (receiving signals), and an axon (transmitting signals).  Neurons transmit information via electrical and chemical signals.'),(6467,'1c810dc9',2365,'Explain the process of photosynthesis. Include the reactants, products, and the importance of this process for life on Earth.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy.  The reactants are carbon dioxide and water, and the products are glucose and oxygen. Photosynthesis is crucial for life because it produces food for most organisms and releases oxygen into the atmosphere.'),(6468,'1c810dc9',2366,'Discuss the various sources of pollution and their impact on the environment and human health.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Pollution sources include air pollution (vehicles, industries), water pollution (industrial discharge, sewage), and land pollution (waste disposal).  These pollutants have various health impacts, such as respiratory illnesses, waterborne diseases, and soil contamination.'),(6469,'1c810dc9',2367,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\n2.  Pascal\n3.  Joule\n4.  Watt\n\nColumn B\nA.  Unit of power\nB.  Unit of force\nC.  Unit of energy\nD.  Unit of pressure','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-D, 3-C, 4-A'),(6470,'1c810dc9',2368,'A farmer notices that his crops are not growing well.  He observes yellowing leaves and stunted growth.  The soil test reveals a deficiency of nitrogen. \n(a) What is the importance of nitrogen for plant growth?\n(b) Suggest a method to improve the nitrogen content in the soil.\n(c) Explain the consequences of nitrogen deficiency in plants.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is a crucial component of chlorophyll, proteins, and nucleic acids, essential for plant growth. (b) Using nitrogen-rich fertilizers or crop rotation with leguminous plants. (c) Nitrogen deficiency leads to stunted growth, chlorosis (yellowing of leaves), and reduced crop yield.'),(6471,'17a47692',2369,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transformation\"]','D'),(6472,'17a47692',2370,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6473,'17a47692',2371,'Which of these is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\"]','D'),(6474,'17a47692',2372,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6475,'17a47692',2373,'Which of the following is responsible for the clotting of blood?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Red blood cells\", \"White blood cells\", \"Platelets\", \"Plasma\"]','C'),(6476,'17a47692',2374,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6477,'17a47692',2375,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Cohesion'),(6478,'17a47692',2376,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(6479,'17a47692',2377,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6480,'17a47692',2378,'An acid reacts with a base to form _____________ and _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','salt, water'),(6481,'17a47692',2379,'The nucleus of an atom contains _____________ and _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','protons, neutrons'),(6482,'17a47692',2380,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but doesn\'t change its chemical composition.  A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties.'),(6483,'17a47692',2381,'What is the role of chlorophyll in photosynthesis?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Chlorophyll is a pigment that absorbs sunlight, providing the energy needed to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose.'),(6484,'17a47692',2382,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another. Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface.'),(6485,'17a47692',2383,'Describe the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves the intake of air into the lungs, the exchange of gases between the lungs and the blood, and the transport of oxygen to cells and carbon dioxide away from them.'),(6486,'17a47692',2384,'Explain the concept of \'evolution\'.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Evolution is the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time, driven by natural selection.'),(6487,'17a47692',2385,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each.'),(6488,'17a47692',2386,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  Its structure includes four chambers (two atria and two ventricles) and valves that regulate blood flow.  The function is to circulate oxygenated blood to the body and deoxygenated blood to the lungs.'),(6489,'17a47692',2387,'Explain the process of digestion in the human digestive system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The digestive system breaks down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream.  This process involves mechanical and chemical digestion, starting in the mouth and ending in the large intestine. The explanation should include the roles of various digestive organs and enzymes.'),(6490,'17a47692',2388,'Discuss the different types of pollution and their impact on the environment.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Different types of pollution include air, water, soil, and noise pollution.  The impact includes various environmental problems such as global warming, acid rain, depletion of the ozone layer, water contamination, and biodiversity loss.'),(6491,'17a47692',2389,'Explain the principles of Mendelian genetics and give examples.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Mendelian genetics explains the inheritance of traits through the passing of genes from parents to offspring.  The principles include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment.  Examples should be given illustrating these laws.'),(6492,'17a47692',2390,'Explain the working principle of an electric generator and its applications.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','An electric generator works on the principle of electromagnetic induction.  When a conductor moves in a magnetic field, an electric current is induced.  This principle is used to generate electricity in power plants and other applications.'),(6493,'17a47692',2391,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Isaac Newton\n3. Albert Einstein\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Laws of Motion\nC. Principles of Inheritance','Matching','Medium',3,'null','1-C, 2-B, 3-A'),(6494,'17a47692',2392,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. The leaves are yellowing, and the plants are stunted.  He suspects a nutrient deficiency.  \n\n(a) What is the likely nutrient deficiency?\n(b) Which nutrient is lacking and why is it essential for plant growth?\n(c) Suggest a solution to address this issue.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) The likely nutrient deficiency is nitrogen. (b) Nitrogen is crucial for chlorophyll synthesis (hence yellowing leaves) and protein formation, essential for plant growth.  (c) The farmer should use a nitrogen-rich fertilizer.'),(6495,'6058baa3',2393,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6496,'6058baa3',2394,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6497,'6058baa3',2395,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Nuclear energy\", \"Hydro energy\"]','C'),(6498,'6058baa3',2396,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6499,'6058baa3',2397,'Which type of lens converges light rays?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Concave lens\", \"Convex lens\", \"Plano-concave lens\", \"Plano-convex lens\"]','B'),(6500,'6058baa3',2398,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6501,'6058baa3',2399,'The force of attraction between two bodies is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitational force'),(6502,'6058baa3',2400,'The smallest unit of an element is called an _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Atom'),(6503,'6058baa3',2401,'The unit of power is the _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(6504,'6058baa3',2402,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6505,'6058baa3',2403,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6506,'6058baa3',2404,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but not its chemical composition.  A chemical change involves the formation of a new substance with different properties.'),(6507,'6058baa3',2405,'State two advantages of using solar energy.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Renewable and environmentally friendly; reduces dependence on fossil fuels.'),(6508,'6058baa3',2406,'What is the role of ozone layer in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','It absorbs harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6509,'6058baa3',2407,'Define Newton\'s First Law of Motion.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','An object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.'),(6510,'6058baa3',2408,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Involves the intake of oxygen and the release of carbon dioxide, producing energy for the body.'),(6511,'6058baa3',2409,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood and the ventricles pump blood out.  The heart valves ensure one-way blood flow.'),(6512,'6058baa3',2410,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(6513,'6058baa3',2411,'Explain the different types of blood groups and their importance in blood transfusion.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Blood groups are determined by the presence or absence of antigens on the surface of red blood cells.  The main blood groups are A, B, AB, and O.  Blood transfusion requires compatibility between donor and recipient blood groups to prevent adverse reactions.'),(6514,'6058baa3',2412,'Explain the concept of electric current, potential difference, and resistance.  State Ohm\'s law.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Electric current is the flow of electric charge. Potential difference is the driving force that pushes the current. Resistance opposes the flow of current. Ohm\'s law states that the current through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature remains constant.'),(6515,'6058baa3',2413,'Describe the different types of mirrors and lenses, and their applications.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Mirrors can be plane, concave, or convex. Lenses can be concave or convex. Plane mirrors form virtual images. Concave mirrors and convex lenses form real images, while convex mirrors and concave lenses form virtual images. Applications vary depending on the type of mirror or lens and its focal length.'),(6516,'6058baa3',2414,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Natural selection is the process by which organisms better adapted to their environment tend to survive and produce more offspring.  Variations within a population lead to some individuals having advantageous traits which increase their survival and reproductive success, leading to the gradual change of species over time.'),(6517,'6058baa3',2415,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Newton\n2. Mendeleev\n3. Einstein\n4. Darwin\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Periodic Table\nC. Theory of Evolution\nD. Laws of Motion','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-B, 3-A, 4-C'),(6518,'6058baa3',2416,'A student observed that a plant kept in a dark room for several days wilted and its leaves turned yellow.  When the plant was placed in sunlight, it recovered after a few days.\n\n(a) Explain why the plant wilted in the dark room.\n(b) Explain why the leaves turned yellow.\n(c) Explain why the plant recovered in sunlight.','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) The plant wilted due to lack of photosynthesis, which is essential for producing food and maintaining turgor pressure in cells. (b) The yellowing of the leaves is due to the breakdown of chlorophyll in the absence of light. (c) The plant recovered in sunlight because it was able to perform photosynthesis again, producing food and restoring its water balance.'),(6519,'c66ca2f7',2417,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6520,'c66ca2f7',2418,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6521,'c66ca2f7',2419,'Which of the following is NOT a greenhouse gas?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Carbon dioxide\", \"Methane\", \"Oxygen\", \"Nitrous oxide\"]','C'),(6522,'c66ca2f7',2420,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(6523,'c66ca2f7',2421,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Cylindrical lens\", \"Biconvex lens\"]','B'),(6524,'c66ca2f7',2422,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6525,'c66ca2f7',2423,'The force of attraction between two bodies due to their masses is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(6526,'c66ca2f7',2424,'The basic unit of heredity is the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(6527,'c66ca2f7',2425,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of water vapor is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6528,'c66ca2f7',2426,'An acid reacts with a base to form _______________ and _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','salt, water'),(6529,'c66ca2f7',2427,'The resistance of a conductor is directly proportional to its length and inversely proportional to its _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cross-sectional area'),(6530,'c66ca2f7',2428,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Physical changes are changes in the form or appearance of a substance, without changing its chemical composition. Chemical changes involve the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(6531,'c66ca2f7',2429,'What is the role of decomposers in an ecosystem?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Decomposers break down dead organic matter, recycling nutrients back into the ecosystem.'),(6532,'c66ca2f7',2430,'Define the term \'refraction of light\'.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Refraction of light is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.'),(6533,'c66ca2f7',2431,'State Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature remains constant.'),(6534,'c66ca2f7',2432,'Explain the process of respiration.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process by which living organisms release energy from food.  It involves the breakdown of glucose in the presence or absence of oxygen.'),(6535,'c66ca2f7',2433,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human respiratory system includes the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs. It is responsible for taking in oxygen and expelling carbon dioxide.'),(6536,'c66ca2f7',2434,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(6537,'c66ca2f7',2435,'Explain the different types of lenses and their uses.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex (converging) and concave (diverging). Convex lenses converge light rays and are used in magnifying glasses, telescopes, and cameras. Concave lenses diverge light rays and are used to correct myopia.'),(6538,'c66ca2f7',2436,'Describe the structure and function of the human eye.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The human eye consists of various parts like cornea, iris, pupil, lens, retina etc. working together to enable us to see.'),(6539,'c66ca2f7',2437,'Explain the concept of electric current, potential difference, and resistance.  State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Electric current is the rate of flow of electric charge. Potential difference is the work done per unit charge in moving a charge between two points. Resistance is the opposition to the flow of electric current. Ohm\'s law states that the current is directly proportional to the potential difference, provided the temperature remains constant. Its limitations include non-ohmic conductors and temperature dependence.'),(6540,'c66ca2f7',2438,'Discuss the causes and effects of global warming.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Global warming is primarily caused by the increase in greenhouse gases in the atmosphere, leading to an increase in the Earth\'s average temperature. Effects include rising sea levels, changes in weather patterns, and threats to biodiversity.'),(6541,'c66ca2f7',2439,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\n2.  Ampere\n3.  Joule\n4.  Watt\n\nColumn B\nA.  Unit of electric current\nB.  Unit of power\n C. Unit of energy\nD. Unit of force','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-A, 3-C, 4-B'),(6542,'c66ca2f7',2440,'A student is conducting an experiment to investigate the effect of different liquids on the rate of rusting of iron nails.  Three test tubes are prepared: Test tube A contains an iron nail immersed in distilled water, Test tube B contains an iron nail immersed in saltwater, and Test tube C contains an iron nail immersed in oil.\n\n(a)  In which test tube would you expect the most rusting to occur? Explain your answer.\n(b)  In which test tube would you expect the least rusting to occur? Explain your answer.\n(c)  What is the chemical name for rust?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Test tube B (saltwater): Saltwater is an electrolyte, providing ions that accelerate the electrochemical reactions involved in rust formation. \n(b) Test tube C (oil): Oil prevents oxygen and water from reaching the iron nail, preventing rust formation. \n(c) Iron(III) oxide (Fe2O3)'),(6543,'f0c334ea',2441,'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of a mammal?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Hair or fur\", \"Give birth to live young\", \"Lay eggs\", \"Mammary glands\"]','C'),(6544,'f0c334ea',2442,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6545,'f0c334ea',2443,'Which process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Digestion\", \"Excretion\"]','B'),(6546,'f0c334ea',2444,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Newton\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','B'),(6547,'f0c334ea',2445,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\"]','D'),(6548,'f0c334ea',2446,'The process of converting a solid directly into a gas is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','sublimation'),(6549,'f0c334ea',2447,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6550,'f0c334ea',2448,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6551,'f0c334ea',2449,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration'),(6552,'f0c334ea',2450,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cohesion'),(6553,'f0c334ea',2451,'The outermost shell of an atom is called the _______________ shell.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','valence'),(6554,'f0c334ea',2452,'Explain the difference between speed and velocity.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Speed is a scalar quantity that measures the rate of change of distance, while velocity is a vector quantity that measures the rate of change of displacement. Velocity includes both magnitude and direction.'),(6555,'f0c334ea',2453,'What is the role of ozone in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ozone layer in the stratosphere absorbs most of the harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6556,'f0c334ea',2454,'Describe the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration involves the intake of oxygen and the release of carbon dioxide. Oxygen is used to break down glucose, releasing energy for the body\'s functions.'),(6557,'f0c334ea',2455,'Explain the concept of Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6558,'f0c334ea',2456,'What are the different types of blood groups?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The main blood groups are A, B, AB, and O. Each group can be further categorized as Rh-positive or Rh-negative.'),(6559,'f0c334ea',2457,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.  Include a diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  (Diagram should be included showing the atria, ventricles, valves, and major blood vessels). The heart functions to circulate oxygenated blood to the body and deoxygenated blood to the lungs.'),(6560,'f0c334ea',2458,'Describe the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce glucose (a sugar) and oxygen.  It\'s crucial for producing food for the plant and releasing oxygen into the atmosphere, which is essential for animal life.  The process occurs in chloroplasts and involves light-dependent and light-independent reactions.'),(6561,'f0c334ea',2459,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into various types including combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox, and neutralization reactions.  Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6562,'f0c334ea',2460,'Explain the laws of reflection of light. Draw a ray diagram to illustrate the laws.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','The laws of reflection state that the angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection, and the incident ray, reflected ray, and normal to the surface at the point of incidence all lie in the same plane.'),(6563,'f0c334ea',2461,'Describe the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Types of pollution include air, water, soil, noise, and light pollution.  Explain the sources and harmful effects of each type.'),(6564,'f0c334ea',2462,'Explain Mendel\'s laws of inheritance with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Mendel\'s laws include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment. Explain these laws with examples of monohybrid and dihybrid crosses.'),(6565,'f0c334ea',2463,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Electric Current\n2.  Electric Potential\n3.  Resistance\n4.  Electric Power\n\nColumn B\nA.  Ohm\nB.  Ampere\nC.  Volt\nD.  Watt','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-C, 3-A, 4-D'),(6566,'f0c334ea',2464,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well despite sufficient sunlight and water. He suspects a nutrient deficiency in the soil.  He conducts a soil test and finds a deficiency in nitrogen. \n(a) What are the symptoms of nitrogen deficiency in plants?\n(b) What are some nitrogen-rich fertilizers that can be used to improve soil fertility?\n(c) Explain the importance of nitrogen for plant growth. \n(d) What are some sustainable agricultural practices to maintain soil fertility?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Symptoms of nitrogen deficiency include stunted growth, yellowing of leaves (chlorosis), and poor yield. \n(b) Examples of nitrogen-rich fertilizers include urea, ammonium nitrate, and ammonium sulfate. \n(c) Nitrogen is essential for plant growth as it is a key component of chlorophyll, amino acids, and proteins. \n(d) Sustainable practices include crop rotation, cover cropping, and using organic fertilizers.'),(6567,'7118c954',2465,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6568,'7118c954',2466,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6569,'7118c954',2467,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6570,'7118c954',2468,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6571,'7118c954',2469,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(6572,'7118c954',2470,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Cylindrical lens\", \"Plano-convex lens\"]','B'),(6573,'7118c954',2471,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It involves the use of carbon dioxide and water, releasing oxygen as a byproduct.'),(6574,'7118c954',2472,'What are the different states of matter? Explain briefly.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three common states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a definite shape and volume. Liquids have a definite volume but take the shape of their container. Gases have neither a definite shape nor volume.'),(6575,'7118c954',2473,'Define acids and bases. Give two examples of each.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Acids are substances that taste sour and turn blue litmus red. Examples: Hydrochloric acid (HCl), Sulphuric acid (H2SO4). Bases are substances that taste bitter and turn red litmus blue. Examples: Sodium hydroxide (NaOH), Calcium hydroxide (Ca(OH)2).'),(6576,'7118c954',2474,'What is Newton\'s third law of motion? Give an example.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Newton\'s third law states that for every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.  Example: When you walk, you push backward on the ground, and the ground pushes forward on you, propelling you forward.'),(6577,'7118c954',2475,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of a substance, forming new substances (e.g., burning wood).'),(6578,'7118c954',2476,'What is the function of the human respiratory system?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The respiratory system is responsible for taking in oxygen from the air and releasing carbon dioxide from the body. This process is essential for cellular respiration, providing energy for the body\'s functions.'),(6579,'7118c954',2477,'Describe the structure of an atom.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','An atom consists of a central nucleus containing protons (positively charged) and neutrons (no charge), surrounded by electrons (negatively charged) orbiting in shells or energy levels.'),(6580,'7118c954',2478,'Explain the process of digestion in the human body.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Digestion is the process of breaking down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed into the bloodstream. It starts in the mouth with mechanical and chemical digestion, continues in the stomach with further breakdown by acids and enzymes, and is completed in the small intestine where nutrients are absorbed. The large intestine absorbs water, and waste is eliminated.'),(6581,'7118c954',2479,'Describe the different types of blood groups and explain the concept of blood transfusion.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The four main blood groups are A, B, AB, and O. Each group has different antigens and antibodies. Blood transfusions must match compatible blood groups to avoid adverse reactions.  O-negative blood is the universal donor, while AB-positive is the universal recipient.'),(6582,'7118c954',2480,'Explain the process of reproduction in flowering plants.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Flowering plants reproduce sexually through pollination, where pollen grains from the anther are transferred to the stigma.  Fertilization occurs, forming a zygote that develops into a seed within a fruit.  The seed contains the embryo and stored food, allowing for germination and the growth of a new plant.'),(6583,'7118c954',2481,'Explain Ohm\'s law and its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across it, provided the temperature remains constant.  Its applications include calculating resistance, voltage, or current in circuits, and understanding the behavior of electrical components.'),(6584,'7118c954',2482,'Explain the structure and functions of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The nervous system consists of the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system (nerves). It receives, processes, and transmits information throughout the body, coordinating actions and responses to stimuli.  The brain is the control center, responsible for higher-level functions, while the spinal cord acts as a communication pathway.'),(6585,'7118c954',2483,'Match the following:\nColumn A\n1.  Iron\n2.  Chlorophyll\n3.  Vitamin C\n4.  Oxygen\n5.  Sodium\nColumn B\nA.  Photosynthesis\nB.  Hemoglobin\n C.  Scurvy\nD.  Respiration\nE.  Electrolyte balance','Matching','Medium',5,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-C, 4-D, 5-E'),(6586,'7118c954',2484,'Match the following:\nColumn A\n1.  Force\n2.  Work\n3.  Energy\n4.  Power\n5.  Pressure\nColumn B\nA.  Joule\nB.  Newton\n C.  Watt\nD.  Pascal\nE.  Joule/second','Matching','Medium',5,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-A, 4-E, 5-D'),(6587,'7118c954',2485,'Match the following:\nColumn A\n1.  Acids\n2.  Bases\n3.  Salts\n4.  Indicators\n5.  pH scale\nColumn B\nA.  Litmus paper\nB.  Neutralization reaction\n C.  Sour taste\nD.  Bitter taste\nE.  0 to 14','Matching','Medium',6,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-B, 4-A, 5-E'),(6588,'7118c954',2486,'A student conducts an experiment to investigate the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction.  They mix two solutions at different temperatures and observe the time taken for a color change. At 25°C, the reaction takes 100 seconds. At 35°C, the reaction takes 50 seconds. At 45°C, the reaction takes 25 seconds. \n(a) What is the independent variable in this experiment?\n(b) What is the dependent variable?\n(c) What is the relationship between temperature and reaction rate?\n(d) Explain why the reaction rate increases with temperature.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Temperature\n(b) Reaction rate (time taken for color change)\n(c) As temperature increases, reaction rate increases.\n(d) Higher temperature means more kinetic energy in the reacting molecules, leading to more frequent and successful collisions, thus faster reaction.'),(6589,'7118c954',2343,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Electric current\n2.  Resistance\n3.  Potential difference\n4.  Power\n\nColumn B\nA.  Volt\nB.  Watt\n C.  Ampere\nD.  Ohm','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6590,'7118c954',2415,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Newton\n2. Mendeleev\n3. Einstein\n4. Darwin\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Periodic Table\nC. Theory of Evolution\nD. Laws of Motion','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-B, 3-A, 4-C'),(6591,'7118c954',2439,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\n2.  Ampere\n3.  Joule\n4.  Watt\n\nColumn B\nA.  Unit of electric current\nB.  Unit of power\n C. Unit of energy\nD. Unit of force','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-A, 3-C, 4-B'),(6592,'7118c954',2463,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Electric Current\n2.  Electric Potential\n3.  Resistance\n4.  Electric Power\n\nColumn B\nA.  Ohm\nB.  Ampere\nC.  Volt\nD.  Watt','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-C, 3-A, 4-D'),(6593,'7118c954',2195,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Acid rain\n2.  Ozone layer\n3.  Global warming\n4.  Deforestation\n\nColumn B\nA.  Increased CO2 levels\nB.  Loss of forest cover\nC.  Damage to plants and buildings\nD.  Protection from UV radiation','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6594,'7118c954',2023,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Ohm\'s Law\n2.  Power\n3.  Energy\n4.  Current\n\nColumn B\nA.  Joules\nB.  Watts\nC.  Amperes\nD.  V=IR','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-B, 3-A, 4-C'),(6595,'7118c954',1995,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Transpiration\n4.  Excretion\n\nColumn B\nA. Removal of waste products\nB. Release of energy from food\nC. Water loss from leaves\nD. Making food using sunlight','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-B, 3-C, 4-A'),(6596,'7118c954',1967,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Sodium Chloride\n2.  Hydrochloric Acid\n3.  Sodium Hydroxide\n4.  Carbon Dioxide\n\nColumn B\nA. Acid\nB. Base\nC. Salt\nD. Oxide','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B, 4-D'),(6597,'7118c954',2367,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\n2.  Pascal\n3.  Joule\n4.  Watt\n\nColumn B\nA.  Unit of power\nB.  Unit of force\nC.  Unit of energy\nD.  Unit of pressure','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-D, 3-C, 4-A'),(6598,'7118c954',2099,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Excretion\n4.  Transpiration\n\nColumn B\nA. Removal of waste products\nB. Release of water vapor from leaves\nC. Conversion of light energy into chemical energy\nD. Release of energy from food','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6599,'7118c954',2272,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\'s First Law\n2.  Newton\'s Second Law\n3.  Newton\'s Third Law\n4.  Inertia\n\nColumn B\nA.  F = ma\nB.  For every action, there\'s an equal and opposite reaction\nC.  An object at rest stays at rest unless acted upon by an external force\nD.  Tendency of an object to resist changes in motion','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B, 4-D'),(6600,'7118c954',2319,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Albert Einstein\n3. Marie Curie\n4. Charles Darwin\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Principles of Inheritance\nC. Theory of Evolution\nD. Discovery of Radium','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-D, 4-C'),(6601,'7118c954',2295,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Transpiration\n4.  Germination\n\nColumn B\nA.  Loss of water vapor from plants\nB.  Process of seed development into seedling\nC.  Process of making food in plants\nD.  Process of releasing energy from food','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6602,'9d88859f',2487,'Which of the following is NOT a greenhouse gas?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Carbon dioxide\", \"Methane\", \"Oxygen\", \"Nitrous oxide\"]','C'),(6603,'9d88859f',2488,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6604,'9d88859f',2489,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Cylindrical lens\", \"Biconvex lens\"]','B'),(6605,'9d88859f',2490,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6606,'9d88859f',2491,'Which element is most reactive among alkali metals?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Lithium\", \"Sodium\", \"Potassium\", \"Francium\"]','D'),(6607,'9d88859f',2492,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _________.  Plants use ________ to carry out this process.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis, chlorophyll'),(6608,'9d88859f',2493,'The force of attraction between two objects due to their masses is called _______. Its strength depends on the ______ of the objects and the distance between them.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gravity, masses'),(6609,'9d88859f',2494,'The smallest unit of an element that can exist independently is called an _______.  Atoms combine to form _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','atom, molecules'),(6610,'9d88859f',2495,'The process by which plants lose water through their leaves is called ________.  This process mainly occurs through the ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration, stomata'),(6611,'9d88859f',2496,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______ and bases turn red litmus paper ______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red, blue'),(6612,'9d88859f',2497,'The functional unit of the kidney is called a _________.  It filters the blood to produce ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','nephron, urine'),(6613,'9d88859f',2498,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6614,'9d88859f',2499,'What is the role of the ozone layer in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The ozone layer absorbs most of the harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6615,'9d88859f',2500,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current through a conductor between two points is directly proportional to the voltage across the two points, provided the temperature remains constant.  V = IR'),(6616,'9d88859f',2501,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves breathing (inhaling and exhaling), gas exchange in the lungs, and cellular respiration.'),(6617,'9d88859f',2502,'Describe the structure and function of a neuron.','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','A neuron is a nerve cell composed of dendrites, a cell body, and an axon. It transmits nerve impulses throughout the body.'),(6618,'9d88859f',2503,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, neutralization, redox, and precipitation reactions.  Examples should be given for each type.'),(6619,'9d88859f',2504,'Describe the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  It is crucial for the food chain and oxygen production.'),(6620,'9d88859f',2505,'Explain the working of the human digestive system with a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','A detailed explanation of the digestive process, including mechanical and chemical digestion, along with a labeled diagram of the digestive system.'),(6621,'9d88859f',2506,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Explain sexual and asexual reproduction in plants with examples (e.g., vegetative propagation, budding, binary fission).'),(6622,'9d88859f',2507,'Discuss the different types of pollution and their impact on the environment.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Discuss air, water, soil, and noise pollution and their harmful effects on living organisms and ecosystems.'),(6623,'9d88859f',2508,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart with a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','A detailed explanation of the heart\'s structure, including chambers, valves, and blood vessels, and its role in circulation, along with a labeled diagram.'),(6624,'9d88859f',2509,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Isaac Newton\n3. Albert Einstein\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Laws of Motion\nC. Principles of Inheritance','Matching','Medium',3,'null','1-C, 2-B, 3-A'),(6625,'9d88859f',2510,'A farmer noticed that his crops were not growing well despite sufficient sunlight and water.  Upon investigation, it was found that the soil lacked essential nutrients.  Explain the importance of soil nutrients for plant growth. What are some ways the farmer can improve soil fertility?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','Soil nutrients are essential for plant growth as they provide the building blocks for various plant processes. The farmer can improve soil fertility through methods like crop rotation, adding organic manure, and using fertilizers.'),(6626,'ee351c8b',2511,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6627,'ee351c8b',2512,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6628,'ee351c8b',2513,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6629,'ee351c8b',2514,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6630,'ee351c8b',2515,'Which element has the atomic number 6?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Hydrogen\", \"Carbon\", \"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\"]','B'),(6631,'ee351c8b',2516,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6632,'ee351c8b',2517,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Cohesion'),(6633,'ee351c8b',2518,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(6634,'ee351c8b',2519,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6635,'ee351c8b',2520,'The process by which plants lose water vapor through their leaves is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6636,'ee351c8b',2521,'The SI unit of power is the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Watt'),(6637,'ee351c8b',2522,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but does not change its chemical composition. A chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(6638,'ee351c8b',2523,'What is the role of enzymes in digestion?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Enzymes are biological catalysts that speed up the rate of chemical reactions in digestion, breaking down complex food molecules into simpler, absorbable forms.'),(6639,'ee351c8b',2524,'State Ohm\'s law. Write the formula and define each term.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current through a conductor between two points is directly proportional to the voltage across the two points. Formula: V = IR, where V is voltage, I is current, and R is resistance.'),(6640,'ee351c8b',2525,'What are the three states of matter? Describe their properties.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have definite shape and volume, liquids have definite volume but indefinite shape, and gases have neither definite shape nor volume.'),(6641,'ee351c8b',2526,'Define the term \'reflex action\' and give an example.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A reflex action is a rapid, automatic, involuntary response to a stimulus. Example: withdrawing your hand when you touch a hot object.'),(6642,'ee351c8b',2527,'Explain the process of photosynthesis, including the reactants, products, and the role of chlorophyll.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water. Reactants: carbon dioxide and water. Products: glucose and oxygen. Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light energy, which is then used to drive the process of photosynthesis.'),(6643,'ee351c8b',2528,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood from the body and lungs, and the ventricles pump blood to the body and lungs. The heart valves ensure that blood flows in only one direction.'),(6644,'ee351c8b',2529,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants reproduce through sexual reproduction (involving the fusion of gametes) and asexual reproduction (without the fusion of gametes). Sexual reproduction involves the formation of seeds from flowers, while asexual reproduction can occur through vegetative propagation (e.g., runners in strawberries, bulbs in onions).'),(6645,'ee351c8b',2530,'Explain the concept of electric potential and potential difference.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Electric potential is the work done per unit charge in bringing a small positive test charge from infinity to a point in an electric field. Potential difference is the difference in electric potential between two points in an electric field, which is measured in volts.'),(6646,'ee351c8b',2531,'Explain the various types of pollution and their harmful effects on the environment and human health.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Pollution can be categorized as air, water, and soil pollution. Air pollution can cause respiratory problems, water pollution can contaminate drinking water sources, and soil pollution can affect plant growth. All forms of pollution pose significant threats to human health and the environment.'),(6647,'ee351c8b',2532,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Natural selection is the process by which organisms better adapted to their environment tend to survive and produce more offspring.  This leads to the gradual change in the characteristics of a population over time, resulting in the evolution of new species.'),(6648,'ee351c8b',2533,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Louis Pasteur\n3. Isaac Newton\n4. Albert Einstein\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Laws of Motion\nC. Germ Theory of Disease\nD. Principles of Inheritance','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-C, 3-B, 4-A'),(6649,'ee351c8b',2534,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. He notices that the leaves are yellowing and the plants are stunted. He suspects a nutrient deficiency in the soil.  \n\n(a) What nutrient deficiency might be causing this problem?  \n(b) What are the symptoms of this deficiency? \n(c) How can the farmer address this deficiency to improve crop growth?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Nitrogen deficiency\n(b) Yellowing leaves, stunted growth, reduced yield\n(c) The farmer can use nitrogen-rich fertilizers or incorporate nitrogen-fixing plants into his crop rotation.'),(6650,'ad88148d',2535,'किस कहानी में एक लकड़हारा मुख्य पात्र है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"निमंत्रण\", \"बूढ़ा वृक्ष\", \"लकड़हारा और ईश्वर\", \"भगत\"]','C'),(6651,'ad88148d',2536,' ‘अंधेर नगरी’ किसकी रचना है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"भारतेन्दु हरिश्चन्द्र\", \"जयशंकर प्रसाद\", \"महादेवी वर्मा\", \"सूर्यकांत त्रिपाठी \'निराला\'\"]','A'),(6652,'ad88148d',2537,' ‘मनुष्य की महानता’ किसकी रचना है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"रामधारी सिंह दिनकर\", \"सोहन लाल द्विवेदी\", \"जायसी\", \"प्रगतिशील कवि\"]','A'),(6653,'ad88148d',2538,' ‘पतझड़’ किस कवि की रचना है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"निराला\", \"प्रसाद\", \"पंत\", \"महादेवी वर्मा\"]','D'),(6654,'ad88148d',2539,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा शब्द विशेषण नहीं है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"सुन्दर\", \"लम्बा\", \"घर\", \"उच्च\"]','C'),(6655,'ad88148d',2540,'________ एक प्रसिद्ध कवि थे।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','सूर्यकान्त त्रिपाठी निराला'),(6656,'ad88148d',2541,' ‘कामायनी’  ________ की रचना है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जयशंकर प्रसाद'),(6657,'ad88148d',2542,'रामधारी सिंह दिनकर  ________ युग के कवि थे।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','आधुनिक'),(6658,'ad88148d',2543,' ‘उसने  ________  किया।’ (क्रिया विशेषण)','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','धीरे-धीरे'),(6659,'ad88148d',2544,' ‘अनपढ़’ शब्द का विलोम शब्द ________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','पढ़ा लिखा'),(6660,'ad88148d',2545,' ‘निर्धन’ शब्द का पर्यायवाची शब्द ________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','गरीब'),(6661,'ad88148d',2546,'‘निमंत्रण’ कहानी का सारांश लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','निमंत्रण कहानी में एक व्यक्ति अपने मित्र को भोजन के लिए बुलाता है, लेकिन मित्र के आने पर उसे  भोजन नहीं मिल पाता है। यह कहानी मानव स्वभाव की कमजोरियों को दर्शाती है।'),(6662,'ad88148d',2547,' ‘बूढ़ा वृक्ष’ कहानी का मुख्य संदेश क्या है?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','प्रकृति के प्रति सम्मान और उसकी रक्षा करने का संदेश।'),(6663,'ad88148d',2548,' ‘अंधेर नगरी’ कहानी का केंद्रीय विचार क्या है?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','यह कहानी व्यंग्य के माध्यम से समाज की बुराइयों और भ्रष्टाचार का चित्रण करती है।'),(6664,'ad88148d',2549,' ‘मनुष्य की महानता’ कविता का भावार्थ संक्षेप में लिखिए।','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','कविता मनुष्य की महानता और उसके कर्मों के महत्व पर प्रकाश डालती है।'),(6665,'ad88148d',2550,' ‘पतझड़’ कविता में किस ऋतु का वर्णन है और उसका क्या महत्व है?','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','पतझड़ कविता में शरद ऋतु का वर्णन है। यह ऋतु परिवर्तन और जीवन के चक्र का प्रतीक है।'),(6666,'ad88148d',2551,' ‘निमंत्रण’ कहानी का विस्तृत सारांश लिखिए और कहानी के पात्रों का चरित्र चित्रण कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','विवरण दिया जाना चाहिए'),(6667,'ad88148d',2552,' ‘बूढ़ा वृक्ष’ कहानी में वृक्ष के चरित्र का विश्लेषण कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','विवरण दिया जाना चाहिए'),(6668,'ad88148d',2553,' ‘अंधेर नगरी’ कहानी में प्रयुक्त व्यंग्य का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','विवरण दिया जाना चाहिए'),(6669,'ad88148d',2554,' ‘मनुष्य की महानता’ कविता का सौंदर्य बोध  व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','विवरण दिया जाना चाहिए'),(6670,'ad88148d',2555,' ‘पतझड़’ कविता के प्रमुख बिम्बों की व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','विवरण दिया जाना चाहिए'),(6671,'ad88148d',2556,'आधुनिक काल के किसी एक कवि का परिचय देते हुए उसकी प्रमुख रचनाओं का उल्लेख कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','विवरण दिया जाना चाहिए'),(6672,'ad88148d',2557,'कॉलम A में दिए गए शब्दों को कॉलम B में दिए गए उनके अर्थों से मिलाएँ:\n\nकॉलम A\n1. प्रसाद\n2. निराला\n3. दिनकर\n4. महादेवी वर्मा\n\nकॉलम B\nA. पतझड़\nB. कामायनी\nC. मनुष्य की महानता\nD. राम की शक्तिपूजा','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-D, 3-C, 4-A'),(6673,'ad88148d',2558,'नीचे दी गई पंक्तियों को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और प्रश्नों का उत्तर दीजिये:\n\n“फिर भी मैं जीना चाहता हूँ,\nइस धरती पर, इस दुनिया में,\nजहाँ इतना दुःख, इतनी पीड़ा है।\nलेकिन फिर भी आशा की किरण दिखाई देती है।”\n\nप्रश्न:\n(क) इस पंक्तियों में किस भाव की अभिव्यक्ति हुई है?\n(ख) इस भाव की पुष्टि पंक्तियों के किस अंश से होती है?\n(ग) इस भाव से लेखक के जीवन दर्शन को कैसे समझते हैं?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(क) जीवन के प्रति आशावाद और दृढ़ संकल्प।\n(ख) “लेकिन फिर भी आशा की किरण दिखाई देती है”\n(ग) लेखक जीवन की कठिनाइयों के बावजूद आशावादी है और जीवन जीने के लिए प्रेरित है।'),(6674,'1f643dd0',2559,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6675,'1f643dd0',2560,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6676,'1f643dd0',2561,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Nuclear energy\", \"Hydro energy\"]','C'),(6677,'1f643dd0',2562,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"H2O2\", \"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\"]','D'),(6678,'1f643dd0',2563,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6679,'1f643dd0',2564,'The process by which plants make their own food is called __________.  The basic unit of life is the __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis, cell'),(6680,'1f643dd0',2565,'The force of attraction between similar kinds of molecules is called __________, while the force of attraction between different kinds of molecules is called __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Cohesion, adhesion'),(6681,'1f643dd0',2566,'The SI unit of force is the __________, and the SI unit of energy is the __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton, Joule'),(6682,'1f643dd0',2567,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called __________, and this process takes place in the __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Photosynthesis, chloroplast'),(6683,'1f643dd0',2568,'Acids turn blue litmus paper __________, while bases turn red litmus paper __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red, blue'),(6684,'1f643dd0',2569,'The smallest particle of an element is called an __________, while a group of atoms bonded together is called a __________. ','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','atom, molecule'),(6685,'1f643dd0',2570,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but not its chemical composition, while a chemical change involves a change in chemical composition, forming new substances.'),(6686,'1f643dd0',2571,'What is the law of conservation of mass?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The law of conservation of mass states that mass cannot be created or destroyed in a chemical reaction; it only changes form.'),(6687,'1f643dd0',2572,'Describe the process of osmosis.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Osmosis is the movement of water molecules across a semi-permeable membrane from a region of higher water concentration to a region of lower water concentration.'),(6688,'1f643dd0',2573,'Explain the difference between renewable and non-renewable resources.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Renewable resources are naturally replenished at a rate comparable to or faster than their consumption, while non-renewable resources are consumed much faster than they are replenished.'),(6689,'1f643dd0',2574,'What are the three states of matter and how do they differ?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a definite shape and volume, liquids have a definite volume but no definite shape, and gases have neither a definite shape nor volume.'),(6690,'1f643dd0',2575,'Explain the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs.  Its function is to take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide through breathing.'),(6691,'1f643dd0',2576,'Describe the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  It\'s crucial for producing food and oxygen for most life on Earth.'),(6692,'1f643dd0',2577,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Examples include combination, decomposition, displacement, and double displacement reactions.'),(6693,'1f643dd0',2578,'Describe the structure and function of the human nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The nervous system consists of the brain, spinal cord, and nerves. It controls and coordinates bodily functions through electrical and chemical signals.'),(6694,'1f643dd0',2579,'Explain the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Air, water, and soil pollution have various harmful effects on the environment and human health.'),(6695,'1f643dd0',2580,'Discuss the different types of energy resources and their advantages and disadvantages.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Renewable (solar, wind, hydro) and non-renewable (fossil fuels, nuclear) energy sources have varying advantages and disadvantages regarding sustainability, cost, and environmental impact.'),(6696,'1f643dd0',2581,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Newton\n2. Einstein\n3. Mendeleev\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Periodic Table\nC. Laws of Motion','Matching','Medium',3,'null','1-C, 2-A, 3-B'),(6697,'1f643dd0',2582,'A farmer observes that his crops are not growing well. He notices that the soil is dry and lacks nutrients. He also observes that the water in his well is becoming increasingly polluted.  \n\n(a) Identify the environmental problems faced by the farmer.\n(b) Suggest ways the farmer can improve his soil health and water quality.\n(c) Explain how these problems are interconnected.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Soil degradation (lack of nutrients, dryness), water pollution.\n(b) Soil improvement through composting, crop rotation, and using organic fertilizers. Water quality improvement through rainwater harvesting and wastewater treatment.\n(c) Polluted water can affect soil health, while poor soil health can lead to increased water runoff and pollution.'),(6698,'f1446427',2583,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6699,'f1446427',2584,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6700,'f1446427',2585,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6701,'f1446427',2586,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(6702,'f1446427',2587,'Which process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Digestion\", \"Combustion\"]','B'),(6703,'f1446427',2588,'The process of converting a solid directly into a gas is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','sublimation'),(6704,'f1446427',2589,'The SI unit of force is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6705,'f1446427',2590,'The nucleus of an atom contains ______________ and ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','protons, neutrons'),(6706,'f1446427',2591,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6707,'f1446427',2592,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of water vapour is called ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration'),(6708,'f1446427',2593,'The resistance of a conductor is inversely proportional to its ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cross-sectional area'),(6709,'f1446427',2594,'The basic unit of heredity is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(6710,'f1446427',2595,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change is a change in the form or appearance of a substance, but not its chemical composition. A chemical change involves the formation of new substances with different chemical properties.'),(6711,'f1446427',2596,'What are the three states of matter? Briefly describe each.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a fixed shape and volume. Liquids have a fixed volume but take the shape of their container. Gases have neither a fixed shape nor volume.'),(6712,'f1446427',2597,'Define Newton\'s First Law of Motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Newton\'s First Law of Motion (Inertia): An object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.'),(6713,'f1446427',2598,'What is the function of chlorophyll in plants?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Chlorophyll is a pigment that absorbs light energy, which is then used to carry out photosynthesis.'),(6714,'f1446427',2599,'Explain the concept of reflection of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface. The angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection.'),(6715,'f1446427',2600,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The respiratory system consists of the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, bronchioles, and alveoli.  It facilitates the intake of oxygen and the removal of carbon dioxide from the body through the process of respiration.  Describe each component and its role in detail.'),(6716,'f1446427',2601,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  Include a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll. The process converts light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  A balanced chemical equation is 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2. Explain the different stages of photosynthesis.'),(6717,'f1446427',2602,'Explain Ohm\'s Law and its applications. Draw a circuit diagram showing how to measure resistance using an ammeter and a voltmeter.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Ohm\'s Law states that the current through a conductor between two points is directly proportional to the voltage across the two points, and inversely proportional to the resistance between them.  V = IR. Explain applications and draw the circuit diagram.'),(6718,'f1446427',2603,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Describe combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions with relevant examples.'),(6719,'f1446427',2604,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants. Give examples for each type.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Explain sexual reproduction (involving pollination, fertilization) and asexual reproduction (vegetative propagation, budding, etc.) in plants with examples of each type.'),(6720,'f1446427',2605,'Explain the different types of pollutants and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Discuss air, water, and soil pollution, their sources, and their harmful effects on various aspects of the environment (e.g., acid rain, ozone depletion, global warming, eutrophication).'),(6721,'f1446427',2606,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Acid rain\n2.  Ozone depletion\n3.  Global warming\n4.  Deforestation\n\nColumn B\nA. Increased carbon dioxide levels\nB. Loss of habitat\nC. CFCs\nD. Sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-C, 3-A, 4-B'),(6722,'f1446427',2607,'A farmer observes that his crop yield is significantly reduced this year compared to last year. He notices that the soil is dry and lacks nutrients. The leaves of the plants are yellowing, and some plants are showing signs of wilting. \n\n(a) What could be the possible reasons for the reduced crop yield?\n(b) Suggest solutions to improve the soil conditions and crop health.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Possible reasons include nutrient deficiency in the soil, lack of water, pest infestation, or disease. (b) Solutions include soil testing to determine nutrient levels, irrigation to provide water, using fertilizers to replenish nutrients, and pest/disease management strategies.'),(6723,'236912da',2608,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transformation\"]','D'),(6724,'236912da',2609,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6725,'236912da',2610,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\", \"Petroleum\"]','C'),(6726,'236912da',2611,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6727,'236912da',2612,'Which process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fermentation\"]','B'),(6728,'236912da',2613,'The process of converting a solid directly into a gas is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','sublimation'),(6729,'236912da',2614,'The functional group present in carboxylic acids is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','-COOH'),(6730,'236912da',2615,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cohesion'),(6731,'236912da',2616,'The basic unit of heredity is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6732,'236912da',2617,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','transpiration'),(6733,'236912da',2618,'The splitting of white light into its constituent colours is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','dispersion'),(6734,'236912da',2619,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(6735,'236912da',2620,'What is the role of enzymes in digestion?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Enzymes are biological catalysts that speed up the rate of digestion by breaking down complex food molecules into simpler ones that can be absorbed by the body.'),(6736,'236912da',2621,'Describe the structure of an atom.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','An atom consists of a central nucleus containing protons and neutrons, surrounded by orbiting electrons.'),(6737,'236912da',2622,'Explain the concept of homologous series in organic chemistry.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A homologous series is a group of organic compounds with the same functional group and similar chemical properties, differing by a -CH2 unit.'),(6738,'236912da',2623,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR'),(6739,'236912da',2624,'Explain the process of photosynthesis. Include the equation for photosynthesis and discuss its importance.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce glucose (a sugar) and oxygen. Equation: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2.  It is crucial for the production of food and oxygen in the ecosystem.'),(6740,'236912da',2625,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions. Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6741,'236912da',2626,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants. Give examples.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Plants reproduce through asexual reproduction (e.g., vegetative propagation) and sexual reproduction (e.g., pollination).  Details and examples should be provided for each type.'),(6742,'236912da',2627,'Explain the human respiratory system. Discuss the process of breathing and the role of alveoli in gas exchange.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The respiratory system includes the nose, trachea, bronchi, lungs and alveoli. Breathing involves inhalation and exhalation. Alveoli are the sites of gas exchange where oxygen diffuses into the blood and carbon dioxide diffuses out.'),(6743,'236912da',2628,'Explain Mendel\'s laws of inheritance with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','Mendel\'s laws include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment.  Explanation and examples of monohybrid and dihybrid crosses should be provided.'),(6744,'236912da',2629,'Discuss the different types of lenses and their uses. Explain how a simple microscope works.','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','Lenses can be converging (convex) or diverging (concave).  A simple microscope uses a converging lens to magnify an object.  Details should be provided about their workings.'),(6745,'236912da',2630,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  HCl\n2.  NaOH\n3.  NaCl\n4.  H2SO4\n\nColumn B\nA.  Sodium hydroxide\nB.  Hydrochloric acid\nC.  Sulfuric acid\nD.  Sodium chloride','Matching','Easy',2,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-D, 4-C'),(6746,'236912da',2631,'A farmer noticed that his crop yield was low despite using fertilizers. He consulted an agricultural expert who suggested testing the soil pH. The soil test revealed that the soil was highly acidic. \n(a) What is soil pH? \n(b) How does acidic soil affect crop growth? \n(c) Suggest methods to improve the soil pH.','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) Soil pH is a measure of the acidity or alkalinity of the soil. (b) Acidic soil affects crop growth by hindering nutrient availability and causing toxicity. (c) Methods to improve soil pH include adding lime or other alkaline materials.'),(6747,'69a80d92',2632,'Which river is considered sacred in Hinduism?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Ganges\", \"Nile\", \"Amazon\", \"Yangtze\"]','A'),(6748,'69a80d92',2633,'What is the capital of India?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Mumbai\", \"Delhi\", \"Kolkata\", \"Chennai\"]','B'),(6749,'69a80d92',2634,'Which mountain range is the longest in the world?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Himalayas\", \"Andes\", \"Rocky Mountains\", \"Alps\"]','B'),(6750,'69a80d92',2635,'Who is considered the father of modern India?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Mahatma Gandhi\", \"Jawaharlal Nehru\", \"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel\", \"Subhas Chandra Bose\"]','A'),(6751,'69a80d92',2636,'Which country gifted the Statue of Liberty to the United States?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"England\", \"France\", \"Germany\", \"Italy\"]','B'),(6752,'69a80d92',2637,'What is the name of Earth\'s only natural satellite?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Sun\", \"Mars\", \"Moon\", \"Venus\"]','C'),(6753,'69a80d92',2638,'Which ancient civilization developed the concept of zero?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Egyptian\", \"Roman\", \"Greek\", \"Indian\"]','D'),(6754,'69a80d92',2639,'What is the name of the longest river in Africa?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Amazon\", \"Nile\", \"Yangtze\", \"Mississippi\"]','B'),(6755,'69a80d92',2640,'In which year did World War II end?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"1918\", \"1939\", \"1945\", \"1950\"]','C'),(6756,'69a80d92',2641,'What is the largest desert in the world?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Sahara Desert\", \"Arabian Desert\", \"Gobi Desert\", \"Antarctic Desert\"]','D'),(6757,'69a80d92',2642,'Which country is known as the \'Land of the Rising Sun\'?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"China\", \"India\", \"Japan\", \"South Korea\"]','C'),(6758,'69a80d92',2643,'What is the name of the process by which plants make their food?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Digestion\", \"Excretion\"]','B'),(6759,'69a80d92',2644,'Which gas is most abundant in the Earth\'s atmosphere?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Carbon Dioxide\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6760,'69a80d92',2645,'What is the chemical symbol for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6761,'69a80d92',2646,'Which planet is known for its rings?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Mars\", \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\", \"Venus\"]','C'),(6762,'69a80d92',2647,'What is the name of the largest ocean in the world?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Atlantic Ocean\", \"Indian Ocean\", \"Arctic Ocean\", \"Pacific Ocean\"]','D'),(6763,'69a80d92',2648,'Which type of government does India have?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Monarchy\", \"Dictatorship\", \"Democracy\", \"Oligarchy\"]','C'),(6764,'69a80d92',2649,'What is the highest peak in the world?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"K2\", \"Kangchenjunga\", \"Mount Everest\", \"Lhotse\"]','C'),(6765,'69a80d92',2650,'Which is the largest country in the world by land area?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"USA\", \"China\", \"Russia\", \"Canada\"]','C'),(6766,'69a80d92',2651,'What is the name of the process that breaks down rocks into smaller pieces?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Erosion\", \"Weathering\", \"Deposition\", \"Subduction\"]','B'),(6767,'00402da9',2652,'हिंदी भाषा किस लिपि में लिखी जाती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"देवनागरी\", \"अरबी\", \"रोमन\", \"गुजराती\"]','A'),(6768,'00402da9',2653,'“आकाश” का पर्यायवाची शब्द कौन सा है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"पृथ्वी\", \"आग\", \"अंबर\", \"पानी\"]','C'),(6769,'00402da9',2654,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा शब्द स्त्रीलिंग है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"घोड़ा\", \"गाय\", \"बकरा\", \"शेर\"]','B'),(6770,'00402da9',2655,'“पुस्तक” शब्द का बहुवचन क्या होगा?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"पुस्तकें\", \"पुस्तक\", \"पुस्तको\", \"पुस्तका\"]','A'),(6771,'00402da9',2656,'“दौड़ना” किस क्रिया का उदाहरण है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"सक्रिय\", \"समास\", \"संज्ञा\", \"विशेषण\"]','A'),(6772,'00402da9',2657,'“मधुर” शब्द का विलोम शब्द क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"कड़वा\", \"तीखा\", \"मीठा\", \"खट्टा\"]','A'),(6773,'00402da9',2658,'“अतिथि” शब्द का संधि विच्छेद क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"अति + इथि\", \"अ + तिथि\", \"अति + थी\", \"अ + तिथि\"]','A'),(6774,'00402da9',2659,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा शब्द शुद्ध है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"प्रतिभावान\", \"प्रतिभावाँन\", \"प्रतिभा वान\", \"प्रतिभा वांन\"]','A'),(6775,'00402da9',2660,'“सुंदर” शब्द में कौन सा प्रत्यय लगा है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"-र\", \"-दार\", \"-ता\", \"-अ\"]','A'),(6776,'00402da9',2661,'कौन सा शब्द विशेषण नहीं है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"लाल\", \"बड़ा\", \"ख़ूबसूरत\", \"दौड़ना\"]','D'),(6777,'00402da9',2662,'“उपवन” शब्द का अर्थ क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"बगीचा\", \"जंगल\", \"पहाड़\", \"नदी\"]','A'),(6778,'00402da9',2663,'“नीलकंठ” शब्द किस पक्षी के लिए प्रयोग होता है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"तोता\", \"मोर\", \"कौआ\", \"किंगफिशर\"]','D'),(6779,'00402da9',2664,'“सर्वनाम” किसे कहते हैं?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"संज्ञा का स्थान लेने वाले शब्द\", \"क्रिया का स्थान लेने वाले शब्द\", \"विशेषण का स्थान लेने वाले शब्द\", \"क्रिया विशेषण का स्थान लेने वाले शब्द\"]','A'),(6780,'00402da9',2665,'“अनेकार्थी शब्द” किसे कहते हैं?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"जिन शब्दों के कई अर्थ होते हैं\", \"जिन शब्दों का एक ही अर्थ होता है\", \"जिन शब्दों का कोई अर्थ नहीं होता\", \"जिन शब्दों का प्रयोग वाक्य में नहीं होता\"]','A'),(6781,'00402da9',2666,'“पर्वत” शब्द का पर्यायवाची शब्द नहीं है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"गिरि\", \"अचल\", \"पहाड़\", \"नदी\"]','D'),(6782,'00402da9',2667,'“अंधकार” का विलोम शब्द क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"प्रकाश\", \"अँधेरा\", \"छाया\", \"धूप\"]','A'),(6783,'00402da9',2668,'“सूरज” का पर्यायवाची शब्द कौन सा है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"चंद्रमा\", \"तारा\", \"दिवाकर\", \"आकाश\"]','C'),(6784,'00402da9',2669,'“घर” शब्द का बहुवचन क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"घर\", \"घरो\", \"घरों\", \"घरे\"]','C'),(6785,'00402da9',2670,'“फल” शब्द का पर्यायवाची शब्द कौन सा नहीं है?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"फल\", \"फला\", \"फलित\", \"फसल\"]','D'),(6786,'00402da9',2671,'“दयालु” शब्द का विलोम शब्द क्या है?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"क्रूर\", \"निष्ठुर\", \"दुष्ट\", \"नृशंस\"]','A'),(6787,'59e873ed',2672,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6788,'59e873ed',2673,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Newton\", \"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','A'),(6789,'59e873ed',2674,'Which of the following is NOT a type of tissue?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Epithelial tissue\", \"Connective tissue\", \"Nervous tissue\", \"Photosynthesis\"]','D'),(6790,'59e873ed',2675,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6791,'59e873ed',2676,'The force of attraction between any two objects having mass is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(6792,'59e873ed',2677,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(6793,'59e873ed',2678,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(6794,'59e873ed',2679,'Explain the difference between speed and velocity.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Speed is the rate of change of distance, while velocity is the rate of change of displacement. Velocity is a vector quantity (has both magnitude and direction), while speed is a scalar quantity (has only magnitude).'),(6795,'59e873ed',2680,'What are the different states of matter? Briefly describe each.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The three main states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a definite shape and volume, liquids have a definite volume but take the shape of their container, and gases have neither a definite shape nor volume.'),(6796,'59e873ed',2681,'Describe the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide.  It involves the intake of air into the lungs (inhalation), the exchange of gases in the alveoli (oxygen into the blood, carbon dioxide out), and the expulsion of air from the lungs (exhalation).'),(6797,'59e873ed',2682,'Explain Newton\'s first law of motion.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Newton\'s first law of motion, also known as the law of inertia, states that an object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion with the same speed and in the same direction unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.'),(6798,'59e873ed',2683,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart. Draw a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria (receiving chambers) and two ventricles (pumping chambers).  The heart has valves to prevent backflow of blood.  The right side of the heart pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs, and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.  (Diagram should show the four chambers, valves, and major blood vessels).'),(6799,'59e873ed',2684,'Describe the different types of forces. Give examples of each.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Forces can be classified into various types, including gravitational force (attraction between objects with mass), electromagnetic force (force between charged particles), strong nuclear force (holds protons and neutrons together in the nucleus), and weak nuclear force (involved in radioactive decay). Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6800,'59e873ed',2685,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  What are its products and importance?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  It involves chlorophyll and takes place in chloroplasts. The products are glucose and oxygen.  Photosynthesis is crucial for the food chain and for the production of oxygen in the atmosphere.'),(6801,'59e873ed',2686,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Chlorophyll\n2.  Stomata\n3.  Xylem\n4.  Phloem\n\nColumn B\nA.  Transport of water\nB.  Transport of food\nC.  Green pigment\nD.  Tiny pores on leaves','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(6802,'59e873ed',2687,'A student conducts an experiment to investigate the effect of temperature on the rate of a chemical reaction.  They measure the time it takes for a certain amount of a reactant to be consumed at different temperatures.  The results show that the reaction time decreases as the temperature increases.\n\n(a) What is the relationship between temperature and reaction rate?\n(b) Explain why increasing the temperature increases the reaction rate.\n(c) Suggest a possible error in the experiment that might affect the accuracy of the results.','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a)  The reaction rate increases as the temperature increases. \n(b) Increasing the temperature increases the kinetic energy of the reactant molecules. This leads to more frequent and energetic collisions, increasing the probability of successful collisions and thus the reaction rate.\n(c)  Possible errors include inaccurate temperature measurement, incomplete mixing of reactants, or variations in the amount of reactant used in different trials.'),(6803,'d4c18465',2688,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Solar energy\", \"Natural gas\"]','C'),(6804,'d4c18465',2689,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6805,'d4c18465',2690,'Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Melting ice\", \"Boiling water\", \"Burning wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6806,'d4c18465',2691,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6807,'d4c18465',2692,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6808,'d4c18465',2693,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Photosynthesis'),(6809,'d4c18465',2694,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'[]','Cohesion'),(6810,'d4c18465',2695,'The basic unit of heredity is _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Gene'),(6811,'d4c18465',2696,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Transpiration'),(6812,'d4c18465',2697,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Red'),(6813,'d4c18465',2698,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition, while a chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of a substance, resulting in the formation of new substances.'),(6814,'d4c18465',2699,'What is the function of the nervous system?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'[]','The nervous system controls and coordinates bodily functions, receiving and transmitting information through electrical and chemical signals.'),(6815,'d4c18465',2700,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to a change in its speed.'),(6816,'d4c18465',2701,'What are the three states of matter?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'[]','The three states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas.'),(6817,'d4c18465',2702,'Explain the concept of sustainable development.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','Sustainable development is development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.'),(6818,'d4c18465',2703,'Describe the process of digestion in humans, mentioning the different organs involved and their functions.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'[]','Digestion begins in the mouth with mechanical breakdown by chewing and chemical breakdown by saliva. The food then travels down the esophagus to the stomach, where it\'s churned and mixed with gastric juices. The partially digested food enters the small intestine, where most nutrient absorption occurs with the help of enzymes from the pancreas and bile from the liver. Finally, indigestible materials pass into the large intestine, where water is absorbed, before elimination.'),(6819,'d4c18465',2704,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'[]','The human heart is a muscular organ with four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood from the body and lungs, while the ventricles pump blood to the lungs and body. Valves ensure one-way blood flow. The heart\'s rhythmic contractions pump blood throughout the circulatory system, delivering oxygen and nutrients while removing waste products.'),(6820,'d4c18465',2705,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'[]','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce glucose (a sugar) and oxygen.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(6821,'d4c18465',2706,'Discuss the different types of pollution and their effects on the environment.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'[]','Pollution includes air, water, and soil pollution. Air pollution causes respiratory problems and acid rain. Water pollution contaminates drinking water and harms aquatic life. Soil pollution reduces fertility and can contaminate food chains.  The effects are widespread and harm human health and ecosystems.'),(6822,'d4c18465',2707,'Explain Ohm\'s law and its applications.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'[]','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Mathematically, V = IR, where V is voltage, I is current, and R is resistance.  Applications include circuit design, calculating power consumption, and understanding electrical behavior in various devices.'),(6823,'d4c18465',2708,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Newton\n2. Einstein\n3. Mendel\n4. Darwin\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Laws of Motion\nC. Theory of Evolution\nD. Laws of Inheritance','Matching','Medium',4,'[]','1-B, 2-A, 3-D, 4-C'),(6824,'d4c18465',2709,'A farmer noticed that his crops were not growing well.  He observed yellowing of leaves and stunted growth.  Soil testing revealed a deficiency of nitrogen. \n(a) Explain why nitrogen is essential for plant growth.\n(b) Suggest ways the farmer can improve the nitrogen content of his soil. \n(c) What are the environmental implications of excessive use of nitrogen fertilizers?','Case Study','Hard',5,'[]','(a) Nitrogen is a crucial component of chlorophyll, amino acids, and proteins, essential for plant growth and development. \n(b) The farmer can use nitrogen-rich fertilizers, crop rotation with nitrogen-fixing plants (legumes), or use organic manure to improve soil nitrogen. \n(c) Excessive nitrogen fertilizer use can lead to water pollution (eutrophication), air pollution (nitrous oxide emissions), and harm biodiversity.'),(6825,'f8484bab',2710,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6826,'f8484bab',2711,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6827,'f8484bab',2712,'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6828,'f8484bab',2713,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(6829,'f8484bab',2714,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6830,'f8484bab',2715,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Photosynthesis'),(6831,'f8484bab',2716,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Cohesion'),(6832,'f8484bab',2717,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','Gene'),(6833,'f8484bab',2718,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'[]','red'),(6834,'f8484bab',2719,'The process by which plants lose water vapor through their leaves is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'[]','Transpiration'),(6835,'f8484bab',2720,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but not its chemical composition, while a chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of a substance, forming new substances.'),(6836,'f8484bab',2721,'Define the terms \'refraction\' and \'reflection\' of light.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another. Reflection is the bouncing back of light when it strikes a surface.'),(6837,'f8484bab',2722,'What is the role of the ozone layer in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','The ozone layer absorbs most of the harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6838,'f8484bab',2723,'State two advantages of using solar energy.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'[]','Renewable and environmentally friendly.'),(6839,'f8484bab',2724,'Briefly explain the process of respiration.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'[]','Respiration is the process by which living organisms break down glucose to release energy.'),(6840,'f8484bab',2725,'Explain the process of photosynthesis in detail. Include the reactants, products, and the role of chlorophyll.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'[]','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  Chlorophyll is essential as it absorbs sunlight. The process converts light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The reactants are carbon dioxide and water, while the products are glucose and oxygen.  The overall equation is 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2.'),(6841,'f8484bab',2726,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'[]','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The atria receive blood from the body and lungs, while the ventricles pump blood to the body and lungs.  Valves ensure one-way blood flow.'),(6842,'f8484bab',2727,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'[]','Plants reproduce through asexual and sexual reproduction. Asexual reproduction involves a single parent and produces genetically identical offspring (e.g., vegetative propagation, budding). Sexual reproduction involves two parents and produces genetically diverse offspring through the fusion of gametes.'),(6843,'f8484bab',2728,'Discuss the different types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'[]','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each type.'),(6844,'f8484bab',2729,'Explain the concept of evolution and the evidence that supports it.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'[]','Evolution is the gradual change in the characteristics of a species over time. Evidence includes fossil records, comparative anatomy, embryology, molecular biology, and biogeography.'),(6845,'f8484bab',2730,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1. Newton\n2. Ohm\n3. Joule\n4. Watt\n\nColumn B\nA. Unit of Power\nB. Unit of Resistance\n C. Unit of Force\nD. Unit of Energy','Matching','Medium',4,'[]','1-C, 2-B, 3-D, 4-A'),(6846,'f8484bab',2731,'A student conducted an experiment to study the effect of different fertilizers on the growth of plants.  He used three types of fertilizers: A, B, and C.  He planted three similar plants in separate pots and used a different fertilizer for each plant.  After a month, he measured the height of each plant. Plant A grew to 10cm, Plant B grew to 15cm, and Plant C grew to 20cm.\n\n(a) Identify the dependent and independent variables in this experiment.\n(b) Which fertilizer was most effective?\n(c) Suggest two factors that could affect the results of this experiment besides the fertilizer used.\n(d) What could be done to improve the reliability of the experiment?','Case Study','Medium',5,'[]','(a) Dependent variable: Plant height; Independent variable: Type of fertilizer\n(b) Fertilizer C\n(c) Amount of sunlight, amount of water\n(d) Use more than one plant per fertilizer type; control other variables more carefully; repeat the experiment.'),(6847,'d2591809',2732,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6848,'d2591809',2733,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6849,'d2591809',2734,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(6850,'d2591809',2735,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(6851,'d2591809',2736,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6852,'d2591809',2737,'What is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fermentation\"]','B'),(6853,'d2591809',2738,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Cylindrical lens\", \"Biconvex lens\"]','B'),(6854,'d2591809',2739,'The basic unit of heredity is a ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','gene'),(6855,'d2591809',2740,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6856,'d2591809',2741,'The process of converting electrical energy into chemical energy is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','electrolysis'),(6857,'d2591809',2742,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','cohesion'),(6858,'d2591809',2743,'The process of a substance changing from liquid to gas is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','vaporization'),(6859,'d2591809',2744,'Define Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6860,'d2591809',2745,'What is the difference between speed and velocity?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Speed is the rate of change of distance, while velocity is the rate of change of displacement (includes direction).'),(6861,'d2591809',2746,'Explain the concept of inertia.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Inertia is the tendency of an object to resist changes in its state of motion.'),(6862,'d2591809',2747,'What are the two types of electric charges?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Positive and negative charges.'),(6863,'d2591809',2748,'Explain briefly the process of respiration in plants.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Plants take in oxygen and release carbon dioxide during respiration, releasing energy from glucose.'),(6864,'d2591809',2749,'Explain the process of photosynthesis in detail, including the factors affecting it.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll.  It involves the conversion of light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. The process takes place in chloroplasts and requires carbon dioxide, water, and sunlight.  The factors affecting photosynthesis include light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, temperature, and water availability.  Higher light intensity, CO2 concentration, and optimal temperature generally increase the rate of photosynthesis, up to a saturation point. Water shortage can limit the rate significantly.'),(6865,'d2591809',2750,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood from the body and the lungs, and the ventricles pump blood to the body and the lungs. The heart\'s structure includes valves that prevent backflow of blood.  The heart functions by a rhythmic contraction and relaxation of its muscles, creating a continuous circulatory system.'),(6866,'d2591809',2751,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Plants reproduce through both asexual and sexual methods. Asexual reproduction involves the production of offspring from a single parent without the fusion of gametes.  Examples include vegetative propagation (e.g., potato tubers, onion bulbs), budding (e.g., yeast), and fragmentation (e.g., spirogyra). Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of male and female gametes, resulting in genetically diverse offspring.  Examples include pollination and fertilization in flowering plants, and the production of spores in non-flowering plants.'),(6867,'d2591809',2752,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Chemical reactions can be classified into several types: combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, neutralization, and redox reactions. Combination reactions involve the combining of two or more substances to form a single product (e.g., formation of water from hydrogen and oxygen). Decomposition reactions involve the breakdown of a compound into simpler substances (e.g., decomposition of calcium carbonate). Displacement reactions involve the replacement of one element by another in a compound (e.g., reaction of zinc with hydrochloric acid). Double displacement reactions involve the exchange of ions between two compounds (e.g., reaction of silver nitrate with sodium chloride). Neutralization reactions involve the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water. Redox reactions involve the transfer of electrons between reactants (e.g., rusting of iron).'),(6868,'d2591809',2753,'Explain the structure and working of the human eye, including common defects of vision and their correction.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human eye is a complex organ responsible for vision. It consists of various parts like cornea, lens, iris, pupil, retina, optic nerve etc. Light enters the eye through the cornea and is focused by the lens onto the retina, which contains photoreceptor cells (rods and cones). These cells convert light into nerve impulses that are transmitted to the brain via the optic nerve. Common defects of vision include myopia (nearsightedness), hypermetropia (farsightedness), and astigmatism.  Myopia is corrected using concave lenses, hypermetropia using convex lenses, and astigmatism using cylindrical lenses.'),(6869,'d2591809',2754,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Transpiration\n4.  Osmosis\n\nColumn B\nA.  Movement of water across a semipermeable membrane\nB.  Release of water vapor from leaves\nC.  Conversion of light energy to chemical energy\nD.  Release of energy from glucose','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-B, 4-A'),(6870,'d2591809',2755,'A student is conducting an experiment to study the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction.  They mix two chemicals at different temperatures and observe the time it takes for a color change to occur. At 25°C, the color change happens in 10 seconds. At 35°C, it happens in 5 seconds. At 45°C, it happens in 2 seconds.\n\n(a) What is the independent variable in this experiment?\n(b) What is the dependent variable?\n(c) What conclusion can the student draw from the results?\n(d) Suggest one way to improve the accuracy of the experiment.','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','(a) Temperature\n(b) Time taken for color change\n(c) The rate of reaction increases with increasing temperature.\n(d) Repeat the experiment multiple times at each temperature and calculate the average time.'),(6871,'1ff596e0',2756,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6872,'1ff596e0',2757,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6873,'1ff596e0',2758,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6874,'1ff596e0',2759,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6875,'1ff596e0',2760,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6876,'1ff596e0',2761,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6877,'1ff596e0',2762,'The SI unit of force is the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6878,'1ff596e0',2763,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6879,'1ff596e0',2764,'The process by which plants lose water vapor through their leaves is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6880,'1ff596e0',2765,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(6881,'1ff596e0',2766,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change is a change in the form or appearance of a substance, without changing its chemical composition.  A chemical change involves the formation of new substances with different properties.'),(6882,'1ff596e0',2767,'State Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.'),(6883,'1ff596e0',2768,'What are the different types of asexual reproduction?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Examples include binary fission, budding, vegetative propagation, spore formation etc.'),(6884,'1ff596e0',2769,'Explain the process of reflex action.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A reflex action is an involuntary and rapid response to a stimulus. It involves a receptor, sensory neuron, relay neuron in the spinal cord, motor neuron, and effector.'),(6885,'1ff596e0',2770,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The respiratory system consists of the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, bronchioles, and alveoli. It facilitates gas exchange (intake of oxygen and expulsion of carbon dioxide).'),(6886,'1ff596e0',2771,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  Include the balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy → C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(6887,'1ff596e0',2772,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, redox etc.  Examples should be given for each.'),(6888,'1ff596e0',2773,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers (two atria and two ventricles) and valves to regulate blood flow.'),(6889,'1ff596e0',2774,'Explain the Mendelian laws of inheritance. Give examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Mendelian laws of inheritance include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment.  Explain each law with a suitable example.'),(6890,'1ff596e0',2775,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1. Sodium\n2. Chlorine\n3. Oxygen\n4. Hydrogen\n\nColumn B\nA. Gas in the air\nB. Reactive metal\nC. Halogen\nD. Lightest element','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-C, 3-A, 4-D'),(6891,'1ff596e0',2776,'A student observes that a plant kept in a dark room for several days wilts and eventually dies.  Explain why this happens using your knowledge of photosynthesis and respiration.','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','In the absence of light, the plant cannot carry out photosynthesis to produce glucose (its food source).  It continues to respire, using up stored glucose. Eventually, it runs out of energy and dies.'),(6892,'a29def9b',2777,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6893,'a29def9b',2778,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6894,'a29def9b',2779,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Hydro energy\", \"Nuclear energy\"]','D'),(6895,'a29def9b',2780,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6896,'a29def9b',2781,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6897,'a29def9b',2782,'What is the process by which plants make their food?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Excretion\"]','B'),(6898,'a29def9b',2783,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Zero\", \"Infinity\", \"One meter\", \"Half a meter\"]','B'),(6899,'a29def9b',2784,'The SI unit of force is ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(6900,'a29def9b',2785,'The process of converting light energy into electrical energy is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photovoltaic effect/Solar energy conversion'),(6901,'a29def9b',2786,'Acids turn blue litmus paper ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6902,'a29def9b',2787,'The basic unit of heredity is ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(6903,'a29def9b',2788,'The process of separating different components of a mixture is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','separation/separation technique'),(6904,'a29def9b',2789,'The process by which plants lose water in the form of vapor is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','transpiration'),(6905,'a29def9b',2790,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.'),(6906,'a29def9b',2791,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but not its chemical composition. A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties.'),(6907,'a29def9b',2792,'What are the components of blood?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Blood consists of plasma, red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets.'),(6908,'a29def9b',2793,'State Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6909,'a29def9b',2794,'What is the role of ozone layer in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The ozone layer absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6910,'a29def9b',2795,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves the intake of air into the lungs, exchange of gases between the lungs and blood, and transportation of oxygen to body cells.'),(6911,'a29def9b',2796,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart. Draw a neat diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood, while the ventricles pump blood out. The heart valves ensure unidirectional blood flow. (Diagram should show the four chambers, valves, and major blood vessels).'),(6912,'a29def9b',2797,'Explain the process of photosynthesis. Write a balanced chemical equation for photosynthesis.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It involves the absorption of sunlight by chlorophyll, the conversion of carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Sunlight → C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(6913,'a29def9b',2798,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Plants reproduce through both asexual and sexual reproduction. Asexual reproduction involves the production of new plants from a single parent, such as through vegetative propagation (e.g., budding, runners, tubers). Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of male and female gametes, leading to the formation of seeds.'),(6914,'a29def9b',2799,'Describe the different types of lenses and their uses.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex and concave. Convex lenses are thicker in the middle and converge light rays, used in magnifying glasses, cameras, and eyeglasses for farsightedness. Concave lenses are thinner in the middle and diverge light rays, used in eyeglasses for nearsightedness and telescopes.'),(6915,'a29def9b',2800,'Explain the concept of electric current and potential difference. Define Ohm\'s law and state its limitations.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Electric current is the flow of electric charge. Potential difference is the work done per unit charge in moving a charge between two points. Ohm\'s law states that the current through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Limitations: Ohm\'s law is not applicable to all materials (e.g., non-ohmic conductors) and it does not hold true at very high or very low temperatures.'),(6916,'a29def9b',2801,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1. Acid rain\n2. Global warming\n3. Ozone depletion\n4. Deforestation\n\nColumn B\nA. Increase in Earth\'s average temperature\nB. Loss of forest cover\nC. Damage to ozone layer\nD. Acidic precipitation','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-A, 3-C, 4-B'),(6917,'a29def9b',2802,'A student conducted an experiment to study the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction. They mixed two solutions, A and B, at different temperatures and measured the time taken for the reaction to complete. The results are shown below:\n\nTemperature (°C): 20, 30, 40\nTime taken (seconds): 120, 60, 30\n\n(a) What is the relationship between temperature and rate of reaction? Explain your answer.\n(b) What is the likely type of reaction being studied?\n(c) Suggest two ways to further improve the accuracy of the experiment.','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) As the temperature increases, the rate of reaction increases. This is because higher temperatures provide more kinetic energy to the reacting molecules, increasing the frequency of successful collisions. \n(b) It is likely an exothermic reaction, as the rate increases with temperature. \n(c)  Maintain a constant volume of solution A and B; Use a thermostat to control the temperature more precisely.'),(6918,'79165a48',2803,'Which of the following is NOT a component of air?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Nitrogen\", \"Oxygen\", \"Carbon Dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','D'),(6919,'79165a48',2804,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6920,'79165a48',2805,'Which of these is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\"]','D'),(6921,'79165a48',2806,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6922,'79165a48',2807,'Which acid is present in lemon juice?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Hydrochloric Acid\", \"Sulphuric Acid\", \"Nitric Acid\", \"Citric Acid\"]','D'),(6923,'79165a48',2808,'The process by which plants make their own food is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6924,'79165a48',2809,'The smallest particle of an element is called an _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Atom'),(6925,'79165a48',2810,'The force of attraction between the earth and an object is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravity'),(6926,'79165a48',2811,'The unit of power is the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Watt'),(6927,'79165a48',2812,'What is the difference between a physical change and a chemical change?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s physical properties are altered, but its chemical composition remains the same.  A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of the substance, forming a new substance with different properties.'),(6928,'79165a48',2813,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide.  It involves the intake of air into the lungs, where oxygen diffuses into the bloodstream and carbon dioxide diffuses out.  The oxygen is then transported to cells where it is used in cellular respiration to release energy.'),(6929,'79165a48',2814,'State Newton\'s third law of motion.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6930,'79165a48',2815,'What are the different types of blood groups?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The main blood groups are A, B, AB, and O.  Each group can also be Rh positive or Rh negative.'),(6931,'79165a48',2816,'Define the term \'refraction of light\'.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Refraction of light is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to a change in its speed.'),(6932,'79165a48',2817,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It is divided into four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The atria receive blood from the body and lungs, while the ventricles pump blood to the body and lungs.  The heart\'s structure ensures unidirectional blood flow. Valves prevent backflow of blood. The heart\'s function is to maintain blood circulation, transporting oxygen, nutrients, and hormones throughout the body and removing waste products.'),(6933,'79165a48',2818,'Explain the process of photosynthesis with a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce glucose and oxygen. The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + sunlight  ---> C6H12O6 + 6O2.  The process takes place in chloroplasts, using chlorophyll to capture light energy.'),(6934,'79165a48',2819,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Several types of chemical reactions exist, including combination (synthesis), decomposition, single displacement, double displacement, and combustion reactions.  Combination reactions involve combining two or more substances to form a new one (e.g., 2H2 + O2 → 2H2O). Decomposition reactions break down a substance into simpler ones (e.g., 2H2O → 2H2 + O2). Single displacement reactions involve one element replacing another in a compound (e.g., Zn + 2HCl → ZnCl2 + H2). Double displacement reactions involve the exchange of ions between two compounds (e.g., AgNO3 + NaCl → AgCl + NaNO3). Combustion reactions involve rapid oxidation, producing heat and light (e.g., CH4 + 2O2 → CO2 + 2H2O).'),(6935,'79165a48',2820,'Describe the structure and functions of the nervous system.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The nervous system is composed of the central nervous system (brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system (nerves extending from the CNS).  The brain controls various bodily functions and processes information from the senses.  The spinal cord relays information between the brain and the rest of the body.  The peripheral nervous system carries signals to and from the CNS. Neurons, specialized cells, transmit information through electrical and chemical signals.  Functions include sensory perception, motor control, and coordination of bodily activities.'),(6936,'79165a48',2821,'Match the following scientists with their contributions:\n\nColumn A\n1. Gregor Mendel\n2. Louis Pasteur\n3. Isaac Newton\n4. Albert Einstein\n\nColumn B\nA. Theory of Relativity\nB. Laws of Motion and Universal Gravitation\nC. Germ Theory of Disease\nD. Principles of Inheritance','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-D, 2-C, 3-B, 4-A'),(6937,'79165a48',2822,'A student is conducting an experiment to investigate the effect of different liquids on the rate of rusting of iron nails.  He uses four test tubes, each containing an iron nail submerged in a different liquid: distilled water, salt water, vinegar, and oil. After a week, he observes that the nail in the salt water is the most rusted, followed by the vinegar, then the distilled water. The nail in the oil shows no signs of rust. \n(a) Explain why the nail in salt water rusted the most.\n(b)  What is rust and how is it formed?','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','(a) Salt water is an electrolyte, which means it conducts electricity. The presence of ions in salt water accelerates the electrochemical reaction that leads to rust formation. \n(b) Rust is iron oxide, formed when iron reacts with oxygen in the presence of water or moisture. This is an example of oxidation.'),(6938,'79165a48',2823,'A farmer notices that his crops are not growing well. He observes that the soil is dry and lacks essential nutrients. He decides to use fertilizers to improve soil fertility. \n(a) Explain how fertilizers help improve crop growth.\n(b) What are some potential negative consequences of using excessive amounts of fertilizers?','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','(a) Fertilizers provide essential nutrients like nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium that are needed for plant growth.  They improve soil fertility, making it richer in nutrients. \n(b) Excessive fertilizer use can lead to water pollution (eutrophication), soil degradation (salinization), and harm beneficial soil organisms.  It can also affect human health.'),(6939,'53484b07',2824,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6940,'53484b07',2825,'The SI unit of force is:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Newton\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','B'),(6941,'53484b07',2826,'What is the chemical formula of water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"H2O2\", \"H2O\", \"O2\", \"CO2\"]','B'),(6942,'53484b07',2827,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6943,'53484b07',2828,'What is the process by which plants make their food?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fermentation\"]','B'),(6944,'53484b07',2829,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"0 cm\", \"Infinity\", \"10 cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(6945,'53484b07',2830,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Nuclear energy\", \"Hydroelectric energy\"]','C'),(6946,'53484b07',2831,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6947,'53484b07',2832,'The unit of electric current is the _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Ampere'),(6948,'53484b07',2833,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(6949,'53484b07',2834,'The force of attraction between the earth and an object is called _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravity'),(6950,'53484b07',2835,'The basic unit of heredity is _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(6951,'53484b07',2836,'The process of separating different components of a mixture based on their boiling points is called _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Distillation'),(6952,'53484b07',2837,'Define the term \'refraction\'.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another.'),(6953,'53484b07',2838,'What is the difference between speed and velocity?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Speed is the rate of change of distance, while velocity is the rate of change of displacement (it includes direction).'),(6954,'53484b07',2839,'Explain the process of neutralization.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Neutralization is a chemical reaction between an acid and a base, producing salt and water.'),(6955,'53484b07',2840,'What are the three states of matter?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Solid, liquid, and gas.'),(6956,'53484b07',2841,'What is the role of ozone in the atmosphere?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Ozone in the stratosphere absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun, protecting life on Earth.'),(6957,'53484b07',2842,'Explain the difference between renewable and non-renewable resources.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Renewable resources can be replenished naturally, while non-renewable resources are finite and cannot be easily replenished.'),(6958,'53484b07',2843,'Explain the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','The human respiratory system consists of the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and lungs. It facilitates the intake of oxygen and the expulsion of carbon dioxide.'),(6959,'53484b07',2844,'Describe the process of photosynthesis.  Include a balanced chemical equation.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.  The balanced chemical equation is: 6CO2 + 6H2O + Light Energy -> C6H12O6 + 6O2'),(6960,'53484b07',2845,'Explain Newton\'s three laws of motion with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Newton\'s three laws of motion are: 1. Inertia: An object at rest stays at rest and an object in motion stays in motion unless acted upon by an unbalanced force. 2. F=ma: The acceleration of an object is directly proportional to the net force acting on it and inversely proportional to its mass. 3. Action-reaction: For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.'),(6961,'53484b07',2846,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Plants reproduce through sexual and asexual reproduction. Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of gametes, while asexual reproduction involves a single parent producing offspring through various methods like vegetative propagation, budding, etc.'),(6962,'53484b07',2847,'Explain the importance of biodiversity and the threats it faces.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Biodiversity refers to the variety of life on Earth at all its levels, from genes to ecosystems. It is crucial for ecosystem services, food security, and human well-being. Threats include habitat loss, climate change, pollution, and invasive species.'),(6963,'53484b07',2848,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Hydrochloric acid\n2.  Sodium hydroxide\n3.  Carbon dioxide\n4.  Oxygen\n\nColumn B\nA.  Base\nB.  Acid\nC.  Greenhouse gas\nD.  Respiratory gas','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-B, 2-A, 3-C, 4-D'),(6964,'53484b07',2849,'A student performs an experiment to investigate the effect of different liquids on the growth of plants. He uses three identical plants and waters them with different liquids: distilled water, salt water, and sugar water. After a week, he observes that the plant watered with distilled water is healthy, the plant watered with salt water is wilting, and the plant watered with sugar water shows moderate growth. \n\n(a)  Explain the results of the experiment.\n(b)  What is the control group in this experiment? \n(c)  What can be concluded about the effect of salt and sugar on plant growth?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) The plant watered with distilled water thrived because it received the necessary nutrients. The plant watered with salt water wilted due to osmosis. The plant watered with sugar water showed moderate growth as sugar provides some energy but not all the essential nutrients. (b) The plant watered with distilled water is the control group. (c) Excess salt can harm plant growth due to osmotic imbalance, while moderate sugar can provide some energy but is not sufficient for optimal growth.'),(6965,'53484b07',1831,'The unit of power is _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Watt'),(6966,'aeb2fd9e',2850,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(6967,'aeb2fd9e',2851,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(6968,'aeb2fd9e',2852,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6969,'aeb2fd9e',2853,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6970,'aeb2fd9e',2854,'Which organelle is responsible for photosynthesis in plants?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Mitochondria\", \"Chloroplast\", \"Vacuole\", \"Nucleus\"]','B'),(6971,'aeb2fd9e',2855,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(6972,'aeb2fd9e',2856,'The force of attraction between molecules of the same substance is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Cohesion'),(6973,'aeb2fd9e',2857,'The smallest unit of an element that can exist independently is called an _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Atom'),(6974,'aeb2fd9e',2858,'The process by which plants lose water through stomata is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Transpiration'),(6975,'aeb2fd9e',2859,'The functional unit of the kidney is called a _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Nephron'),(6976,'aeb2fd9e',2860,'The type of reaction where heat is absorbed is called an _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Endothermic reaction'),(6977,'aeb2fd9e',2861,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but does not change its chemical composition. A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of a substance, resulting in the formation of a new substance.'),(6978,'aeb2fd9e',2862,'State Ohm\'s law.  Give its mathematical representation.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature remains constant.  Mathematical representation: V = IR'),(6979,'aeb2fd9e',2863,'Briefly describe the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves the intake of air into the lungs, exchange of gases between the lungs and blood, and the transport of oxygen to the body\'s cells.  Carbon dioxide is then transported back to the lungs to be expelled.'),(6980,'aeb2fd9e',2864,'Explain the role of decomposers in an ecosystem.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Decomposers break down dead organisms and organic waste, releasing nutrients back into the environment. This makes the nutrients available for plants and other organisms.'),(6981,'aeb2fd9e',2865,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The atria receive blood from the body and the lungs, while the ventricles pump blood to the body and the lungs. The heart\'s valves ensure that blood flows in one direction. The heart\'s rhythmic contractions maintain blood flow and deliver oxygen and nutrients to the body\'s tissues.'),(6982,'aeb2fd9e',2866,'Describe the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. It involves the absorption of light energy by chlorophyll, the conversion of light energy into chemical energy, and the formation of glucose. Photosynthesis is crucial for producing food for plants and other organisms and for maintaining atmospheric oxygen levels.'),(6983,'aeb2fd9e',2867,'Explain the different types of reproduction in plants.  Give examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Plants reproduce both sexually and asexually. Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of gametes (sperm and egg) to produce seeds.  Asexual reproduction involves the production of new plants from a single parent plant, without the fusion of gametes. Examples of asexual reproduction include vegetative propagation (e.g., runners, bulbs, tubers), budding, and fragmentation. Examples of sexual reproduction include pollination and seed formation.'),(6984,'aeb2fd9e',2868,'Discuss the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination reactions (e.g., formation of water from hydrogen and oxygen), decomposition reactions (e.g., breakdown of calcium carbonate into calcium oxide and carbon dioxide), displacement reactions (e.g., iron reacting with copper sulfate), double displacement reactions (e.g., reaction between sodium chloride and silver nitrate), neutralization reactions (e.g., reaction between an acid and a base), redox reactions (e.g., rusting of iron), and combustion reactions (e.g., burning of methane).'),(6985,'aeb2fd9e',2869,'Explain the process of evolution by natural selection.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Natural selection is a process where organisms with traits better suited to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on those advantageous traits to their offspring.  Over time, this leads to the evolution of species.'),(6986,'aeb2fd9e',2870,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Newton\'s First Law\n2.  Newton\'s Second Law\n3.  Newton\'s Third Law\n4.  Inertia\n5.  Acceleration\n\nColumn B\nA.  For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.\nB.  The rate of change of velocity\nC.  An object at rest stays at rest, and an object in motion stays in motion unless acted upon by an unbalanced force.\nD.  Resistance to change in motion\nE.  Force equals mass times acceleration (F=ma)','Matching','Medium',5,'null','1-C, 2-E, 3-A, 4-D, 5-B'),(6987,'aeb2fd9e',2871,'A student is conducting an experiment to investigate the effect of temperature on the rate of a chemical reaction. They mix two reactants at different temperatures and observe the time it takes for the reaction to complete.  At 25°C, the reaction takes 10 minutes. At 35°C, the reaction takes 5 minutes. At 45°C, the reaction takes 2.5 minutes.\n\n(a) What is the relationship between temperature and reaction rate?\n(b) Explain why this relationship exists.\n(c) What is the independent variable in this experiment?\n(d) What is the dependent variable?\n(e)  Suggest one way to improve the accuracy of the experiment.','Case Study','Medium',5,'null','(a) As temperature increases, the rate of reaction increases.\n(b) Higher temperatures increase the kinetic energy of the reactant molecules, leading to more frequent and energetic collisions, increasing the probability of successful reactions.\n(c) Temperature\n(d) Reaction time\n(e) Repeat the experiment multiple times at each temperature and calculate the average reaction time.'),(6988,'aeb2fd9e',2872,'A farmer notices that his crops are not growing well. He suspects a nutrient deficiency.  He conducts soil tests and finds that the soil is low in nitrogen. \n\n(a) What are the functions of nitrogen in plants?\n(b) What are the symptoms of nitrogen deficiency in plants?\n(c) Suggest a way the farmer can increase the nitrogen content in his soil.\n(d) What are some other important nutrients needed by plants?\n(e)  Why is soil testing important for farmers?','Case Study','Medium',5,'null','(a) Nitrogen is essential for the synthesis of proteins and chlorophyll.\n(b) Symptoms of nitrogen deficiency include stunted growth, yellowing of leaves (chlorosis), and reduced yield.\n(c) The farmer can use nitrogen fertilizers or plant nitrogen-fixing crops (legumes).\n(d) Phosphorus, potassium, magnesium, calcium, sulfur, etc.\n(e) Soil testing helps farmers determine nutrient deficiencies and adjust their farming practices accordingly, improving crop yields and soil health.'),(6989,'aeb2fd9e',2873,'A group of students are investigating the properties of different types of rocks. They observe that one rock is easily scratched by a fingernail, another is harder, and a third rock is very hard and cannot be scratched by a steel knife.  \n\n(a) What property of rocks are the students investigating?\n(b) Explain the difference in hardness between the three rocks.\n(c) Name one rock type that is relatively soft and one that is very hard.\n(d) What is the Mohs hardness scale?\n(e) How is the hardness of a rock related to its composition and formation?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Hardness\n(b) The difference in hardness reflects the different minerals present in the rocks and the strength of their chemical bonds.  Softer rocks may contain softer minerals while harder rocks may contain minerals like quartz or diamond.\n(c) Soft: Talc. Hard: Diamond\n(d) The Mohs hardness scale is a numerical scale used to describe the relative hardness of minerals.\n(e) Hardness is related to the type of mineral, their crystal structure, and the conditions under which they formed.'),(6990,'aeb2fd9e',2874,'A scientist is studying the effect of pollution on a local lake. They observe that the water is cloudy, has a high level of algae, and many fish are dead. \n\n(a) What type of water pollution is likely causing these problems?\n(b) Explain how this type of pollution affects the lake\'s ecosystem.\n(c) What are the sources of this type of pollution?\n(d) Suggest some solutions to reduce this type of pollution.\n(e) How can we monitor the health of a lake?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Eutrophication (Nutrient pollution)\n(b) Excess nutrients cause algal blooms, which reduce oxygen levels in the water (hypoxia), leading to fish kills and harming other aquatic life.\n(c) Sources include agricultural runoff (fertilizers), sewage, and industrial discharge.\n(d) Solutions include reducing fertilizer use, improving sewage treatment, and implementing stricter regulations on industrial discharge.\n(e) We can monitor water quality parameters such as oxygen levels, nutrient levels, and the presence of pollutants.'),(6991,'aeb2fd9e',2875,'A doctor observes that a patient has a high fever, fatigue, and a persistent cough. The patient recently traveled to a region known for the Zika virus.\n\n(a) What disease might the patient have?\n(b) How is this disease transmitted?\n(c) What are the symptoms of this disease?\n(d) What are the preventative measures for this disease?\n(e) How is this disease diagnosed?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) Zika Virus Infection\n(b) Zika virus is primarily transmitted through the bite of infected Aedes mosquitoes.\n(c) Symptoms can include fever, rash, joint pain, conjunctivitis, muscle pain, and headache.  Many people infected with the Zika virus do not develop any symptoms.\n(d) Preventative measures include using mosquito repellents, wearing protective clothing, and using mosquito nets.\n(e) Zika virus is usually diagnosed through blood tests.'),(6992,'e08015ee',2876,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Burning of wood\", \"Dissolving salt in water\"]','C'),(6993,'e08015ee',2877,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Newton\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','B'),(6994,'e08015ee',2878,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(6995,'e08015ee',2879,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(6996,'e08015ee',2880,'Which type of mirror is used in a car\'s rearview mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Plane mirror\", \"Concave mirror\", \"Convex mirror\", \"None of the above\"]','C'),(6997,'e08015ee',2881,'What is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fermentation\"]','B'),(6998,'e08015ee',2882,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Oil\", \"Natural gas\", \"Solar energy\"]','D'),(6999,'e08015ee',2883,'What is the function of the human heart?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"To digest food\", \"To filter blood\", \"To pump blood\", \"To control breathing\"]','C'),(7000,'e08015ee',2884,'What is the name of the force that pulls objects towards the center of the Earth?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Friction\", \"Gravity\", \"Tension\", \"Pressure\"]','B'),(7001,'e08015ee',2885,'What is the pH of pure water?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"0\", \"7\", \"14\", \"10\"]','B'),(7002,'e08015ee',2886,'Which scientist formulated the laws of motion?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Albert Einstein\", \"Isaac Newton\", \"Galileo Galilei\", \"Archimedes\"]','B'),(7003,'e08015ee',2887,'What is the process of converting a gas directly into a solid called?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Melting\", \"Freezing\", \"Sublimation\", \"Deposition\"]','D'),(7004,'e08015ee',2888,'Which element is most abundant in the Earth\'s crust?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Iron\", \"Oxygen\", \"Silicon\", \"Aluminum\"]','B'),(7005,'e08015ee',2889,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(7006,'e08015ee',2890,'What is the name of the process by which plants lose water vapor?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Photosynthesis\", \"Respiration\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fertilization\"]','C'),(7007,'e08015ee',2891,'Which type of lens converges light rays?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Concave lens\", \"Convex lens\", \"Plane lens\", \"None of the above\"]','B'),(7008,'e08015ee',2892,'What is the speed of light in a vacuum?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"3 x 10^5 m/s\", \"3 x 10^7 m/s\", \"3 x 10^8 m/s\", \"3 x 10^9 m/s\"]','C'),(7009,'e08015ee',2893,'What is the name of the positively charged particle in an atom?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Electron\", \"Neutron\", \"Proton\", \"Ion\"]','C'),(7010,'e08015ee',2894,'Which of the following is a semiconductor?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"Copper\", \"Silicon\", \"Iron\", \"Gold\"]','B'),(7011,'e08015ee',2895,'What is the name of the process by which cells divide to produce two identical daughter cells?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Meiosis\", \"Mitosis\", \"Fertilization\", \"Differentiation\"]','B'),(7012,'348c9f1d',2896,'Which of the following is a good conductor of electricity?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Wood\", \"Rubber\", \"Copper\", \"Plastic\"]','C'),(7013,'348c9f1d',2897,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(7014,'348c9f1d',2898,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable resource?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Coal\", \"Hydropower\"]','C'),(7015,'348c9f1d',2899,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Watt\", \"Ohm\"]','B'),(7016,'348c9f1d',2900,'What process converts light energy into chemical energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Respiration\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Transpiration\", \"Fermentation\"]','B'),(7017,'348c9f1d',2901,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(7018,'348c9f1d',2902,'What is the name of the force that keeps planets in orbit around the sun?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Friction\", \"Gravity\", \"Electromagnetism\", \"Nuclear force\"]','B'),(7019,'348c9f1d',2903,'Which type of lens is used to correct nearsightedness?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Cylindrical lens\", \"Plano-convex lens\"]','B'),(7020,'348c9f1d',2904,'What is the pH of a neutral solution?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"0\", \"7\", \"14\", \"10\"]','B'),(7021,'348c9f1d',2905,'Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting ice\", \"Boiling water\", \"Burning wood\", \"Crushing a can\"]','C'),(7022,'3e43e24a',2906,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा पदार्थ एक यौगिक है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हीलियम\"]','C'),(7023,'3e43e24a',2907,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया किस अंग में होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जड़\", \"तना\", \"पत्तियाँ\", \"फूल\"]','C'),(7024,'3e43e24a',2908,'बल का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"जूल\", \"वाट\", \"न्यूटन\", \"पास्कल\"]','C'),(7025,'3e43e24a',2909,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"पानी का उबलना\", \"कागज़ का जलना\", \"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"लोहे का पिघलना\"]','B'),(7026,'3e43e24a',2910,'ध्वनि की गति अधिकतम होती है:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"वायु में\", \"जल में\", \"इस्पात में\", \"निर्वात में\"]','C'),(7027,'3e43e24a',2911,'मानव शरीर में सबसे बड़ी ग्रंथि कौन सी है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"हृदय\", \"फेफड़े\", \"यकृत\", \"मस्तिष्क\"]','C'),(7028,'3e43e24a',2912,'जैव निम्नीकरणीय और अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थों में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','जैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे होते हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से सूक्ष्मजीवों द्वारा अपघटित हो जाते हैं, जबकि अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ प्राकृतिक रूप से अपघटित नहीं होते हैं।'),(7029,'3e43e24a',2913,'बल की परिभाषा दीजिये और इसके मात्रक लिखिए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','बल वह कारक है जो किसी वस्तु की गति की अवस्था में परिवर्तन करता है या करने का प्रयास करता है। इसका SI मात्रक न्यूटन है।'),(7030,'3e43e24a',2914,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण क्या है? संक्षेप में समझाइए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण वह प्रक्रिया है जिसमें हरे पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश की उपस्थिति में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड और जल से अपना भोजन बनाते हैं।'),(7031,'3e43e24a',2915,'दाब क्या है? इसके मात्रक लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','दाब प्रति इकाई क्षेत्रफल पर लगने वाले बल को कहते हैं। इसका SI मात्रक पास्कल है।'),(7032,'3e43e24a',2916,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र बनाइए और इसके विभिन्न अंगों के कार्यों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र और विभिन्न अंगों (मुख, ग्रासनली, आमाशय, छोटी आंत, बड़ी आंत, मलाशय, गुदा) के कार्यों का वर्णन।'),(7033,'3e43e24a',2917,'न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों को समझाइए और उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों का विस्तृत वर्णन और प्रत्येक नियम के उदाहरण।'),(7034,'3e43e24a',2918,'ध्वनि क्या है? ध्वनि के उत्पन्न होने, संचरण और परावर्तन की व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','ध्वनि की परिभाषा, उत्पन्न होने की प्रक्रिया, संचरण के माध्यम और परावर्तन की व्याख्या।'),(7035,'3e43e24a',2919,'अम्ल, क्षार और लवण में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए। उदाहरण दीजिये।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','अम्ल, क्षार और लवण की परिभाषा, उनके गुणों में अंतर और उदाहरण।'),(7036,'3e43e24a',2920,'कोई भी पाँच रासायनिक अभिक्रियाएँ लिखिए और उनके प्रकार लिखिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','पाँच रासायनिक अभिक्रियाओं के समीकरण और उनके प्रकार (संयोजन, वियोजन, विस्थापन, द्विविस्थापन, अपघटन)।'),(7037,'3e43e24a',2921,'एक छात्र ने एक प्रयोग किया जिसमें उसने एक पेड़ की पत्तियों पर आयोडीन घोल डाला। पत्तियाँ नीली-काली हो गईं।\n(a) इस प्रयोग से क्या निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है?\n(b) पत्तियों में नीली-काली रंग क्यों आया?\n(c) आयोडीन घोल का प्रयोग क्यों किया गया?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) पत्तियों में स्टार्च उपस्थित है।\n(b) आयोडीन स्टार्च के साथ अभिक्रिया करके नीला-काला रंग देता है।\n(c) आयोडीन स्टार्च का पता लगाने के लिए प्रयोग किया जाता है।'),(7038,'3e43e24a',2676,'The force of attraction between any two objects having mass is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(7039,'3e43e24a',2675,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(7040,'3e43e24a',2677,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(7041,'3e43e24a',2678,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(7042,'3e43e24a',2686,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Chlorophyll\n2.  Stomata\n3.  Xylem\n4.  Phloem\n\nColumn B\nA.  Transport of water\nB.  Transport of food\nC.  Green pigment\nD.  Tiny pores on leaves','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(7043,'d00f3b8b',2922,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा पदार्थ एक अम्ल है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"सोडियम हाइड्रॉक्साइड\", \"पोटेशियम हाइड्रॉक्साइड\", \"हाइड्रोक्लोरिक अम्ल\", \"अमोनिया\"]','C'),(7044,'d00f3b8b',2923,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण के दौरान पौधे किस गैस का उपयोग करते हैं?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"हाइड्रोजन\