b) पौधे प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया द्वारा अपना भोजन बनाते हैं, जिसके लिए प्रकाश आवश्यक है।'),(7366,'f5a4f0e1',3223,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सी धातु कमरे के तापमान पर द्रव अवस्था में पाई जाती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"लोहा\", \"पारा\", \"सोना\", \"चाँदी\"]','B'),(7367,'f5a4f0e1',3224,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया में पौधे किस गैस का उपयोग करते हैं?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हाइड्रोजन\"]','C'),(7368,'f5a4f0e1',3225,'बल का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जूल\", \"वाट\", \"न्यूटन\", \"पास्कल\"]','C'),(7369,'f5a4f0e1',3226,'अम्लीय वर्षा का मुख्य कारण क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"ओजोन\", \"सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड\", \"नाइट्रोजन\"]','C'),(7370,'f5a4f0e1',3227,'कौन सा कोशिकांग पादप कोशिका में पाया जाता है, परंतु जंतु कोशिका में नहीं?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"माइटोकॉन्ड्रिया\", \"राइबोसोम\", \"हरितलवक\", \"गॉल्जीकाय\"]','C'),(7371,'f5a4f0e1',3228,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"पानी का उबलना\", \"कागज का जलना\", \"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"लोहे का पिघलना\"]','B'),(7372,'f5a4f0e1',3229,'जैव निम्नीकरणीय और अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थों में अंतर स्पष्ट करें।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','जैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे पदार्थ होते हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से सूक्ष्मजीवों द्वारा विघटित हो जाते हैं, जबकि अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे पदार्थ होते हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से विघटित नहीं होते हैं।'),(7373,'f5a4f0e1',3230,'बल क्या है? इसके मात्रक लिखिए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','बल वह कारक है जो किसी वस्तु की गति की अवस्था में परिवर्तन करता है या उसे परिवर्तित करने का प्रयास करता है। इसका SI मात्रक न्यूटन है।'),(7374,'f5a4f0e1',3231,'ज्वालामुखी से निकलने वाले पदार्थों का वर्णन करें।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','ज्वालामुखी से लावा, राख, गैसें, और भाप निकलती हैं।'),(7375,'f5a4f0e1',3232,'किसी पदार्थ के घनत्व की परिभाषा दीजिए। इसका सूत्र लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','किसी पदार्थ का घनत्व उसके द्रव्यमान और आयतन के अनुपात को कहते हैं। सूत्र: घनत्व = द्रव्यमान/आयतन'),(7376,'f5a4f0e1',3233,'ऊष्मा चालन क्या है? उदाहरण दीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','ऊष्मा चालन ऊष्मा का एक स्थान से दूसरे स्थान पर ठोस पदार्थों में संचरण है। उदाहरण: गर्म लोहे की छड़ को छूने पर हाथ जलता है।'),(7377,'f5a4f0e1',3234,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण की प्रक्रिया का विस्तृत वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण वह प्रक्रिया है जिसमें पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश की उपस्थिति में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड और जल से अपना भोजन बनाते हैं और ऑक्सीजन गैस मुक्त करते हैं। यह प्रक्रिया पौधे के हरितलवक में होती है।  इस प्रक्रिया में क्लोरोफिल, सूर्य का प्रकाश, जल और कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड आवश्यक हैं।  ग्लूकोज और ऑक्सीजन इस प्रक्रिया के उत्पाद हैं।'),(7378,'f5a4f0e1',3235,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र बनाइए और इसके विभिन्न अंगों के कार्यों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','यह एक लम्बा उत्तर है जिसमे चित्र और सभी अंगों के कार्य लिखने होंगे।'),(7379,'f5a4f0e1',3236,'ध्वनि क्या है? ध्वनि के परावर्तन और इसके अनुप्रयोगों की व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','ध्वनि एक प्रकार की ऊर्जा है जो कंपन के रूप में यात्रा करती है। ध्वनि का परावर्तन तब होता है जब ध्वनि तरंगें किसी सतह से टकराकर वापस परावर्तित हो जाती हैं। ध्वनि के परावर्तन के अनुप्रयोग हैं: सोनार, इकोलोकेशन, अल्ट्रासाउंड इत्यादि।'),(7380,'f5a4f0e1',3237,'जैव विविधता क्या है? इसके संरक्षण के महत्व और तरीकों पर चर्चा कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','जैव विविधता पृथ्वी पर विभिन्न प्रकार के जीवों और उनके आवासों का समूह है। इसका संरक्षण आवश्यक है क्योंकि यह पारिस्थितिक संतुलन बनाए रखता है, दवाइयों, खाद्य पदार्थों और अन्य संसाधनों का स्रोत है। जैव विविधता के संरक्षण के तरीके हैं: वन संरक्षण, वन्यजीव संरक्षण, प्रदूषण नियंत्रण इत्यादि।'),(7381,'f5a4f0e1',3238,'रासायनिक अभिक्रिया क्या है? रासायनिक अभिक्रिया के प्रकारों का वर्णन कीजिए।  उदाहरण सहित स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','रासायनिक अभिक्रिया वह प्रक्रिया है जिसमें एक या अधिक पदार्थ नए पदार्थों में परिवर्तित होते हैं। विभिन्न प्रकार की रासायनिक अभिक्रियाएँ हैं, जैसे संयोजन अभिक्रिया, वियोजन अभिक्रिया, विस्थापन अभिक्रिया, द्विविस्थापन अभिक्रिया, अपचयन-ऑक्सीकरण अभिक्रिया इत्यादि। प्रत्येक प्रकार की अभिक्रिया को उदाहरणों सहित समझाया जा सकता है।'),(7382,'f5a4f0e1',3239,'कोशिका क्या है? पादप कोशिका और जंतु कोशिका में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए।  नामांकित चित्र बनाइए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','कोशिका जीवन की मूलभूत इकाई है। पादप कोशिका और जंतु कोशिका में कई अंतर होते हैं, जैसे कोशिका भित्ति की उपस्थिति, हरितलवक की उपस्थिति, रिक्तिका का आकार इत्यादि। चित्र बनाकर इन अंतरों को दर्शाया जा सकता है।'),(7383,'f5a4f0e1',3240,'निम्नलिखित को सुमेलित कीजिए:','Matching','Medium',5,'null','सुमेलित करने के लिए प्रश्न और उत्तर की सूची दी जाएगी।'),(7384,'f5a4f0e1',3241,'एक किसान ने अपनी फसल में कीटनाशक का छिड़काव किया, जिससे उसके आस-पास के जीवों को भी नुकसान हुआ। इस घटना के पर्यावरणीय प्रभावों पर चर्चा करें। क्या आप कोई समाधान सुझा सकते हैं?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','कीटनाशक के उपयोग से पर्यावरण प्रदूषण, जैव विविधता में कमी, मनुष्य और पशुओं पर नकारात्मक प्रभाव, मिट्टी और जल प्रदूषण जैसे प्रभाव होते हैं। समाधान के रूप में जैविक कीट नियंत्रण, कीटों के प्राकृतिक शत्रुओं का उपयोग और IPM (Integrated Pest Management) जैसे तरीकों का उपयोग सुझाया जा सकता है।'),(7385,'f5a4f0e1',3207,'ऊष्मा का एसआई मात्रक __________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जूल'),(7386,'f5a4f0e1',3179,'________  एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन का उदाहरण है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','लोहे में जंग लगना'),(7387,'f5a4f0e1',3205,'पौधों में जल का परिवहन __________ द्वारा होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जाइलम'),(7388,'f5a4f0e1',3184,'वायुमंडल की सबसे निचली परत ________ कहलाती है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','क्षोभमंडल'),(7389,'f5a4f0e1',3183,'किसी वस्तु का संवेग उसके ________ और ________ के गुणनफल के बराबर होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','द्रव्यमान, वेग'),(7390,'f5a4f0e1',3208,'वायुमंडल में सबसे अधिक मात्रा में पाई जाने वाली गैस __________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','नाइट्रोजन'),(7391,'a12b32f6',3242,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा पदार्थ एक यौगिक है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हीलियम\"]','C'),(7392,'a12b32f6',3243,'पौधे किस प्रक्रिया द्वारा अपना भोजन बनाते हैं?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"श्वसन\", \"प्रकाश संश्लेषण\", \"अपघटन\", \"उत्सर्जन\"]','B'),(7393,'a12b32f6',3244,'बल का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जूल\", \"वाट\", \"न्यूटन\", \"पास्कल\"]','C'),(7394,'a12b32f6',3245,'ध्वनि किस माध्यम में सबसे तेज गति से चलती है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"वायु\", \"जल\", \"इस्पात\", \"निर्वात\"]','C'),(7395,'a12b32f6',3246,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"कागज़ का फटना\", \"लोहे में जंग लगना\", \"पानी का उबलना\"]','C'),(7396,'a12b32f6',3247,'एक परमाणु का नाभिक किससे बना होता है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"प्रोटॉन और इलेक्ट्रॉन\", \"न्यूट्रॉन और इलेक्ट्रॉन\", \"प्रोटॉन और न्यूट्रॉन\", \"केवल प्रोटॉन\"]','C'),(7397,'a12b32f6',3248,'जड़त्व क्या है? उदाहरण सहित समझाइए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','जड़त्व किसी वस्तु का वह गुण है जिसके कारण वह अपनी विराम अवस्था या एकसमान गति की अवस्था को बनाए रखने का प्रयास करती है जब तक कि उस पर कोई बाहरी बल कार्य न करे। उदाहरण: जब हम चलती बस से अचानक उतरते हैं तो हम आगे की ओर गिर जाते हैं क्योंकि हमारे शरीर का जड़त्व हमें आगे की ओर गतिमान बनाए रखता है।'),(7398,'a12b32f6',3249,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की प्रक्रिया का संक्षेप में वर्णन कीजिए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण में, पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश की ऊर्जा का उपयोग करके कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड और जल से अपना भोजन (ग्लूकोज) बनाते हैं और ऑक्सीजन गैस मुक्त करते हैं।'),(7399,'a12b32f6',3250,'दाब क्या है? इसके मात्रक लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','दाब किसी सतह के इकाई क्षेत्रफल पर लगने वाले बल को कहते हैं। इसका SI मात्रक पास्कल (Pa) है।'),(7400,'a12b32f6',3251,'किन्ही दो रासायनिक परिवर्तनों के उदाहरण दीजिये।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','दूध का दही बनना और लोहे में जंग लगना।'),(7401,'a12b32f6',3252,'ऊर्जा के विभिन्न रूपों के नाम लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','यांत्रिक ऊर्जा, ऊष्मा ऊर्जा, प्रकाश ऊर्जा, ध्वनि ऊर्जा, रासायनिक ऊर्जा, विद्युत ऊर्जा, परमाणु ऊर्जा आदि।'),(7402,'a12b32f6',3253,'न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों को उदाहरण सहित समझाइए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियम इस प्रकार हैं:\n1. जड़त्व का नियम: कोई वस्तु तब तक अपनी विराम अवस्था या एकसमान गति की अवस्था को बनाए रखती है जब तक कि उस पर कोई बाहरी बल कार्य न करे। उदाहरण: एक गेंद तब तक स्थिर रहेगी जब तक हम उसे धक्का नहीं देते।\n2. संवेग का नियम: किसी वस्तु पर कार्य करने वाला बल उस वस्तु के संवेग में परिवर्तन की दर के समानुपाती होता है। उदाहरण: क्रिकेटर गेंद को पकड़ते समय अपने हाथ पीछे खींचता है ताकि गेंद का वेग धीरे-धीरे घटे और हाथों पर कम बल लगे।\n3. क्रिया-प्रतिक्रिया का नियम: प्रत्येक क्रिया के बराबर और विपरीत दिशा में एक प्रतिक्रिया होती है। उदाहरण: जब हम किसी दीवार को धक्का देते हैं तो दीवार भी हमें उतने ही बल से धक्का देती है।'),(7403,'a12b32f6',3254,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का सचित्र वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र मुँह से आरंभ होकर गुदा तक जाता है। इसमें मुँह, ग्रसनी, ग्रासनली, आमाशय, छोटी आंत, बड़ी आंत, मलाशय और गुदा शामिल हैं। चित्र आवश्यक है।'),(7404,'a12b32f6',3255,'किसी वस्तु के गतिज ऊर्जा और स्थितिज ऊर्जा को समझाइए। सूत्र भी लिखिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','गतिज ऊर्जा किसी गतिमान वस्तु में धारित ऊर्जा होती है। इसका सूत्र 1/2mv² है जहाँ m वस्तु का द्रव्यमान और v उसका वेग है। स्थितिज ऊर्जा किसी वस्तु में उसकी स्थिति के कारण धारित ऊर्जा होती है। इसका सूत्र mgh है जहाँ m वस्तु का द्रव्यमान, g गुरुत्वीय त्वरण और h वस्तु की ऊँचाई है।'),(7405,'a12b32f6',3256,'वायुमंडल की परतों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','वायुमंडल कई परतों में विभाजित है: क्षोभमंडल, समतापमंडल, मध्यमंडल, आयनमंडल और बाह्यमंडल। प्रत्येक परत की अपनी विशेषताएँ हैं, जैसे तापमान, घनत्व और वायुमंडलीय दबाव।'),(7406,'a12b32f6',3257,'परमाणु संरचना का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','एक परमाणु में नाभिक होता है जिसमें प्रोटॉन और न्यूट्रॉन होते हैं और उसके चारों ओर इलेक्ट्रॉन चक्कर लगाते हैं। प्रोटॉन धनावेशित, न्यूट्रॉन उदासीन और इलेक्ट्रॉन ऋणावेशित होते हैं।'),(7407,'a12b32f6',3258,'जैव विविधता क्या है? इसके संरक्षण के कोई तीन तरीके बताइए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','जैव विविधता पृथ्वी पर पाए जाने वाले सभी जीवों और उनके आवासों की विविधता को संदर्भित करती है। इसके संरक्षण के तरीके हैं: वन संरक्षण, वन्यजीव संरक्षण और जागरूकता फैलाना।'),(7408,'a12b32f6',3259,'निम्नलिखित को सुमेलित कीजिए:','Matching','Medium',3,'null','A-iv, B-iii, C-i, D-ii'),(7409,'a12b32f6',3260,'एक छात्र ने एक प्रयोग में एक गेंद को ऊपर की ओर फेंका। गेंद ने कुछ ऊँचाई तक पहुँचकर फिर नीचे गिरना शुरू कर दिया।\n(a) गेंद के ऊपर जाने पर उसकी गतिज ऊर्जा और स्थितिज ऊर्जा में क्या परिवर्तन होता है?\n(b) गेंद के नीचे गिरने पर उसकी गतिज ऊर्जा और स्थितिज ऊर्जा में क्या परिवर्तन होता है?\n(c) ऊर्जा संरक्षण के सिद्धांत को इस प्रयोग से कैसे समझाया जा सकता है?','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','(a) गेंद के ऊपर जाने पर उसकी गतिज ऊर्जा घटती है और स्थितिज ऊर्जा बढ़ती है।\n(b) गेंद के नीचे गिरने पर उसकी गतिज ऊर्जा बढ़ती है और स्थितिज ऊर्जा घटती है।\n(c) ऊर्जा संरक्षण के सिद्धांत के अनुसार, ऊर्जा न तो उत्पन्न की जा सकती है और न ही नष्ट की जा सकती है, केवल एक रूप से दूसरे रूप में परिवर्तित की जा सकती है। इस प्रयोग में, गेंद की कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा (गतिज ऊर्जा + स्थितिज ऊर्जा) स्थिर रहती है, केवल गतिज ऊर्जा स्थितिज ऊर्जा में और स्थितिज ऊर्जा गतिज ऊर्जा में परिवर्तित होती है।'),(7410,'a12b32f6',3181,'पौधों में जल का परिवहन ________ द्वारा होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जाइलम'),(7411,'a12b32f6',3184,'वायुमंडल की सबसे निचली परत ________ कहलाती है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','क्षोभमंडल'),(7412,'a12b32f6',3179,'________  एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन का उदाहरण है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','लोहे में जंग लगना'),(7413,'a12b32f6',3204,'__________ एक धातु है जो कमरे के तापमान पर द्रव अवस्था में रहती है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','पारा'),(7414,'a12b32f6',3208,'वायुमंडल में सबसे अधिक मात्रा में पाई जाने वाली गैस __________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','नाइट्रोजन'),(7415,'a12b32f6',3182,'प्रकाश का परावर्तन के नियम ________  है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','दो'),(7416,'95b1938d',3261,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सी धातु सबसे अधिक अभिक्रियाशील है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"सोना\", \"चाँदी\", \"पोटेशियम\", \"ताँबा\"]','C'),(7417,'95b1938d',3262,'पौधों में भोजन का निर्माण किस प्रक्रिया द्वारा होता है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"श्वसन\", \"प्रकाश संश्लेषण\", \"परिवहन\", \"उत्सर्जन\"]','B'),(7418,'95b1938d',3263,'वायुमंडल में सबसे अधिक मात्रा में कौन सी गैस पाई जाती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"आर्गन\"]','C'),(7419,'95b1938d',3264,'बल का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"जूल\", \"वाट\", \"न्यूटन\", \"पास्कल\"]','C'),(7420,'95b1938d',3265,'किस प्रकार के उत्तक शरीर के विभिन्न अंगों को जोड़ते हैं?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"उपकला ऊतक\", \"संयोजी ऊतक\", \"पेशीय ऊतक\", \"तंत्रिका ऊतक\"]','B'),(7421,'95b1938d',3266,'पृथ्वी पर गुरुत्वाकर्षण का मान लगभग कितना होता है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"9.8 m/s²\", \"98 m/s²\", \"980 m/s²\", \"0.98 m/s²\"]','A'),(7422,'95b1938d',3267,'जीवों में पाए जाने वाले दो मुख्य प्रकार के कोशिकाओं के नाम लिखिए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','प्रोकैरियोटिक और यूकैरियोटिक कोशिकाएँ'),(7423,'95b1938d',3268,'किसी वस्तु का संवेग क्या होता है? सूत्र लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','किसी वस्तु का संवेग उसके द्रव्यमान और वेग के गुणनफल के बराबर होता है। सूत्र: संवेग = द्रव्यमान × वेग'),(7424,'95b1938d',3269,'जैव निम्नीकरणीय और अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थों में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','जैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे पदार्थ हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से विघटित हो जाते हैं, जबकि अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ विघटित नहीं होते हैं।'),(7425,'95b1938d',3270,'गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल क्या है? इसके दो उदाहरण दीजिये।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल वह बल है जो दो वस्तुओं के बीच उनके द्रव्यमान के कारण लगता है। उदाहरण: सेब का पेड़ से गिरना, चाँद का पृथ्वी के चारों ओर चक्कर लगाना।'),(7426,'95b1938d',3271,'संक्षेप में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की प्रक्रिया समझाइए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण वह प्रक्रिया है जिसमें पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश की उपस्थिति में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड और जल से भोजन बनाते हैं और ऑक्सीजन गैस छोड़ते हैं।'),(7427,'95b1938d',3272,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण की प्रक्रिया का विस्तार से वर्णन कीजिए। इसमें शामिल पदार्थों और परिस्थितियों का उल्लेख कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण एक जटिल प्रक्रिया है जिसमें पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश, जल, और कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड का उपयोग करके ग्लूकोज (भोजन) का निर्माण करते हैं और ऑक्सीजन गैस छोड़ते हैं। यह क्लोरोप्लास्ट में होता है, जिसमें क्लोरोफिल होता है जो प्रकाश को अवशोषित करता है।'),(7428,'95b1938d',3273,'बल के विभिन्न प्रकारों का वर्णन कीजिए और प्रत्येक का एक उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','बल के कई प्रकार हैं, जैसे गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल, घर्षण बल, चुंबकीय बल, स्थिर विद्युत बल इत्यादि। गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल दो वस्तुओं के बीच लगने वाला आकर्षण बल है (उदाहरण: सेब का पेड़ से गिरना)। घर्षण बल दो सतहों के बीच लगने वाला बल है (उदाहरण: ब्रेक लगाना)। चुंबकीय बल चुंबक के द्वारा लगने वाला बल है (उदाहरण: चुंबक द्वारा लोहे को खींचना)। स्थिर विद्युत बल दो आवेशित वस्तुओं के बीच लगने वाला बल है (उदाहरण: स्टैटिक शॉक)।'),(7429,'95b1938d',3274,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का सचित्र वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र मुँह से शुरू होकर गुदा तक जाता है। इसमें मुँह, ग्रासनली, आमाशय, छोटी आंत, बड़ी आंत और गुदा शामिल हैं। मुँह में भोजन का पाचन लार एन्ज़ाइम द्वारा शुरू होता है। आमाशय में अम्लीय माध्यम में भोजन का पाचन होता है। छोटी आंत में भोजन का अधिकांश पाचन और अवशोषण होता है। बड़ी आंत में जल का अवशोषण होता है और मल का निर्माण होता है। (चित्र आवश्यक है)'),(7430,'95b1938d',3275,'कोशिका के विभिन्न भागों का वर्णन कीजिए और उनके कार्यों को समझाइए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','कोशिका जीवन की आधारभूत इकाई है। इसमें केन्द्रक, कोशिका द्रव्य, कोशिका झिल्ली, माइटोकांड्रिया, राइबोसोम, एंडोप्लाज़्मिक रेटिकुलम, गॉल्जी उपकरण आदि अंगक होते हैं। केन्द्रक कोशिका का नियंत्रण केंद्र है, कोशिका झिल्ली कोशिका की सुरक्षा करती है, माइटोकांड्रिया ऊर्जा उत्पादन करता है, राइबोसोम प्रोटीन संश्लेषण करता है, आदि।'),(7431,'95b1938d',3276,'जल प्रदूषण के कारणों और इसके नियंत्रण के उपायों पर विस्तार से चर्चा कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','जल प्रदूषण के कई कारण हैं जैसे औद्योगिक अपशिष्ट, कृषि रसायनों का उपयोग, घरेलू कचरा, तेल रिसाव आदि। इसके नियंत्रण के लिए उचित अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन, औद्योगिक अपशिष्टों का उपचार, जागरूकता अभियान, और जल संरक्षण के उपायों को अपनाना आवश्यक है।'),(7432,'95b1938d',3277,'धातु और अधातु में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए। उदाहरण सहित समझाइए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','धातुएँ चमकदार, तन्य, आघातवर्धनीय होती हैं और विद्युत और ऊष्मा की सुचालक होती हैं। उदाहरण: लोहा, ताँबा, सोना। अधातुएँ भंगुर, कुचालक होती हैं और चमकदार नहीं होती हैं। उदाहरण: कार्बन, ऑक्सीजन, सल्फर।'),(7433,'95b1938d',3278,'निम्नलिखित को सुमेलित कीजिए:','Matching','Medium',5,'null','A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2, E-5'),(7434,'95b1938d',3279,'रिया ने एक प्रयोग में एक लोहे की कील को पानी में डुबोया और उसे कुछ दिनों के लिए छोड़ दिया। कुछ दिनों बाद उसने देखा कि कील पर जंग लग गया है।\n(क) यह किस प्रकार का परिवर्तन है? स्पष्ट कीजिए।\n(ख) जंग लगने की प्रक्रिया को रोकने के लिए क्या किया जा सकता है? दो उपाय बताइए।\n(ग) इस प्रक्रिया में कौन सी गैस महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाती है?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(क) यह एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है क्योंकि लोहे की कील का रासायनिक संगठन बदल गया है और नया पदार्थ (जंग) बन गया है।\n(ख) जंग लगने को रोकने के लिए कील पर पेंट या तेल लगाया जा सकता है, या इसे जस्ती किया जा सकता है।\n(ग) इस प्रक्रिया में ऑक्सीजन गैस महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाती है।'),(7435,'95b1938d',3180,'ऊष्मा का SI मात्रक ________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जूल'),(7436,'95b1938d',3206,'किसी वस्तु का द्रव्यमान उसकी __________ का माप है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','निष्क्रियता'),(7437,'95b1938d',3182,'प्रकाश का परावर्तन के नियम ________  है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','दो'),(7438,'95b1938d',3183,'किसी वस्तु का संवेग उसके ________ और ________ के गुणनफल के बराबर होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','द्रव्यमान, वेग'),(7439,'95b1938d',3208,'वायुमंडल में सबसे अधिक मात्रा में पाई जाने वाली गैस __________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','नाइट्रोजन'),(7440,'95b1938d',3205,'पौधों में जल का परिवहन __________ द्वारा होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जाइलम'),(7441,'ed41cef2',3280,'पौधे किस प्रक्रिया द्वारा अपना भोजन बनाते हैं?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"श्वसन\", \"प्रकाश संश्लेषण\", \"अपघटन\", \"परासरण\"]','B'),(7442,'ed41cef2',3281,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सी धातु सबसे अधिक अभिक्रियाशील है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"सोना\", \"चाँदी\", \"ताँबा\", \"पोटेशियम\"]','D'),(7443,'ed41cef2',3282,'मानव शरीर में रक्त का मुख्य कार्य क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऊर्जा उत्पादन\", \"शरीर का तापमान नियंत्रित करना\", \"ऑक्सीजन और पोषक तत्वों का परिवहन\", \"अपशिष्ट पदार्थों का उत्सर्जन\"]','C'),(7444,'ed41cef2',3283,'कौन सा बल पृथ्वी पर वस्तुओं को अपनी ओर खींचता है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"घर्षण बल\", \"चुम्बकीय बल\", \"गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल\", \"स्थितिज ऊर्जा\"]','C'),(7445,'ed41cef2',3284,'ध्वनि की तीव्रता किससे मापी जाती है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"मीटर\", \"किलोग्राम\", \"डेसिबल\", \"सेल्शियस\"]','C'),(7446,'ed41cef2',3285,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन का उदाहरण है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"कागज़ का फटना\", \"लोहे में जंग लगना\", \"पानी का उबलना\"]','C'),(7447,'ed41cef2',3286,'जैव निम्नीकरणीय और अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थों में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','जैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे पदार्थ हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से सूक्ष्मजीवों द्वारा विघटित हो जाते हैं, जबकि अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ प्राकृतिक रूप से विघटित नहीं होते हैं।'),(7448,'ed41cef2',3287,'किसी वस्तु का वेग क्या होता है? इसे कैसे मापा जाता है?','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','वेग किसी वस्तु के विस्थापन की दर है। इसे विस्थापन को समय से भाग देकर मापा जाता है।'),(7449,'ed41cef2',3288,'घर्षण बल क्या है? इसके लाभ और हानियाँ लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','घर्षण बल दो सतहों के बीच एक विरोधी बल है जो उनकी आपेक्षिक गति का विरोध करता है। लाभ: चलना, लिखना, वाहनों को रोकना। हानियाँ: ऊर्जा का क्षय, मशीनों में टूट-फूट।'),(7450,'ed41cef2',3289,'ऊर्जा के विभिन्न रूपों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','ऊर्जा के विभिन्न रूप हैं: यांत्रिक ऊर्जा, तापीय ऊर्जा, प्रकाश ऊर्जा, ध्वनि ऊर्जा, रासायनिक ऊर्जा, विद्युत ऊर्जा, परमाणु ऊर्जा।'),(7451,'ed41cef2',3290,'ज्वालामुखी से निकलने वाले पदार्थों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','ज्वालामुखी से लावा, गैसें, राख, पत्थर और भाप निकलते हैं।'),(7452,'ed41cef2',3291,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण की प्रक्रिया का विस्तृत वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण एक प्रक्रिया है जिसमें हरे पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश की उपस्थिति में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड और जल से अपना भोजन बनाते हैं और ऑक्सीजन मुक्त करते हैं। इस प्रक्रिया में क्लोरोफिल की महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका होती है।'),(7453,'ed41cef2',3292,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र बनाइए और इसके विभिन्न अंगों के कार्यों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र मुँह से शुरू होकर गुदा तक जाता है। इसमें मुँह, ग्रासनली, आमाशय, छोटी आंत, बड़ी आंत, मलाशय और गुदा शामिल हैं। प्रत्येक अंग का विशिष्ट कार्य होता है जैसे भोजन का पाचन, अवशोषण और उत्सर्जन।'),(7454,'ed41cef2',3293,'ध्वनि क्या है? ध्वनि के संचरण के लिए माध्यम की आवश्यकता क्यों होती है?','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','ध्वनि एक प्रकार की ऊर्जा है जो कंपन के रूप में संचरित होती है। ध्वनि के संचरण के लिए माध्यम (जैसे हवा, पानी, ठोस) की आवश्यकता होती है क्योंकि ध्वनि तरंगें माध्यम के कणों के कंपन के द्वारा चलती हैं। निर्वात में ध्वनि संचारित नहीं हो सकती।'),(7455,'ed41cef2',3294,'बल क्या है? बल के प्रकारों का वर्णन कीजिए और प्रत्येक प्रकार के बल के उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',3,'null','बल वह कारक है जो किसी वस्तु की गति की अवस्था में परिवर्तन करता है या उसे विकृत करता है। बल के मुख्य प्रकार हैं: गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल, विद्युत बल, चुम्बकीय बल, घर्षण बल, और प्रत्यानयन बल।'),(7456,'ed41cef2',3295,'जल प्रदूषण के कारणों और उसके प्रभावों पर चर्चा कीजिए। जल प्रदूषण को रोकने के उपाय सुझाइए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','जल प्रदूषण के मुख्य कारण हैं: औद्योगिक अपशिष्ट, कृषि रसायन, घरेलू कचरा, तेल रिसाव आदि। इसके प्रभाव हैं: जलजन्य रोग, जलीय जीवन का क्षय, पर्यावरणीय असंतुलन। जल प्रदूषण को रोकने के लिए अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन, जागरूकता, और कड़े नियमों की आवश्यकता है।'),(7457,'ed41cef2',3296,'कार्बन चक्र का वर्णन कीजिए और इसके महत्व पर प्रकाश डालिए।','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','कार्बन चक्र कार्बन के विभिन्न रूपों (कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड, कार्बोहाइड्रेट, आदि) के वायुमंडल, जल, मिट्टी और जीवों के बीच चक्रण को दर्शाता है। यह जीवन के लिए अत्यंत महत्वपूर्ण है क्योंकि यह पौधों द्वारा प्रकाश संश्लेषण में उपयोग किया जाता है और भोजन श्रृंखला में ऊर्जा का स्थानांतरण करता है।'),(7458,'ed41cef2',3297,'निम्नलिखित स्तंभों का मिलान कीजिए:','Matching','Medium',3,'null','A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3'),(7459,'ed41cef2',3298,'एक किसान ने अपनी फसल में अधिक उपज प्राप्त करने के लिए बहुत अधिक रासायनिक उर्वरक का प्रयोग किया। कुछ समय बाद, वह फसल की बुरी स्थिति देखकर चिंतित हो गया। फसल मुरझा रही थी और पौधे पीले पड़ रहे थे।','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','अधिक रासायनिक उर्वरकों के प्रयोग से मिट्टी का क्षारीयकरण हुआ होगा जिससे पौधे पोषक तत्वों को अवशोषित नहीं कर पा रहे हैं और मुरझा रहे हैं।'),(7460,'ed41cef2',3205,'पौधों में जल का परिवहन __________ द्वारा होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जाइलम'),(7461,'ed41cef2',3180,'ऊष्मा का SI मात्रक ________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जूल'),(7462,'ed41cef2',3182,'प्रकाश का परावर्तन के नियम ________  है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','दो'),(7463,'ed41cef2',3183,'किसी वस्तु का संवेग उसके ________ और ________ के गुणनफल के बराबर होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','द्रव्यमान, वेग'),(7464,'ed41cef2',3179,'________  एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन का उदाहरण है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','लोहे में जंग लगना'),(7465,'ed41cef2',3206,'किसी वस्तु का द्रव्यमान उसकी __________ का माप है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','निष्क्रियता'),(7466,'19cf1ec6',3299,'पौधों में भोजन का निर्माण किस प्रक्रिया द्वारा होता है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"श्वसन\", \"प्रकाश संश्लेषण\", \"परिवहन\", \"उत्सर्जन\"]','B'),(7467,'19cf1ec6',3300,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"कागज़ का फटना\", \"लोहे में जंग लगना\", \"पानी का उबलना\"]','C'),(7468,'19cf1ec6',3301,'मानव शरीर में सबसे लंबी कोशिका कौन सी होती है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"न्यूरॉन\", \"मांसपेशी कोशिका\", \"रक्त कोशिका\", \"त्वचा कोशिका\"]','A'),(7469,'19cf1ec6',3302,'वायुमंडल की सबसे निचली परत कौन सी है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"समताप मंडल\", \"आयन मंडल\", \"क्षोभ मंडल\", \"बाह्य मंडल\"]','C'),(7470,'19cf1ec6',3303,'किस गैस की अधिकता से ग्लोबल वार्मिंग होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हाइड्रोजन\"]','C'),(7471,'19cf1ec6',3304,'जैव निम्नीकरणीय और अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थों में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','जैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे पदार्थ हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से अपघटित हो जाते हैं, जैसे कि फल और सब्जियाँ। अजैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ वे पदार्थ हैं जो प्राकृतिक रूप से अपघटित नहीं होते हैं, जैसे कि प्लास्टिक और धातु।'),(7472,'19cf1ec6',3305,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण क्या है? संक्षेप में समझाइए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','प्रकाश संश्लेषण वह प्रक्रिया है जिसमें पौधे सूर्य के प्रकाश, जल और कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड का उपयोग करके अपना भोजन बनाते हैं।'),(7473,'19cf1ec6',3306,'किसी भी दो ऊर्जा के स्रोतों के नाम लिखिए।','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','सूर्य और कोयला'),(7474,'19cf1ec6',3307,'पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र क्या है?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र जीवों और उनके पर्यावरण के बीच परस्पर क्रिया का एक समुदाय है।'),(7475,'19cf1ec6',3308,'ऊष्मा चालन क्या है?','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','ऊष्मा चालन ऊष्मा का एक पिंड से दूसरे पिंड में प्रत्यक्ष संपर्क द्वारा स्थानांतरण है।'),(7476,'19cf1ec6',3309,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का विस्तृत वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र मुँह से शुरू होता है जहाँ भोजन चबाया जाता है और लार द्वारा पाचन शुरू होता है। फिर भोजन ग्रासनली से होता हुआ आमाशय में जाता है जहाँ हाइड्रोक्लोरिक अम्ल और एंजाइम भोजन को पचाते हैं। आमाशय से भोजन छोटी आंत में जाता है जहाँ अधिकांश पाचन और पोषक तत्वों का अवशोषण होता है। छोटी आंत के बाद भोजन बड़ी आंत में जाता है जहाँ पानी का अवशोषण होता है और मल बनता है जो गुदा से बाहर निकलता है।'),(7477,'19cf1ec6',3310,'वायु प्रदूषण के कारणों और प्रभावों पर चर्चा कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','वायु प्रदूषण के कई कारण हैं, जैसे कि औद्योगिक उत्सर्जन, वाहनों से निकलने वाला धुआँ, जंगल की आग और निर्माण गतिविधियाँ। इनसे कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड, सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड और नाइट्रोजन ऑक्साइड जैसी हानिकारक गैसें निकलती हैं। वायु प्रदूषण के प्रभावों में श्वसन संबंधी समस्याएँ, अम्लीय वर्षा, ओजोन परत का क्षरण और ग्लोबल वार्मिंग शामिल हैं।'),(7478,'19cf1ec6',3311,'पौधों में जल का परिवहन कैसे होता है? विस्तार से समझाइए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','पौधों में जल का परिवहन जाइलम द्वारा होता है।  जल जड़ों द्वारा अवशोषित होता है और जाइलम के माध्यम से पत्तियों तक पहुँचता है। यह प्रक्रिया मूल दाब,  केशिकत्व और वाष्पोत्सर्जन द्वारा संचालित होती है। मूल दाब जड़ों में जल का दबाव है जो जल को ऊपर की ओर धकेलता है। केशिकत्व जाइलम के संकीर्ण नलिकाओं में जल के चढ़ने की प्रवृत्ति है। वाष्पोत्सर्जन पत्तियों से जल का वाष्पीकरण है जो एक खिंचाव बल बनाता है जो जल को ऊपर खींचता है।'),(7479,'19cf1ec6',3312,'विभिन्न प्रकार की मृदाओं के नाम लिखिए और उनके गुणों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','मुख्य मृदा प्रकार हैं: बलुई मिट्टी, दोमट मिट्टी और चिकनी मिट्टी। बलुई मिट्टी में बड़े कण होते हैं, जल निकासी अच्छी होती है लेकिन जलधारण क्षमता कम होती है। दोमट मिट्टी में बलुई और चिकनी मिट्टी के गुणों का मिश्रण होता है। चिकनी मिट्टी में छोटे कण होते हैं, जलधारण क्षमता अधिक होती है लेकिन जल निकासी कम होती है।'),(7480,'19cf1ec6',3313,'पर्यावरण संरक्षण के लिए हम क्या कदम उठा सकते हैं? कम से कम पाँच सुझाव दीजिये।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','पर्यावरण संरक्षण के लिए हम कई कदम उठा सकते हैं जैसे कि वृक्षारोपण, प्रदूषण कम करना, ऊर्जा संरक्षण, अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन और जागरूकता फैलाना।'),(7481,'19cf1ec6',3314,'रिया ने अपने घर के पास एक नदी में बहुत सारा प्रदूषण देखा। पानी गंदा था और उसमें कचरा तैर रहा था।  उसने देखा कि फैक्ट्री से निकलने वाला गंदा पानी सीधे नदी में मिल रहा था।\n\n(क) नदी के प्रदूषण के क्या कारण हो सकते हैं?\n(ख) इस प्रदूषण के क्या प्रभाव हो सकते हैं?\n(ग) इस समस्या का समाधान कैसे किया जा सकता है?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(क) नदी के प्रदूषण के कारण फैक्ट्री से निकलने वाला गंदा पानी, घरेलू कचरा, और अन्य प्रदूषक हो सकते हैं।\n(ख) इस प्रदूषण से पानी दूषित हो सकता है, जलीय जीवों को नुकसान पहुँच सकता है और मानव स्वास्थ्य पर भी बुरा प्रभाव पड़ सकता है।\n(ग) इस समस्या का समाधान फैक्ट्री मालिकों को प्रदूषण नियंत्रण उपाय अपनाने के लिए प्रेरित करके, कचरा प्रबंधन में सुधार करके और जनजागरूकता अभियान चलाकर किया जा सकता है।'),(7482,'7550dcad',2961,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक जैव निम्नीकरणीय पदार्थ है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"प्लास्टिक\", \"काँच\", \"लकड़ी\", \"धातु\"]','C'),(7483,'7550dcad',2979,'मानव शरीर में किस अंग में पाचन प्रक्रिया शुरू होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"आमाशय\", \"छोटी आंत\", \"मुख\", \"बड़ी आंत\"]','C'),(7484,'7550dcad',2962,'ध्वनि की तीव्रता मापी जाती है:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"मीटर में\", \"सेल्सियस में\", \"डेसीबल में\", \"केल्विन में\"]','C'),(7485,'7550dcad',2959,'अम्ल का pH मान होता है:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"7 से अधिक\", \"7\", \"7 से कम\", \"0\"]','C'),(7486,'7550dcad',3044,'अम्लीय वर्षा का मुख्य कारण क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"ओजोन परत का क्षरण\", \"ग्रीनहाउस प्रभाव\", \"वायु प्रदूषण\", \"जल प्रदूषण\"]','C'),(7487,'7550dcad',2982,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक जैव अपघटनीय पदार्थ है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"प्लास्टिक\", \"कांच\", \"कागज़\", \"एल्यूमीनियम\"]','C'),(7488,'7550dcad',3011,'जल प्रदूषण के कारणों और निवारण के उपायों पर चर्चा कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','जल प्रदूषण के कई कारण हैं, जैसे औद्योगिक अपशिष्ट, कृषि रसायन, घरेलू कचरा, तेल रिसाव इत्यादि।  इनसे जल में हानिकारक पदार्थों का प्रवेश होता है, जिससे जलजीवन प्रभावित होता है और मानव स्वास्थ्य के लिए खतरा पैदा होता है।  निवारण के उपायों में शामिल हैं: उचित अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन, औद्योगिक अपशिष्ट का उपचार, जैविक खेती, जागरूकता अभियान इत्यादि।'),(7489,'7550dcad',3014,'वायु प्रदूषण के प्रमुख स्रोतों और इसके नियंत्रण के उपायों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','वायु प्रदूषण के प्रमुख स्रोत हैं: वाहनों से निकलने वाला धुआँ, औद्योगिक उत्सर्जन, जंगल की आग, निर्माण कार्य इत्यादि।  इनसे वायु में हानिकारक गैसें और कणिकाएँ मिल जाती हैं, जिससे स्वास्थ्य समस्याएँ और पर्यावरणीय क्षति होती है।  नियंत्रण के उपायों में शामिल हैं: वाहनों में उत्सर्जन मानकों का पालन, उद्योगों में प्रदूषण नियंत्रण तकनीक का उपयोग, पौधरोपण, सार्वजनिक परिवहन का उपयोग इत्यादि।'),(7490,'7550dcad',3013,'आनुवंशिकता और विविधता के बीच संबंध स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','आनुवंशिकता माता-पिता से संतानों में लक्षणों के हस्तांतरण की प्रक्रिया है, जो जीन द्वारा नियंत्रित होती है। विविधता जीवों में लक्षणों के अंतर को दर्शाती है।  ये दोनों परस्पर संबंधित हैं क्योंकि आनुवंशिकता के दौरान होने वाले जीन उत्परिवर्तन और जीन पुनर्संयोजन विविधता उत्पन्न करते हैं। विविधता जीवों को बदलते पर्यावरण के अनुकूल होने में मदद करती है।'),(7491,'7550dcad',2969,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र बनाइए और इसके विभिन्न अंगों के कार्यों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','चित्र सहित उत्तर। विभिन्न अंगों के कार्य का विस्तृत वर्णन।'),(7492,'7550dcad',2973,'जैव विकास के सिद्धांत की व्याख्या कीजिए। डार्विन के प्राकृतिक वरण के सिद्धांत का उल्लेख कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','जैव विकास के सिद्धांत की व्याख्या। डार्विन के प्राकृतिक वरण के सिद्धांत का विस्तृत वर्णन।'),(7493,'7550dcad',3016,'एक किसान अपनी फसल को कीटों से बचाने के लिए कीटनाशकों का उपयोग करता है। लेकिन, बारिश के पानी से यह कीटनाशक पास की झील में मिल जाता है। झील में मछलियाँ मरने लगी हैं।','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','कीटनाशकों के उपयोग से झील में जल प्रदूषण हुआ है।  कीटनाशक मछलियों के लिए हानिकारक हैं और उनकी मृत्यु का कारण बनते हैं।  यह एक उदाहरण है कि कैसे मानवीय क्रियाएँ पर्यावरण को प्रभावित करती हैं। किसान को जैविक खेती के तरीकों को अपनाना चाहिए या कम हानिकारक कीटनाशकों का उपयोग करना चाहिए।'),(7494,'fc544f9a',2924,'मानव शरीर में सबसे बड़ी धमनी कौन सी है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"शिरा\", \"धमनी\", \"महाधमनी\", \"केशिका\"]','C'),(7495,'fc544f9a',2200,'What is the focal length of a plane mirror?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Zero\", \"Infinity\", \"10 cm\", \"Variable\"]','B'),(7496,'fc544f9a',2778,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(7497,'fc544f9a',2901,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(7498,'fc544f9a',1819,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll.  It involves the conversion of carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen using light energy.'),(7499,'fc544f9a',1833,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change is a change in which the substance\'s chemical composition remains the same.  Examples include melting ice, tearing paper.  A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition, resulting in the formation of a new substance. Examples include burning wood, rusting iron.'),(7500,'22ef76ee',2777,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(7501,'22ef76ee',2396,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(7502,'22ef76ee',2466,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(7503,'22ef76ee',2759,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(7504,'22ef76ee',1834,'State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Limitations include its non-applicability to non-ohmic conductors (like diodes) and its breakdown at high temperatures or voltages.'),(7505,'22ef76ee',1851,'Differentiate between mitosis and meiosis. Mention the significance of each.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Mitosis is a type of cell division that produces two identical daughter cells, while meiosis produces four genetically different haploid cells. Mitosis is for growth and repair; meiosis is for sexual reproduction.'),(7506,'3c3d4c54',2104,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\"]','C'),(7507,'3c3d4c54',2884,'What is the name of the force that pulls objects towards the center of the Earth?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Friction\", \"Gravity\", \"Tension\", \"Pressure\"]','B'),(7508,'3c3d4c54',2152,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\"]','C'),(7509,'3c3d4c54',2877,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Newton\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','B'),(7510,'5ab197e9',2877,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Newton\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','B'),(7511,'5ab197e9',2902,'What is the name of the force that keeps planets in orbit around the sun?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Friction\", \"Gravity\", \"Electromagnetism\", \"Nuclear force\"]','B'),(7512,'5ab197e9',2825,'The SI unit of force is:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Newton\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','B'),(7513,'5ab197e9',2884,'What is the name of the force that pulls objects towards the center of the Earth?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Friction\", \"Gravity\", \"Tension\", \"Pressure\"]','B'),(7514,'8ba67077',2081,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Plano-convex lens\", \"Plano-concave lens\"]','B'),(7515,'8ba67077',2346,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(7516,'8ba67077',2396,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"H2O\", \"NaCl\", \"O2\"]','B'),(7517,'8ba67077',2299,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\", \"Nuclear Energy\"]','C'),(7518,'8ba67077',2805,'Which of these is a renewable source of energy?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Petroleum\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\"]','D'),(7519,'8ba67077',2899,'What is the unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Watt\", \"Ohm\"]','B'),(7520,'8ba67077',2032,'The SI unit of force is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Newton'),(7521,'8ba67077',2057,'The process of converting light energy into electrical energy is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','photovoltaic'),(7522,'8ba67077',2697,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _____________','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Red'),(7523,'8ba67077',2761,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(7524,'8ba67077',1836,'What are the different types of lenses and their uses?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex (converging) and concave (diverging). Convex lenses are used in magnifying glasses, cameras, and eyeglasses for farsightedness. Concave lenses are used in eyeglasses for nearsightedness and telescopes.'),(7525,'8ba67077',1849,'Explain the difference between a physical and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(7526,'8ba67077',1821,'Explain the difference between a conductor and an insulator.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Conductors allow electric current to flow easily through them due to the presence of free electrons. Insulators resist the flow of electric current because they have very few free electrons.'),(7527,'8ba67077',1834,'State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant. Limitations include its non-applicability to non-ohmic conductors (like diodes) and its breakdown at high temperatures or voltages.'),(7528,'8ba67077',2600,'Describe the structure and function of the human respiratory system.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The respiratory system consists of the nose, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, bronchioles, and alveoli.  It facilitates the intake of oxygen and the removal of carbon dioxide from the body through the process of respiration.  Describe each component and its role in detail.'),(7529,'8ba67077',1840,'Explain the Mendelian laws of inheritance with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Mendelian laws of inheritance include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment. The law of segregation states that during gamete formation, the alleles for each gene segregate from each other so that each gamete carries only one allele for each gene. The law of independent assortment states that during gamete formation, the segregation of the alleles for one gene occurs independently of the segregation of alleles for other genes. Examples should be given using monohybrid and dihybrid crosses.'),(7530,'8ba67077',2728,'Discuss the different types of chemical reactions with suitable examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Different types of chemical reactions include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples should be provided for each type.'),(7531,'8ba67077',1856,'Describe the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','(The answer should describe various types of chemical reactions such as combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions with suitable examples for each.)'),(7532,'8ba67077',2099,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Photosynthesis\n2.  Respiration\n3.  Excretion\n4.  Transpiration\n\nColumn B\nA. Removal of waste products\nB. Release of water vapor from leaves\nC. Conversion of light energy into chemical energy\nD. Release of energy from food','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(7533,'8ba67077',2731,'A student conducted an experiment to study the effect of different fertilizers on the growth of plants.  He used three types of fertilizers: A, B, and C.  He planted three similar plants in separate pots and used a different fertilizer for each plant.  After a month, he measured the height of each plant. Plant A grew to 10cm, Plant B grew to 15cm, and Plant C grew to 20cm.\n\n(a) Identify the dependent and independent variables in this experiment.\n(b) Which fertilizer was most effective?\n(c) Suggest two factors that could affect the results of this experiment besides the fertilizer used.\n(d) What could be done to improve the reliability of the experiment?','Case Study','Medium',5,'null','(a) Dependent variable: Plant height; Independent variable: Type of fertilizer\n(b) Fertilizer C\n(c) Amount of sunlight, amount of water\n(d) Use more than one plant per fertilizer type; control other variables more carefully; repeat the experiment.'),(7534,'3d3b2f53',2907,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया किस अंग में होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जड़\", \"तना\", \"पत्तियाँ\", \"फूल\"]','C'),(7535,'3d3b2f53',2906,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा पदार्थ एक यौगिक है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हीलियम\"]','C'),(7536,'3d3b2f53',2909,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"पानी का उबलना\", \"कागज़ का जलना\", \"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"लोहे का पिघलना\"]','B'),(7537,'3d3b2f53',2674,'Which of the following is NOT a type of tissue?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Epithelial tissue\", \"Connective tissue\", \"Nervous tissue\", \"Photosynthesis\"]','D'),(7538,'3d3b2f53',2673,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Newton\", \"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','A'),(7539,'3d3b2f53',2678,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(7540,'3d3b2f53',2675,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(7541,'3d3b2f53',2676,'The force of attraction between any two objects having mass is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(7542,'3d3b2f53',2677,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(7543,'3d3b2f53',2918,'ध्वनि क्या है? ध्वनि के उत्पन्न होने, संचरण और परावर्तन की व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','ध्वनि की परिभाषा, उत्पन्न होने की प्रक्रिया, संचरण के माध्यम और परावर्तन की व्याख्या।'),(7544,'3d3b2f53',2685,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  What are its products and importance?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  It involves chlorophyll and takes place in chloroplasts. The products are glucose and oxygen.  Photosynthesis is crucial for the food chain and for the production of oxygen in the atmosphere.'),(7545,'3d3b2f53',2684,'Describe the different types of forces. Give examples of each.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Forces can be classified into various types, including gravitational force (attraction between objects with mass), electromagnetic force (force between charged particles), strong nuclear force (holds protons and neutrons together in the nucleus), and weak nuclear force (involved in radioactive decay). Examples should be provided for each type.'),(7546,'3d3b2f53',2920,'कोई भी पाँच रासायनिक अभिक्रियाएँ लिखिए और उनके प्रकार लिखिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','पाँच रासायनिक अभिक्रियाओं के समीकरण और उनके प्रकार (संयोजन, वियोजन, विस्थापन, द्विविस्थापन, अपघटन)।'),(7547,'3d3b2f53',2917,'न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों को समझाइए और उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों का विस्तृत वर्णन और प्रत्येक नियम के उदाहरण।'),(7548,'3d3b2f53',2686,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Chlorophyll\n2.  Stomata\n3.  Xylem\n4.  Phloem\n\nColumn B\nA.  Transport of water\nB.  Transport of food\nC.  Green pigment\nD.  Tiny pores on leaves','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(7549,'3d3b2f53',2921,'एक छात्र ने एक प्रयोग किया जिसमें उसने एक पेड़ की पत्तियों पर आयोडीन घोल डाला। पत्तियाँ नीली-काली हो गईं।\n(a) इस प्रयोग से क्या निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है?\n(b) पत्तियों में नीली-काली रंग क्यों आया?\n(c) आयोडीन घोल का प्रयोग क्यों किया गया?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) पत्तियों में स्टार्च उपस्थित है।\n(b) आयोडीन स्टार्च के साथ अभिक्रिया करके नीला-काला रंग देता है।\n(c) आयोडीन स्टार्च का पता लगाने के लिए प्रयोग किया जाता है।'),(7550,'231b1591',2906,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा पदार्थ एक यौगिक है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हीलियम\"]','C'),(7551,'231b1591',2911,'मानव शरीर में सबसे बड़ी ग्रंथि कौन सी है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"हृदय\", \"फेफड़े\", \"यकृत\", \"मस्तिष्क\"]','C'),(7552,'231b1591',2907,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया किस अंग में होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जड़\", \"तना\", \"पत्तियाँ\", \"फूल\"]','C'),(7553,'231b1591',2909,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"पानी का उबलना\", \"कागज़ का जलना\", \"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"लोहे का पिघलना\"]','B'),(7554,'231b1591',2674,'Which of the following is NOT a type of tissue?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Epithelial tissue\", \"Connective tissue\", \"Nervous tissue\", \"Photosynthesis\"]','D'),(7555,'231b1591',2675,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(7556,'231b1591',2676,'The force of attraction between any two objects having mass is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(7557,'231b1591',2677,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(7558,'231b1591',2678,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(7559,'231b1591',2683,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart. Draw a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria (receiving chambers) and two ventricles (pumping chambers).  The heart has valves to prevent backflow of blood.  The right side of the heart pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs, and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.  (Diagram should show the four chambers, valves, and major blood vessels).'),(7560,'231b1591',2917,'न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों को समझाइए और उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों का विस्तृत वर्णन और प्रत्येक नियम के उदाहरण।'),(7561,'231b1591',2918,'ध्वनि क्या है? ध्वनि के उत्पन्न होने, संचरण और परावर्तन की व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','ध्वनि की परिभाषा, उत्पन्न होने की प्रक्रिया, संचरण के माध्यम और परावर्तन की व्याख्या।'),(7562,'231b1591',2684,'Describe the different types of forces. Give examples of each.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Forces can be classified into various types, including gravitational force (attraction between objects with mass), electromagnetic force (force between charged particles), strong nuclear force (holds protons and neutrons together in the nucleus), and weak nuclear force (involved in radioactive decay). Examples should be provided for each type.'),(7563,'231b1591',2920,'कोई भी पाँच रासायनिक अभिक्रियाएँ लिखिए और उनके प्रकार लिखिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','पाँच रासायनिक अभिक्रियाओं के समीकरण और उनके प्रकार (संयोजन, वियोजन, विस्थापन, द्विविस्थापन, अपघटन)।'),(7564,'231b1591',2686,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Chlorophyll\n2.  Stomata\n3.  Xylem\n4.  Phloem\n\nColumn B\nA.  Transport of water\nB.  Transport of food\nC.  Green pigment\nD.  Tiny pores on leaves','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(7565,'231b1591',2921,'एक छात्र ने एक प्रयोग किया जिसमें उसने एक पेड़ की पत्तियों पर आयोडीन घोल डाला। पत्तियाँ नीली-काली हो गईं।\n(a) इस प्रयोग से क्या निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है?\n(b) पत्तियों में नीली-काली रंग क्यों आया?\n(c) आयोडीन घोल का प्रयोग क्यों किया गया?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) पत्तियों में स्टार्च उपस्थित है।\n(b) आयोडीन स्टार्च के साथ अभिक्रिया करके नीला-काला रंग देता है।\n(c) आयोडीन स्टार्च का पता लगाने के लिए प्रयोग किया जाता है।'),(7566,'5f01f982',3059,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया कहाँ होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जड़ों में\", \"तनों में\", \"पत्तियों में\", \"फूलों में\"]','C'),(7567,'5f01f982',3224,'प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया में पौधे किस गैस का उपयोग करते हैं?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ऑक्सीजन\", \"नाइट्रोजन\", \"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"हाइड्रोजन\"]','C'),(7568,'5f01f982',3060,'किसी वस्तु का संवेग किसका गुणनफल होता है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"द्रव्यमान और वेग\", \"द्रव्यमान और त्वरण\", \"बल और समय\", \"बल और विस्थापन\"]','A'),(7569,'5f01f982',3266,'पृथ्वी पर गुरुत्वाकर्षण का मान लगभग कितना होता है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"9.8 m/s²\", \"98 m/s²\", \"980 m/s²\", \"0.98 m/s²\"]','A'),(7570,'5f01f982',3203,'ध्वनि किस माध्यम में सबसे तेज गति से चलती है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"वायु\", \"जल\", \"इस्पात\", \"निर्वात\"]','C'),(7571,'5f01f982',3184,'वायुमंडल की सबसे निचली परत ________ कहलाती है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','क्षोभमंडल'),(7572,'5f01f982',3182,'प्रकाश का परावर्तन के नियम ________  है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','दो'),(7573,'5f01f982',3205,'पौधों में जल का परिवहन __________ द्वारा होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जाइलम'),(7574,'5f01f982',3206,'किसी वस्तु का द्रव्यमान उसकी __________ का माप है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','निष्क्रियता'),(7575,'5f01f982',3180,'ऊष्मा का SI मात्रक ________ है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','जूल'),(7576,'5f01f982',3150,'रासायनिक अभिक्रियाओं के प्रकारों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','रासायनिक अभिक्रिया के विभिन्न प्रकारों जैसे संयोजन, वियोजन, विस्थापन, द्विविस्थापन, अपचयन-ऑक्सीकरण आदि का वर्णन करना होगा। उदाहरण सहित स्पष्टीकरण देना आवश्यक है।'),(7577,'5f01f982',3152,'पर्यावरण प्रदूषण के प्रमुख कारण और उसके नियंत्रण के उपायों पर प्रकाश डालिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','वायु, जल और ध्वनि प्रदूषण के मुख्य कारणों और उन्हें कम करने के उपायों का विस्तृत वर्णन करना होगा।'),(7578,'5f01f982',3148,'जीवों में गति के विभिन्न प्रकारों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','जीवों में विभिन्न प्रकार की गतियाँ होती हैं जैसे - पादपों में गति, जन्तुओं में गति, आदि।  उदाहरण सहित वर्णन करना होगा।'),(7579,'5f01f982',3147,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का सचित्र वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र का एक विस्तृत चित्र सहित वर्णन होना चाहिए जिसमें मुँह, ग्रासनली, आमाशय, छोटी आँत, बड़ी आँत, मलाशय और गुदा का उल्लेख हो।'),(7580,'5f01f982',3149,'ऊष्मा स्थानांतरण की विभिन्न विधियों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','ऊष्मा स्थानांतरण की तीन विधियाँ हैं - चालन, संवहन और विकिरण।  इन तीनों को उदाहरण सहित समझाना होगा।'),(7581,'5f01f982',3153,'एक किसान ने अपनी फसल में कीटनाशक का प्रयोग किया। कुछ दिनों बाद उसने देखा कि उसके खेत में पक्षी मर रहे हैं।','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','कीटनाशक के उपयोग से खाद्य श्रृंखला में विषाक्त पदार्थ पहुँचते हैं जिससे उच्च स्तरीय जीवों को नुकसान होता है।'),(7582,'bb88609d',2672,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(7583,'bb88609d',2674,'Which of the following is NOT a type of tissue?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Epithelial tissue\", \"Connective tissue\", \"Nervous tissue\", \"Photosynthesis\"]','D'),(7584,'bb88609d',2908,'बल का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"जूल\", \"वाट\", \"न्यूटन\", \"पास्कल\"]','C'),(7585,'bb88609d',2907,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया किस अंग में होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जड़\", \"तना\", \"पत्तियाँ\", \"फूल\"]','C'),(7586,'bb88609d',2911,'मानव शरीर में सबसे बड़ी ग्रंथि कौन सी है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"हृदय\", \"फेफड़े\", \"यकृत\", \"मस्तिष्क\"]','C'),(7587,'bb88609d',2678,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(7588,'bb88609d',2677,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(7589,'bb88609d',2675,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(7590,'bb88609d',2676,'The force of attraction between any two objects having mass is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(7591,'bb88609d',2685,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  What are its products and importance?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  It involves chlorophyll and takes place in chloroplasts. The products are glucose and oxygen.  Photosynthesis is crucial for the food chain and for the production of oxygen in the atmosphere.'),(7592,'bb88609d',2919,'अम्ल, क्षार और लवण में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए। उदाहरण दीजिये।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','अम्ल, क्षार और लवण की परिभाषा, उनके गुणों में अंतर और उदाहरण।'),(7593,'bb88609d',2684,'Describe the different types of forces. Give examples of each.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Forces can be classified into various types, including gravitational force (attraction between objects with mass), electromagnetic force (force between charged particles), strong nuclear force (holds protons and neutrons together in the nucleus), and weak nuclear force (involved in radioactive decay). Examples should be provided for each type.'),(7594,'bb88609d',2918,'ध्वनि क्या है? ध्वनि के उत्पन्न होने, संचरण और परावर्तन की व्याख्या कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','ध्वनि की परिभाषा, उत्पन्न होने की प्रक्रिया, संचरण के माध्यम और परावर्तन की व्याख्या।'),(7595,'bb88609d',2917,'न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों को समझाइए और उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों का विस्तृत वर्णन और प्रत्येक नियम के उदाहरण।'),(7596,'bb88609d',2686,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Chlorophyll\n2.  Stomata\n3.  Xylem\n4.  Phloem\n\nColumn B\nA.  Transport of water\nB.  Transport of food\nC.  Green pigment\nD.  Tiny pores on leaves','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(7597,'bb88609d',2921,'एक छात्र ने एक प्रयोग किया जिसमें उसने एक पेड़ की पत्तियों पर आयोडीन घोल डाला। पत्तियाँ नीली-काली हो गईं।\n(a) इस प्रयोग से क्या निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है?\n(b) पत्तियों में नीली-काली रंग क्यों आया?\n(c) आयोडीन घोल का प्रयोग क्यों किया गया?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) पत्तियों में स्टार्च उपस्थित है।\n(b) आयोडीन स्टार्च के साथ अभिक्रिया करके नीला-काला रंग देता है।\n(c) आयोडीन स्टार्च का पता लगाने के लिए प्रयोग किया जाता है।'),(7598,'f357861b',2907,'पौधों में प्रकाश संश्लेषण की क्रिया किस अंग में होती है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जड़\", \"तना\", \"पत्तियाँ\", \"फूल\"]','C'),(7599,'f357861b',2908,'बल का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"जूल\", \"वाट\", \"न्यूटन\", \"पास्कल\"]','C'),(7600,'f357861b',2910,'ध्वनि की गति अधिकतम होती है:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"वायु में\", \"जल में\", \"इस्पात में\", \"निर्वात में\"]','C'),(7601,'f357861b',2909,'निम्नलिखित में से कौन सा एक रासायनिक परिवर्तन है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"पानी का उबलना\", \"कागज़ का जलना\", \"बर्फ का पिघलना\", \"लोहे का पिघलना\"]','B'),(7602,'f357861b',2673,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Newton\", \"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Pascal\"]','A'),(7603,'f357861b',2675,'The process of converting light energy into chemical energy is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Photosynthesis'),(7604,'f357861b',2677,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Gene'),(7605,'f357861b',2678,'The smallest particle of an element that can exist independently is called an _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atom'),(7606,'f357861b',2676,'The force of attraction between any two objects having mass is called _____________ .','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gravitation'),(7607,'f357861b',2919,'अम्ल, क्षार और लवण में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए। उदाहरण दीजिये।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','अम्ल, क्षार और लवण की परिभाषा, उनके गुणों में अंतर और उदाहरण।'),(7608,'f357861b',2685,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.  What are its products and importance?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water.  It involves chlorophyll and takes place in chloroplasts. The products are glucose and oxygen.  Photosynthesis is crucial for the food chain and for the production of oxygen in the atmosphere.'),(7609,'f357861b',2916,'मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र बनाइए और इसके विभिन्न अंगों के कार्यों का वर्णन कीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','मानव पाचन तंत्र का नामांकित चित्र और विभिन्न अंगों (मुख, ग्रासनली, आमाशय, छोटी आंत, बड़ी आंत, मलाशय, गुदा) के कार्यों का वर्णन।'),(7610,'f357861b',2683,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart. Draw a labeled diagram.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria (receiving chambers) and two ventricles (pumping chambers).  The heart has valves to prevent backflow of blood.  The right side of the heart pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs, and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.  (Diagram should show the four chambers, valves, and major blood vessels).'),(7611,'f357861b',2917,'न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों को समझाइए और उदाहरण दीजिए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','न्यूटन के गति के तीनों नियमों का विस्तृत वर्णन और प्रत्येक नियम के उदाहरण।'),(7612,'f357861b',2686,'Match the following:\n\nColumn A\n1.  Chlorophyll\n2.  Stomata\n3.  Xylem\n4.  Phloem\n\nColumn B\nA.  Transport of water\nB.  Transport of food\nC.  Green pigment\nD.  Tiny pores on leaves','Matching','Medium',4,'null','1-C, 2-D, 3-A, 4-B'),(7613,'f357861b',2921,'एक छात्र ने एक प्रयोग किया जिसमें उसने एक पेड़ की पत्तियों पर आयोडीन घोल डाला। पत्तियाँ नीली-काली हो गईं।\n(a) इस प्रयोग से क्या निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है?\n(b) पत्तियों में नीली-काली रंग क्यों आया?\n(c) आयोडीन घोल का प्रयोग क्यों किया गया?','Case Study','Hard',5,'null','(a) पत्तियों में स्टार्च उपस्थित है।\n(b) आयोडीन स्टार्च के साथ अभिक्रिया करके नीला-काला रंग देता है।\n(c) आयोडीन स्टार्च का पता लगाने के लिए प्रयोग किया जाता है।'),(7614,'3dfa96fb',2325,'Which gas is responsible for the greenhouse effect?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','C'),(7615,'3dfa96fb',2104,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\"]','C'),(7616,'3dfa96fb',2891,'Which type of lens converges light rays?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Concave lens\", \"Convex lens\", \"Plane lens\", \"None of the above\"]','B'),(7617,'3dfa96fb',2610,'Which of the following is an example of a renewable resource?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Coal\", \"Natural Gas\", \"Solar Energy\", \"Petroleum\"]','C'),(7618,'3dfa96fb',1918,'Which of the following is a chemical change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting of ice\", \"Boiling of water\", \"Rusting of iron\", \"Dissolving sugar in water\"]','C'),(7619,'3dfa96fb',2380,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance but doesn\'t change its chemical composition.  A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance with different properties.'),(7620,'3dfa96fb',2187,'State Ohm\'s Law and write its mathematical expression.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across it, provided the temperature remains constant.  V = IR'),(7621,'3dfa96fb',2089,'What are the three states of matter? Explain the properties of each state.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Solid, liquid, and gas. Solids have a fixed shape and volume. Liquids have a fixed volume but take the shape of their container. Gases have neither fixed shape nor fixed volume.'),(7622,'3dfa96fb',1961,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Respiration is the process of taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. It involves the intake of air into the lungs, diffusion of oxygen into the blood, transport of oxygen to cells, cellular respiration, and the release of carbon dioxide.'),(7623,'3dfa96fb',2357,'Define the term \'Biodiversity\'.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Biodiversity refers to the variety of life on Earth at all its levels, from genes to ecosystems, and the ecological and evolutionary processes that sustain it.'),(7624,'3dfa96fb',2015,'State two differences between mitosis and meiosis.','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','Mitosis produces two identical diploid daughter cells, while meiosis produces four genetically different haploid daughter cells. Mitosis occurs in somatic cells, while meiosis occurs in germ cells.'),(7625,'3dfa96fb',1871,'Explain the different types of chemical reactions with examples.','Long Answer','Medium',4,'null','Different types include combination, decomposition, displacement, double displacement, and redox reactions.  Examples of each should be provided.'),(7626,'3dfa96fb',2437,'Explain the concept of electric current, potential difference, and resistance.  State Ohm\'s law and explain its limitations.','Long Answer','Hard',4,'null','Electric current is the rate of flow of electric charge. Potential difference is the work done per unit charge in moving a charge between two points. Resistance is the opposition to the flow of electric current. Ohm\'s law states that the current is directly proportional to the potential difference, provided the temperature remains constant. Its limitations include non-ohmic conductors and temperature dependence.'),(7627,'3dfa96fb',2726,'Describe the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The human heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body.  It has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  The atria receive blood from the body and lungs, while the ventricles pump blood to the body and lungs.  Valves ensure one-way blood flow.'),(7628,'3dfa96fb',2070,'Explain the structure and function of the human heart.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','The heart is a muscular organ with four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.  It pumps blood throughout the body, delivering oxygen and nutrients. The right side pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs, and the left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body.'),(7629,'3dfa96fb',2047,'Explain the process of photosynthesis and its importance.','Long Answer','Hard',3,'null','A detailed description of the process, including the light-dependent and light-independent reactions, and its importance in providing food and oxygen.'),(7630,'4cfe57d6',2104,'What is the SI unit of force?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Joule\", \"Watt\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\"]','C'),(7631,'4cfe57d6',2419,'Which of the following is NOT a greenhouse gas?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Carbon dioxide\", \"Methane\", \"Oxygen\", \"Nitrous oxide\"]','C'),(7632,'4cfe57d6',2779,'Which of the following is NOT a renewable energy source?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Solar energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Hydro energy\", \"Nuclear energy\"]','D'),(7633,'4cfe57d6',2515,'Which element has the atomic number 6?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Hydrogen\", \"Carbon\", \"Oxygen\", \"Nitrogen\"]','B'),(7634,'4cfe57d6',2735,'What is the chemical formula for water?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"CO2\", \"NaCl\", \"H2O\", \"O2\"]','C'),(7635,'4cfe57d6',2204,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(7636,'4cfe57d6',2253,'Acids turn blue litmus paper _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','red'),(7637,'4cfe57d6',2518,'The basic unit of heredity is called a _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Gene'),(7638,'4cfe57d6',1928,'The basic unit of heredity is the ______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','gene'),(7639,'4cfe57d6',2477,'Describe the structure of an atom.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','An atom consists of a central nucleus containing protons (positively charged) and neutrons (no charge), surrounded by electrons (negatively charged) orbiting in shells or energy levels.'),(7640,'4cfe57d6',1836,'What are the different types of lenses and their uses?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','There are two main types of lenses: convex (converging) and concave (diverging). Convex lenses are used in magnifying glasses, cameras, and eyeglasses for farsightedness. Concave lenses are used in eyeglasses for nearsightedness and telescopes.'),(7641,'4cfe57d6',1852,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light. Explain the phenomenon with a diagram.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to change in speed. (A suitable diagram showing the refraction of light from air to water or glass should be included.)'),(7642,'4cfe57d6',1835,'Explain the process of respiration in humans.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Respiration is the process of exchanging gases between an organism and its environment. In humans, it involves taking in oxygen and releasing carbon dioxide. This process occurs through the lungs, where oxygen from the inhaled air diffuses into the bloodstream and carbon dioxide from the blood diffuses into the air to be exhaled.'),(7643,'4cfe57d6',2774,'Explain the Mendelian laws of inheritance. Give examples.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Mendelian laws of inheritance include the law of segregation and the law of independent assortment.  Explain each law with a suitable example.'),(7644,'4cf018b1',1895,'Which of the following is NOT a type of chemical reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Combination\", \"Decomposition\", \"Displacement\", \"Transpiration\"]','D'),(7645,'4cf018b1',2441,'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of a mammal?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Hair or fur\", \"Give birth to live young\", \"Lay eggs\", \"Mammary glands\"]','C'),(7646,'4cf018b1',2081,'Which type of lens is used to correct myopia?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Convex lens\", \"Concave lens\", \"Plano-convex lens\", \"Plano-concave lens\"]','B'),(7647,'4cf018b1',2939,'मानव शरीर में सबसे बड़ी धमनी कौन सी है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"महाधमनी\", \"शिरा\", \"केशिका\", \"फुफ्फुसीय धमनी\"]','A'),(7648,'4cf018b1',2198,'What is the SI unit of electric current?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Volt\", \"Ampere\", \"Ohm\", \"Watt\"]','B'),(7649,'4cf018b1',2475,'Explain the difference between a physical change and a chemical change.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change alters the form or appearance of a substance without changing its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change involves a change in the chemical composition of a substance, forming new substances (e.g., burning wood).'),(7650,'4cf018b1',1819,'Explain the process of photosynthesis.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods with the help of chlorophyll.  It involves the conversion of carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen using light energy.'),(7651,'4cf018b1',1850,'State Ohm\'s law and write its mathematical expression. Draw a circuit diagram to verify Ohm\'s law.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Ohm\'s law states that the current flowing through a conductor is directly proportional to the potential difference across its ends, provided the temperature and other physical conditions remain constant.  Mathematical expression: V = IR. (A circuit diagram showing a battery, resistor, ammeter, and voltmeter connected in series should be included).'),(7652,'4cf018b1',1849,'Explain the difference between a physical and a chemical change with examples.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','A physical change alters the form of a substance but not its chemical composition (e.g., melting ice). A chemical change results in the formation of new substances with different properties (e.g., burning wood).'),(7653,'4cf018b1',1852,'Define the term \'refraction\' of light. Explain the phenomenon with a diagram.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium to another due to change in speed. (A suitable diagram showing the refraction of light from air to water or glass should be included.)'),(7654,'0ff90b43',3315,'Which of the following reactions is an example of a displacement reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"A. $2H_2 + O_2 \\\\rightarrow 2H_2O$\", \"B. $AgNO_3 + NaCl \\\\rightarrow AgCl + NaNO_3$\", \"C. $Fe + CuSO_4 \\\\rightarrow FeSO_4 + Cu$\", \"D. $CaCO_3 \\\\rightarrow CaO + CO_2$\"]','C'),(7655,'0ff90b43',3316,'Where does the exchange of gases (oxygen and carbon dioxide) primarily occur in the human respiratory system?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"A. Trachea\", \"B. Bronchi\", \"C. Alveoli\", \"D. Pharynx\"]','C'),(7656,'0ff90b43',3317,'An object is placed at the center of curvature (C) of a concave mirror. Where is the image formed?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"A. Between P and F\", \"B. At F\", \"C. Beyond C\", \"D. At C\"]','D'),(7657,'0ff90b43',3318,'Covalent compounds generally have low melting and boiling points because:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"A. They are formed by the transfer of electrons\", \"B. They are highly reactive\", \"C. The intermolecular forces are weak\", \"D. They conduct electricity in solution\"]','C'),(7658,'0ff90b43',3319,'If a dominant trait determines brown eyes (B) and a recessive trait determines blue eyes (b), what proportion of offspring will have blue eyes if a heterozygous brown-eyed parent (Bb) is crossed with a blue-eyed parent (bb)?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"A. 0%\", \"B. 25%\", \"C. 50%\", \"D. 75%\"]','C'),(7659,'0ff90b43',3320,'State the main function of the \'Pupil\' in the human eye.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','The main function of the pupil is to regulate and control the amount of light entering the eye. In bright light, the pupil contracts to reduce light entry, and in dim light, it dilates (opens up) to allow more light to enter.'),(7660,'0ff90b43',3321,'Differentiate between the processes of \'roasting\' and \'calcination\' used in metallurgy, with respect to the presence of air.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Roasting: It is the process of heating an ore (usually sulphide ore) strongly in the presence of excess air. (e.g., $2ZnS + 3O_2 \\rightarrow 2ZnO + 2SO_2$).\nCalcination: It is the process of heating an ore (usually carbonate or hydroxide ore) strongly in the limited supply or absence of air. (e.g., $ZnCO_3 \\rightarrow ZnO + CO_2$).'),(7661,'0ff90b43',3322,'Two resistors, $R_1$ (4 $\\Omega$) and $R_2$ (6 $\\Omega$), are connected in parallel. If the combination is connected to a 12 V battery, calculate the total resistance of the circuit and the current drawn from the battery.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','1. Calculation of Total Resistance ($R_p$):\n$\\frac{1}{R_p} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{6}$\n$\\frac{1}{R_p} = \\frac{3+2}{12} = \\frac{5}{12}$\n$R_p = \\frac{12}{5} = 2.4 \\Omega$\n2. Calculation of Current Drawn ($I$):\nUsing Ohm\'s Law, $I = \\frac{V}{R_p} = \\frac{12 V}{2.4 \\Omega} = 5 A$. \nTotal Resistance = 2.4 $\\Omega$. Current Drawn = 5 A.'),(7662,'0ff90b43',3323,'Write the balanced chemical equations for the reaction of ethanol with: (i) Sodium metal, and (ii) Hot concentrated Sulphuric Acid. Name the products formed in each case.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','(i) Reaction with Sodium metal:\n$2C_2H_5OH + 2Na \\rightarrow 2C_2H_5ONa + H_2$\nProducts: Sodium Ethoxide and Hydrogen gas.\n(ii) Reaction with Hot concentrated Sulphuric Acid (Dehydration):\n$C_2H_5OH \\xrightarrow{Hot\\ Conc.\\ H_2SO_4} C_2H_4 + H_2O$\nProducts: Ethene (or Ethylene) and Water.'),(7663,'0ff90b43',3324,'Give two major advantages of classifying elements in the Periodic Table.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','1. Systematic Study: Classification arranges elements based on similarities in properties, making the study of millions of compounds and individual elements much more systematic, easy, and efficient.\n2. Prediction of Properties: The periodic table allows scientists to predict the properties of elements (especially new or undiscovered ones) based on their position relative to known elements in the same group or period.'),(7664,'55f78d51',3325,'Which of the following processes involves a combination reaction?','MCQ','Easy',2,'[\"Heating Limestone to produce Calcium oxide and Carbon dioxide.\", \"Rusting of iron in the presence of moisture and air.\", \"Decomposition of Silver Chloride into Silver and Chlorine gas.\", \"Neutralization reaction between acid and base.\"]','B'),(7665,'55f78d51',3326,'In the following reaction, identify the reducing agent:\nZnO + C → Zn + CO','MCQ','Medium',2,'[\"ZnO\", \"C\", \"Zn\", \"CO\"]','B'),(7666,'55f78d51',3327,'Balance the following chemical equation and identify the type of reaction:\nFe₂O₃ + Al → Al₂O₃ + Fe','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Balanced Equation: Fe₂O₃ + 2Al → Al₂O₃ + 2Fe.\nType of Reaction: Displacement Reaction. Aluminium is more reactive than Iron, so it displaces Iron from its compound.'),(7667,'55f78d51',3328,'When lead nitrate powder is heated in a test tube, students observe brown fumes being evolved, and a yellow residue remains.\n(a) Name the brown fumes evolved.\n(b) Write the complete balanced chemical equation for the reaction.\n(c) What type of chemical reaction is this?','Short Answer','Hard',4,'null','(a) The brown fumes evolved are Nitrogen Dioxide gas (NO₂).\n(b) 2Pb(NO₃)₂(s) → 2PbO(s) + 4NO₂(g) + O₂(g)\n(c) This is a Thermal Decomposition Reaction (specifically, a decomposition reaction triggered by heat).'),(7668,'493185ea',3329,'Which of the following is an example of a combination reaction?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"2FeSO₄(s) → Fe₂O₃(s) + SO₂(g) + SO₃(g)\", \"Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g)\", \"CaO(s) + H₂O(l) → Ca(OH)₂(aq)\", \"2AgBr(s) → 2Ag(s) + Br₂(g)\"]','C'),(7669,'493185ea',3330,'The power of a lens is -4.0 D. What type of lens is it and what is its focal length?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Convex lens, f = +0.25 m\", \"Concave lens, f = -0.25 m\", \"Convex lens, f = +0.4 m\", \"Concave lens, f = -0.4 m\"]','B'),(7670,'493185ea',3331,'Which process is responsible for the movement of water from the xylem to the surrounding air spaces in the leaf during the day?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Translocation\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Osmosis and diffusion (Transpiration)\", \"Respiration\"]','C'),(7671,'493185ea',3332,'A student tests a solution using universal indicator paper. The paper turns dark purple. Which substance is most likely present in the solution?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Lemon juice (pH ~2)\", \"Vinegar (pH ~3)\", \"Tap water (pH ~7)\", \"Sodium Hydroxide solution (pH ~13-14)\"]','D'),(7672,'493185ea',3333,'Two resistors, R₁ (10 Ω) and R₂ (20 Ω), are first connected in series to a 6V battery, and then connected in parallel to the same battery. What is the ratio of the total current drawn from the battery in the series connection to the parallel connection (I_series : I_parallel)?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"1:3\", \"1:9\", \"3:1\", \"9:1\"]','B'),(7673,'493185ea',3334,'A metallic strip X is dipped into a solution of salt YSO₄. After some time, a new salt solution XSO₄ is formed, and the metal Y is deposited. Based on this observation, answer the following:\n(a) Which metal (X or Y) is more reactive?\n(b) Write a general balanced chemical equation for the reaction.\n(c) What happens if the metallic strip Y is dipped into the salt solution XSO₄? Justify your answer.','Short Answer','Easy',4,'null','(a) Metal X is more reactive.\n(b) X(s) + YSO₄(aq) → XSO₄(aq) + Y(s)\n(c) No reaction will take place. Since X is more reactive than Y, Y cannot displace X from its salt solution (XSO₄).'),(7674,'493185ea',3335,'Explain the significance of the umbilical cord in human embryonic development. List two major functions it performs.','Short Answer','Easy',4,'null','The umbilical cord is a tube-like structure connecting the developing fetus to the placenta, which is attached to the wall of the uterus. It serves as the lifeline between the mother and the embryo.\nFunctions:\n1. Provides Nutrition and Oxygen: It transports essential nutrients (glucose, amino acids) and oxygen from the maternal blood (via the placenta) to the developing fetus.\n2. Removes Waste: It carries metabolic waste products (like urea and carbon dioxide) from the fetal circulation back to the maternal circulation for excretion.'),(7675,'493185ea',3336,'Define magnetic field lines. Why do two magnetic field lines never intersect each other? Illustrate the pattern of magnetic field lines produced by a current-carrying solenoid.','Short Answer','Medium',4,'null','Magnetic field lines are continuous curves used to represent the direction and magnitude of a magnetic field in a region. They emerge from the North pole and merge at the South pole (outside the magnet).\nReason for Non-Intersection: If two magnetic field lines were to intersect at a point, it would imply that at the point of intersection, the compass needle would point in two different directions simultaneously. Since a magnetic field can only have one resultant direction at any given point, intersection is physically impossible.\nSolenoid Pattern: The pattern resembles that of a bar magnet. Inside the solenoid, the field lines are parallel to the axis of the solenoid, indicating a uniform magnetic field. Outside, the lines spread out, forming closed loops from the North pole to the South pole.'),(7676,'493185ea',3337,'Explain the process of formation of micelles when detergent is added to water containing oily dirt. Why are soaps not effective in hard water?','Short Answer','Medium',4,'null','Micelle Formation: Detergents contain long hydrocarbon chains (hydrophobic tail) and ionic ends (hydrophilic head). When mixed with water, the hydrophobic tail clusters towards the oily dirt particle, while the hydrophilic head faces the water. This structure, where the dirt is trapped in the center of a spherical cluster, is called a micelle. The repulsion between the ionic heads stabilizes the emulsion, allowing the dirt to be washed away.\nIneffectiveness in Hard Water: Hard water contains salts of calcium (Ca²⁺) and magnesium (Mg²⁺). Soaps react with these ions to form a white precipitate known as scum (an insoluble compound). This scum separates out, reducing the cleaning action and wasting the soap.'),(7677,'493185ea',3338,'Atomic radii generally decrease across a period and increase down a group in the Modern Periodic Table. Justify these two trends by referring to the change in nuclear charge and the number of shells.','Short Answer','Hard',4,'null','1. Decrease across a Period (L to R): As we move across a period, electrons are added to the same outermost shell. However, the nuclear charge (number of protons) increases progressively. This increased positive charge exerts a stronger pull on the valence electrons, drawing the electron cloud closer to the nucleus, resulting in a decrease in atomic radius.\n2. Increase Down a Group (Top to Bottom): As we move down a group, a new principal energy shell is added at each subsequent period. Although the nuclear charge increases, the effect of the added shells (and increased screening/shielding effect) outweighs the nuclear pull. Since the outermost electrons are significantly further from the nucleus, the atomic radius increases substantially.'),(7678,'926993a2',3339,'Which agricultural practice involves turning and loosening the soil before sowing seeds?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Sowing\", \"Irrigation\", \"Tilling or Ploughing\", \"Harvesting\"]','C'),(7679,'926993a2',3340,'Which among the following is a non-biodegradable material?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Cotton cloth\", \"Paper\", \"Plastic carry bags\", \"Jute rope\"]','C'),(7680,'926993a2',3341,'The force applied by an object perpendicular to a surface is called thrust. Pressure is defined as:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Thrust per unit volume\", \"Thrust per unit area\", \"Force multiplied by area\", \"Force only\"]','B'),(7681,'926993a2',3342,'During the process of electroplating, the object upon which the metal is to be deposited must be connected to which terminal of the battery?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Positive terminal (Anode)\", \"Negative terminal (Cathode)\", \"Electrolyte solution\", \"Neutral terminal\"]','B'),(7682,'926993a2',3343,'Which celestial body is characterized by a highly elliptical orbit around the Sun and develops a bright, long, glowing tail when it approaches the Sun?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"Asteroid\", \"Meteoroid\", \"Comet\", \"Artificial Satellite\"]','C'),(7683,'926993a2',3344,'Define fermentation. Name the microorganism primarily responsible for this process in the making of bread or alcohol.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Fermentation is the process where sugar (like glucose) is converted into alcohol, carbon dioxide, or acid under anaerobic conditions (without oxygen) by microorganisms. The microorganism primarily responsible for fermentation in bread and alcohol production is Yeast.'),(7684,'926993a2',3345,'Distinguish between external fertilization and internal fertilization. Give one specific animal example for each type.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','External fertilization is the fusion of male and female gametes outside the female body, usually in water (Example: Frog or Fish). Internal fertilization is the fusion of male and female gametes inside the female body (Example: Human or Cow).'),(7685,'926993a2',3346,'Give two reasons why metals are generally preferred over non-metals for manufacturing cooking utensils. Additionally, state one reason why the non-metal Carbon (in the form of graphite) is crucial in electrochemical cells.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Reasons for using metals in cooking utensils: 1. They are good conductors of heat, ensuring efficient cooking. 2. They have high melting points, preventing deformation at cooking temperatures (or are highly malleable).\nReason for Carbon (Graphite) in cells: Graphite is a good conductor of electricity, making it suitable for use as an electrode, despite being a non-metal.'),(7686,'926993a2',3347,'Explain the difference between regular reflection and diffused reflection. Which type of reflection allows us to see clear images?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Regular Reflection occurs when parallel rays of light strike a smooth, polished surface and are reflected as parallel rays. Diffused Reflection occurs when parallel rays of light strike a rough or uneven surface and are reflected in different directions (scattered).\nRegular reflection allows us to see clear images because the reflected rays maintain their order and focus.'),(7687,'926993a2',3348,'Describe the main chemical mechanism through which the Ozone layer is depleted. What is one major consequence of Ozone depletion for human health?','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Mechanism: Ozone depletion primarily occurs when compounds like Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) reach the stratosphere. UV radiation breaks down CFCs, releasing highly reactive Chlorine atoms. A single Chlorine atom acts as a catalyst, reacting with and destroying thousands of ozone (O3) molecules.\nConsequence for human health: Increased penetration of harmful Ultraviolet (UV-B) radiation to the Earth\'s surface, leading to a higher incidence of skin cancer, cataracts, and damage to the immune system.'),(7688,'e6efa78d',3349,'Which cell organelle is known as the \'suicidal bag\' of the cell?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Mitochondria\", \"Lysosomes\", \"Ribosomes\", \"Endoplasmic Reticulum\"]','B'),(7689,'e6efa78d',3350,'If an object covers equal distances in equal intervals of time, what type of motion is it exhibiting?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Non-uniform motion\", \"Uniform circular motion\", \"Uniform motion\", \"Accelerated motion\"]','C'),(7690,'e6efa78d',3351,'Which of the following elements has the lowest number of valence electrons?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Oxygen (Z=8)\", \"Neon (Z=10)\", \"Sodium (Z=11)\", \"Chlorine (Z=17)\"]','C'),(7691,'e6efa78d',3352,'What is the physical state of water at 100°C and standard atmospheric pressure?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Only solid\", \"Only liquid\", \"Only gas\", \"Both liquid and gas\"]','D'),(7692,'e6efa78d',3353,'A body is thrown vertically upwards. At the highest point of its trajectory, which of the following is zero?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Acceleration\", \"Momentum\", \"Potential Energy\", \"Kinetic Energy\"]','D'),(7693,'e6efa78d',3354,'Which characteristic is used to primarily classify organisms into Phylum Porifera?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"Presence of coelom\", \"Absence of true tissues/cellular level of organization\", \"Presence of a notochord\", \"Bilateral symmetry\"]','B'),(7694,'e6efa78d',3355,'The property of fluids to flow easily is primarily due to weak forces of attraction between their constituent particles, leading to low ___________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','viscosity'),(7695,'e6efa78d',3356,'The functional group that characterizes an alcohol in organic compounds is the ___________ group.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','hydroxyl (-OH)'),(7696,'e6efa78d',3357,'Differentiate between solutions, suspensions, and colloidal solutions based on particle size and the Tyndall effect.','Short Answer','Medium',4,'null','Solution: Particle size < 1 nm; Does not show Tyndall effect. Suspension: Particle size > 100 nm; Shows Tyndall effect (if transparent, which is rare) and particles settle down. Colloidal Solution: Particle size between 1 nm and 100 nm; Shows Tyndall effect.'),(7697,'e6efa78d',3358,'Define work done by a force. A person carries a load of 15 kg on his head and walks 50 meters on a horizontal road. Calculate the work done by him against gravity. Justify your answer.','Short Answer','Easy',4,'null','Definition: Work is done when a force causes displacement of an object in the direction of the force (W = F × d cos θ). Calculation: Work done = 0 Joules. Justification: Work done against gravity requires displacement in the vertical direction. Since the person walks horizontally (displacement is perpendicular to the force of gravity), the angle (θ) is 90°, and cos 90° = 0. Therefore, W = 0.'),(7698,'e6efa78d',3359,'Explain the significance of the ozone layer in the atmosphere. List two negative effects of its depletion.','Short Answer','Hard',4,'null','Significance: The ozone layer (O3) in the stratosphere shields the Earth\'s surface from harmful high-energy ultraviolet (UV) radiation coming from the sun, preventing damage to living organisms. Effects of Depletion: 1. Increased incidence of skin cancer and cataracts in humans. 2. Damage to plant life and reduction in crop yields; disruption of aquatic ecosystems.'),(7699,'e6efa78d',3360,'a) Define acceleration and derive the second equation of motion graphically. b) Calculate the mass of a body if a force of 10 N causes an acceleration of 2 m/s² in it. (Use Force and Laws of Motion principles).','Long Answer','Medium',7,'null','a) Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity. Derivation of Second Equation (S = ut + 1/2 at^2) requires a velocity-time graph for uniformly accelerated motion. The displacement (S) is calculated as the area under the v-t graph (Area of Rectangle + Area of Triangle). Area = (u * t) + (1/2 * (v-u) * t). Since v-u = at, substituting this yields S = ut + 1/2 at^2. b) According to Newton\'s Second Law, F = m × a. Given F = 10 N, a = 2 m/s². m = F / a = 10 N / 2 m/s² = 5 kg. The mass of the body is 5 kg.'),(7700,'e6efa78d',3361,'a) Explain the term \'Plasmolysis\'. Describe what happens when a plant cell is kept in a hypertonic solution. b) Differentiate between parenchyma and sclerenchyma tissues based on their cell wall, shape, and function.','Long Answer','Hard',7,'null','a) Plasmolysis is the shrinking or contraction of the protoplast (cell contents) away from the cell wall when the cell loses water by osmosis. When a plant cell is kept in a hypertonic solution (higher solute concentration outside the cell), water moves out of the cell due to exosmosis, causing the protoplast to shrink and detach from the rigid cell wall. b) Differentiation:\n| Feature | Parenchyma | Sclerenchyma |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cell Wall | Thin, primary walls (cellulosic) | Thickened by lignin |\n| Shape | Isodiametric, loosely packed | Long, narrow, pointed ends (fibers) or irregular (sclereids) |\n| Function | Storage, Photosynthesis, Packaging | Mechanical strength, support, protection |\n| Nature | Living cells | Dead cells at maturity |'),(7701,'e6efa78d',3362,'a) State the Law of Constant Proportions. If 4 grams of hydrogen react completely with 32 grams of oxygen to form water, how much oxygen is required to react with 6 grams of hydrogen? b) Define mole and calculate the number of moles in 52 grams of Helium (He). (Atomic Mass of He = 4 u).','Long Answer','Easy',7,'null','a) Law of Constant Proportions (Law of Definite Proportions): In a chemical substance, the elements are always present together in fixed proportions by mass. Calculation: Ratio of H:O in water is 4:32 or 1:8 by mass. For 6 grams of hydrogen (H), the required oxygen (O) mass is 6 × 8 = 48 grams. b) Definition: A mole is the amount of substance that contains the same number of particles (atoms, molecules, or ions) as there are atoms in exactly 12 grams of Carbon-12. This number is Avogadro\'s constant (6.022 × 10^23). Calculation: Number of moles = Given mass / Molar mass. Moles = 52 g / 4 g/mol = 13 moles. There are 13 moles in 52 grams of Helium.'),(7702,'a59880c9',3363,'Which of the following processes requires heat energy to be supplied to the substance?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Condensation\", \"Freezing\", \"Evaporation\", \"Deposition\"]','C'),(7703,'a59880c9',3364,'In the context of animal tissues, a tissue responsible for the movement of food in the alimentary canal and movement of iris is:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Striated muscle\", \"Cardiac muscle\", \"Unstriated muscle\", \"Nervous tissue\"]','C'),(7704,'a59880c9',3365,'If an object covers equal distances in equal intervals of time, it is said to be in:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Non-uniform acceleration\", \"Uniform velocity\", \"Non-uniform speed\", \"Variable displacement\"]','B'),(7705,'a59880c9',3366,'The acceleration due to gravity (g) at a specific point above Earth\'s surface depends primarily on:','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"The mass of the falling object\", \"The density of the atmosphere\", \"The mass and radius of the Earth\", \"The presence of vacuum\"]','C'),(7706,'a59880c9',3367,'Which organelle is responsible for synthesizing and secreting enzymes and hormones in eukaryotic cells?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Ribosomes\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Golgi Apparatus\", \"Lysosomes\"]','C'),(7707,'a59880c9',3368,'What is the molecular mass of water (H₂O), given that the atomic masses of Hydrogen (H) and Oxygen (O) are 1 u and 16 u, respectively?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"17 u\", \"18 u\", \"16 u\", \"2 u\"]','B'),(7708,'a59880c9',3369,'In the classification of organisms, \'Monera\' includes organisms that are prokaryotic and fundamentally _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','unicellular'),(7709,'a59880c9',3370,'The rate of doing work is defined as _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Power'),(7710,'a59880c9',3371,'Differentiate between a compound and a mixture based on composition, properties, and separation methods. (Give three points of distinction).','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','1. Composition: Compounds have a fixed composition by mass, while mixtures have a variable composition. \n2. Properties: Compounds exhibit entirely different properties from their constituent elements, while mixtures retain the properties of their components.\n3. Separation: Constituents of a compound can only be separated by chemical or electrochemical reactions, while constituents of a mixture can be separated by physical methods (e.g., filtration, distillation).'),(7711,'a59880c9',3372,'Explain the concept of Isotopes and Isobars. Give one example for each.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Isotopes are atoms of the same element that have the same atomic number (same number of protons) but different mass numbers (different number of neutrons). Example: Carbon-12 and Carbon-14.\nIsobars are atoms of different elements that have the same mass number but different atomic numbers (different number of protons). Example: Argon-40 and Calcium-40.'),(7712,'a59880c9',3373,'What is reverberation? List two measures that can be taken to reduce excessive reverberation in a large hall or auditorium.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Reverberation is the persistence of sound in a large enclosure due to multiple successive reflections from surfaces like walls, ceilings, and floors.\nMeasures to reduce reverberation:\n1. Using sound-absorbing materials (like fiberboard, rough plaster, or acoustic tiles) on walls and ceilings.\n2. Installing heavy curtains or using seat materials that absorb sound energy.'),(7713,'a59880c9',3374,'Describe the structural differences between a typical plant cell and a typical animal cell. Draw a neat labelled diagram of a plant cell to illustrate these differences.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Differences:\n1. Cell Wall: Plant cells possess a rigid cell wall outside the cell membrane; Animal cells lack a cell wall.\n2. Plastids (Chloroplasts): Plant cells generally contain chloroplasts for photosynthesis; Animal cells lack plastids.\n3. Vacuole: Plant cells usually have a large central vacuole (occupying 50% to 90% of cell volume); Animal cells either lack vacuoles or have small, temporary vacuoles.\n4. Centrosome/Centrioles: Animal cells have centrosomes and centrioles (important for cell division); Plant cells usually lack centrioles.\n(Diagram required showing cell wall, large central vacuole, and chloroplasts in the plant cell.)'),(7714,'a59880c9',3375,'A body of mass 5 kg is accelerated uniformly from an initial velocity of 10 m/s to a final velocity of 20 m/s in 5 seconds. Calculate the magnitude of the force required to achieve this acceleration. State the law of motion used in this calculation.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The law of motion used is Newton’s Second Law of Motion (Force is proportional to the rate of change of momentum).\nGiven: Mass (m) = 5 kg; Initial velocity (u) = 10 m/s; Final velocity (v) = 20 m/s; Time (t) = 5 s.\nStep 1: Calculate acceleration (a).\na = (v - u) / t \na = (20 m/s - 10 m/s) / 5 s = 10 / 5 m/s² = 2 m/s².\nStep 2: Calculate Force (F).\nF = m × a\nF = 5 kg × 2 m/s²\nF = 10 N.\nTherefore, the magnitude of the force required is 10 Newtons.'),(7715,'a59880c9',3376,'Rutherford\'s alpha-particle scattering experiment was a landmark achievement, but his model had significant drawbacks. Explain the observation and conclusion of Rutherford\'s experiment, and detail the major limitation of his Atomic Model.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Experiment Observation & Conclusion:\nObservation: Most alpha particles passed straight through the gold foil undeflected. A small fraction deflected at small angles. Very few (about 1 in 12,000) rebounded, showing deflection of 180 degrees.\nConclusion:\n1. Most of the atom is empty space (from undeflected particles).\n2. The positive charge and most of the mass of the atom are concentrated in a very small region called the nucleus (from large-angle deflections).\nMajor Limitation of Rutherford\'s Model:\nClassical physics predicts that an electron, moving in a circular orbit around the nucleus (as proposed by Rutherford), must continuously accelerate. An accelerating charged particle should continuously radiate energy. If the electron continuously loses energy, its path should spiral inwards, leading to the collapse of the atom into the nucleus in a fraction of a second. This contradicts the stability of matter, which Rutherford\'s model failed to explain.'),(7716,'57c5376d',3377,'The phenomenon of change of liquid into vapour at any temperature below its boiling point is called:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Condensation\", \"Fusion\", \"Evaporation\", \"Sublimation\"]','C'),(7717,'57c5376d',3378,'Which of the following represents a heterogeneous mixture?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Salt dissolved in water\", \"Brass\", \"Tincture of Iodine\", \"Smoke\"]','D'),(7718,'57c5376d',3379,'Which cell organelle is responsible for synthesizing lipids and detoxifying drugs?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum\", \"Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Lysosomes\"]','B'),(7719,'57c5376d',3380,'If the velocity of an object changes uniformly from 20 m/s to 40 m/s in 5 seconds, what is its acceleration?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"4 m/s²\", \"12 m/s²\", \"8 m/s²\", \"2 m/s²\"]','A'),(7720,'57c5376d',3381,'Calculate the number of moles in 88 grams of CO₂ (Atomic mass C=12 u, O=16 u).','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"1 mole\", \"2 moles\", \"4 moles\", \"0.5 moles\"]','B'),(7721,'57c5376d',3382,'The group of organisms that have naked seeds are known as:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Pteridophyta\", \"Angiosperms\", \"Thallophyta\", \"Gymnosperms\"]','D'),(7722,'57c5376d',3383,'Which type of tissue is responsible for movement in our body?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Nervous tissue\", \"Epithelial tissue\", \"Muscular tissue\", \"Connective tissue\"]','C'),(7723,'57c5376d',3384,'The SI unit of universal gravitational constant (G) is ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Nm²kg⁻²'),(7724,'57c5376d',3385,'Sound travels fastest in ________ media and slowest in ________ media.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','solid, gaseous'),(7725,'57c5376d',3386,'The technique used to separate butter from curd is called ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Centrifugation'),(7726,'57c5376d',3387,'When an electron jumps from a higher energy level to a lower energy level, the atom ________ energy.','Fill in the Blanks','Hard',1,'null','releases (or emits)'),(7727,'57c5376d',3388,'The natural process by which Nitrogen gas is converted into usable forms like nitrates is known as ________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Nitrogen fixation'),(7728,'57c5376d',3389,'Define power. A man does 500 J of work in 10 seconds. Calculate the power developed by him.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Power is defined as the rate of doing work or the rate of transfer of energy. Mathematically, Power (P) = Work done (W) / Time taken (t).\nCalculation: P = 500 J / 10 s = 50 Watts.'),(7729,'57c5376d',3390,'State the key differences between Parenchyma and Sclerenchyma plant tissues based on cell wall composition and function.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Parenchyma:\n1. Cell wall: Thin, made up of cellulose.\n2. Function: Storage of food, providing temporary support, photosynthesis.\nSclerenchyma:\n1. Cell wall: Thickened, due to the deposition of lignin, making it dead.\n2. Function: Provides mechanical strength and rigidity to the plant.'),(7730,'57c5376d',3391,'Why does the temperature of a substance remain constant during the change of state, such as melting?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','During the change of state (e.g., solid melting into liquid), the heat energy supplied is utilized entirely to overcome the forces of attraction between the particles of the substance. This energy, known as Latent Heat of Fusion, does not increase the kinetic energy of the particles, thus the temperature remains constant until all the substance has changed state.'),(7731,'57c5376d',3392,'State any three major conclusions drawn by Rutherford from his alpha-particle scattering experiment.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','1. Most of the space inside the atom is empty because most alpha particles passed straight through the gold foil.\n2. There is a small, dense, positively charged center in the atom called the nucleus, which deflected a few alpha particles.\n3. The size of the nucleus is very small compared to the size of the atom, as only a very few particles (1 in 12,000) bounced back.'),(7732,'57c5376d',3393,'A body starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 0.5 m/s² for 10 seconds. Calculate the distance covered by the body in this time.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Given: Initial velocity (u) = 0 m/s (starts from rest), Acceleration (a) = 0.5 m/s², Time (t) = 10 s.\nUsing the second equation of motion: S = ut + (1/2)at².\nS = (0 * 10) + (1/2) * (0.5) * (10)²\nS = 0 + (1/2) * 0.5 * 100\nS = 0.5 * 50\nS = 25 meters.\nThe distance covered is 25 meters.'),(7733,'57c5376d',3394,'Why is the classification of organisms considered to be a continuous, evolving process rather than a fixed one? Give one example of an ambiguity in classification.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Classification is continuous and evolving because scientific understanding of evolutionary relationships (phylogeny) constantly improves through new genetic and molecular data. Older systems based only on morphology are often revised when closer links are discovered, leading to adjustments in hierarchies.\nExample of ambiguity: Viruses are acellular and do not fit neatly into any kingdom, blurring the line between living and non-living.'),(7734,'57c5376d',3395,'Draw a neat labelled diagram of a plant cell. Describe the functions of the Cell Wall and the Vacuole in plant cells.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','The answer requires a diagram of a plant cell clearly labelling at least 6 components (e.g., cell wall, cell membrane, nucleus, vacuole, chloroplast, cytoplasm).\nFunctions:\n1. Cell Wall: Provides structural strength and protection to the cell. It maintains the cell\'s shape and prevents the cell from bursting when absorbing water (turgidity).\n2. Vacuole: Stores sap, providing turgidity to the cell. It stores amino acids, sugars, and organic acids, and helps in waste management. In plant cells, vacuoles are typically large and central.'),(7735,'57c5376d',3396,'State the Law of Conservation of Mass. In a chemical reaction, 4.9 g of Potassium Chlorate (KClO₃) was heated to produce 2.96 g of Potassium Chloride (KCl) and Oxygen gas. Calculate the mass of Oxygen gas produced. Which fundamental law of chemistry supports your calculation?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Law of Conservation of Mass: Mass can neither be created nor destroyed in a chemical reaction. The total mass of reactants must equal the total mass of products.\nCalculation:\nMass of Reactant (KClO₃) = 4.9 g\nMass of Products = Mass of KCl + Mass of O₂\n4.9 g = 2.96 g + Mass of O₂\nMass of O₂ = 4.9 g - 2.96 g = 1.94 g.\nMass of Oxygen gas produced is 1.94 g.\nThis calculation is supported by the Law of Conservation of Mass.'),(7736,'57c5376d',3397,'Define acceleration due to gravity (g). How does the value of \'g\' change when an object is taken to the surface of the moon? Explain the difference between mass and weight.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Acceleration due to gravity (g) is the acceleration gained by an object because of gravitational force. On Earth\'s surface, g ≈ 9.8 m/s².\nChange in \'g\' on the moon: The value of \'g\' on the Moon is significantly less than on Earth, approximately one-sixth (1/6) of the Earth\'s value, because the Moon has a much smaller mass and radius.\nDifference between Mass and Weight:\n1. Mass: It is the measure of the amount of matter contained in an object. It is a scalar quantity and remains constant everywhere.\n2. Weight: It is the force with which a body is attracted towards the center of the Earth (W = mg). It is a vector quantity and varies with the value of \'g\' (location).'),(7737,'57c5376d',3398,'Derive the mathematical formula for Newton\'s Second Law of Motion. Using this derivation, define the SI unit of force.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Derivation:\nNewton\'s Second Law states that the rate of change of momentum (p) of an object is proportional to the applied unbalanced force (F) in the direction of the force.\n1. Momentum, p = mv.\n2. Change in momentum: Δp = final momentum - initial momentum = mv - mu = m(v - u).\n3. Rate of change of momentum: F ∝ m(v - u) / t.\n4. Since acceleration a = (v - u) / t, we get F ∝ ma.\n5. Introducing the proportionality constant k, F = kma. By defining the unit of force such that k=1, we get F = ma.\nDefinition of SI Unit of Force (Newton, N):\nOne Newton (1 N) is defined as the amount of force required to produce an acceleration of 1 m/s² in an object of mass 1 kg. (1 N = 1 kg⋅m/s²).'),(7738,'57c5376d',3399,'Differentiate between solutions, suspensions, and colloids based on three parameters: visibility, stability, and filtration.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','Differences based on particle characteristics:\n| Feature | True Solution | Suspension | Colloid |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Visibility/Particle Size** | Particles < 1 nm; invisible to naked eye/microscope. | Particles > 100 nm; visible to naked eye. | Particles between 1 nm and 100 nm; invisible to naked eye but scatter light (Tyndall effect). |\n| **Stability** | Highly stable; particles do not settle on standing. | Unstable; particles settle down after some time. | Quite stable; particles do not settle down. |\n| **Filtration** | Cannot be separated by filtration or ultra-filtration. | Can be separated by filtration. | Cannot be separated by filtration, but can be separated by centrifugation or ultra-filtration. |'),(7739,'57c5376d',3400,'Read the following passage and answer the questions:\nThe atmosphere acts as the major reservoir of Nitrogen, containing approximately 78% N₂. However, most organisms cannot utilize atmospheric nitrogen directly. This nitrogen must be \'fixed\' or converted into usable inorganic compounds like nitrates or ammonia by specific organisms, often bacteria (like Rhizobium in leguminous plants or free-living bacteria). This fixed nitrogen is then taken up by plants. Consumers then obtain nitrogen by feeding on plants. When organisms die or excrete waste, decomposers return the nitrogen back to the soil. Finally, certain bacteria convert nitrates back into atmospheric N₂ completing the cycle.','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','A. Rhizobium (or nitrogen-fixing bacteria).\nB. They convert the atmospheric N₂ into usable inorganic forms like ammonia, nitrites, or nitrates, which plants can absorb.\nC. Decomposers (bacteria and fungi).\nD. Denitrification.'),(7740,'57c5376d',3401,'A student observed a permanent slide under a microscope showing plant cells that were small, actively dividing, and lacked large vacuoles. In contrast, another slide showed large, specialized cells with thick or thin walls that performed specific functions like photosynthesis or storage, but did not divide.','Case Study','Easy',4,'null','A. Meristematic tissue.\nB. Meristematic tissues are responsible for growth, as they actively divide, increasing the length and girth of the plant.\nC. Xylem and Phloem (or Parenchyma, Collenchyma, Sclerenchyma).\nD. Dedifferentiation.'),(7741,'2b33fe4d',3402,'The phenomenon of change of liquid into vapour at any temperature below its boiling point is called:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Condensation\", \"Sublimation\", \"Evaporation\", \"Fusion\"]','C'),(7742,'2b33fe4d',3403,'Which organelle is known as the \'Powerhouse of the cell\'?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Ribosome\", \"Lysosome\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Endoplasmic Reticulum\"]','C'),(7743,'2b33fe4d',3404,'What is the chemical formula for Sodium Oxide?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"NaO\", \"Na₂O\", \"SO₂\", \"Na(OH)₂\"]','B'),(7744,'2b33fe4d',3405,'Which of the following units is used to measure acceleration?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"m/s\", \"m²\", \"m/s²\", \"N\"]','C'),(7745,'2b33fe4d',3406,'Which level of classification includes organisms that share the least common characteristics?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Species\", \"Phylum\", \"Genus\", \"Kingdom\"]','D'),(7746,'2b33fe4d',3407,'The tissue responsible for the transportation of food from leaves to other parts of the plant is:','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"Xylem\", \"Parenchyma\", \"Phloem\", \"Collenchyma\"]','C'),(7747,'2b33fe4d',3408,'The commercial unit of energy is the  ____________________.','Fill in the Blanks','Hard',1,'null','kilowatt-hour (kWh)'),(7748,'2b33fe4d',3409,'The number of protons in the nucleus of an atom is called its ____________________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Atomic Number (Z)'),(7749,'2b33fe4d',3410,'The unit used to measure the frequency of a sound wave is ____________________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Hertz (Hz)'),(7750,'2b33fe4d',3411,'In the process of respiration, glucose is broken down in the presence of oxygen to release energy. This is an example of a ____________________ change.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Chemical'),(7751,'2b33fe4d',3412,'The property of matter that resists a change in its state of motion or rest is called ____________________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Inertia'),(7752,'2b33fe4d',3413,'A solution that uniformly shows the Tyndall effect is commonly identified as a ____________________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Colloid (or Colloidal Solution)'),(7753,'2b33fe4d',3414,'Differentiate between Mass and Weight. List two points of distinction.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Mass: 1. It is the measure of the quantity of matter contained in a body. 2. It is a scalar quantity. 3. Its value remains constant everywhere in the universe. 4. Its SI unit is kilogram (kg).\n\nWeight: 1. It is the force with which a body is attracted towards the center of the Earth (W=mg). 2. It is a vector quantity. 3. Its value varies from place to place (due to changes in \'g\'). 4. Its SI unit is Newton (N).'),(7754,'2b33fe4d',3415,'How would you separate a mixture of salt and ammonium chloride? Explain the process with a reason.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','The mixture can be separated using the process of Sublimation. Ammonium chloride is a sublime substance, meaning it changes directly from solid to gaseous state upon heating without passing through the liquid state. Salt (Sodium Chloride) does not sublime.\nProcess: The mixture is heated in a china dish covered by an inverted funnel with a cotton plug. Ammonium chloride vaporizes and solidifies on the cooler walls of the funnel (sublimate), while the salt remains in the china dish.'),(7755,'2b33fe4d',3416,'Why is the plasma membrane called a selectively permeable membrane? State the two main components of the plasma membrane.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','The plasma membrane is called a selectively permeable membrane because it allows the entry and exit of some materials in and out of the cell, while preventing the passage of other materials. This mechanism ensures the cell maintains its internal composition.\n\nTwo main components of the plasma membrane are: 1. Lipids (specifically phospholipids forming a bilayer). 2. Proteins (embedded or peripheral).'),(7756,'2b33fe4d',3417,'Identify and explain the function of the three types of plant meristematic tissues.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','The three types of meristematic tissues are:\n1. Apical Meristem: Found at the growing tips of roots and stems. Function: Responsible for increasing the length (primary growth) of the plant.\n2. Intercalary Meristem: Located at the base of leaves or internodes. Function: Responsible for growth in length of the stem and fixing parts removed by grazing animals.\n3. Lateral Meristem (Cambium): Found along the sides of the stem and root. Function: Responsible for increasing the girth or diameter (secondary growth) of the plant.'),(7757,'2b33fe4d',3418,'Derive the second equation of motion, s = ut + ½at², using the graphical method (velocity-time graph).','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Let \'u\' be the initial velocity and \'v\' be the final velocity of an object moving with uniform acceleration \'a\' in time \'t\'. The distance \'s\' travelled is represented by the area under the velocity-time graph.\n\nDistance (s) = Area of OABD (Trapezium)\nArea OABD = Area of Rectangle OACD + Area of Triangle ABC\nArea OACD = Length × Breadth = OA × OD = u × t = ut\nArea ABC = ½ × Base × Height = ½ × AC × BC\nFrom the graph, AC = OD = t.\nAnd BC = BD - CD = v - u\nWe know from the first equation: v = u + at, so (v - u) = at.\nArea ABC = ½ × t × (at) = ½at²\n\nTherefore, s = Area OACD + Area ABC = ut + ½at².'),(7758,'2b33fe4d',3419,'An element X has a mass number of 35 and contains 18 neutrons. Write the electronic configuration and determine the valency of X. (Assume neutral atom).','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','1. Determine Atomic Number (Z):\nAtomic Number (Z) = Mass Number (A) - Number of Neutrons (n)\nZ = 35 - 18 = 17.\nElement X is Chlorine (Cl).\n\n2. Electronic Configuration:\nSince Z=17, the atom has 17 electrons. The configuration is filled according to the Bohr-Bury scheme (2, 8, 7).\n\n3. Valency:\nValency is the combining capacity. X has 7 electrons in its outermost shell (valence shell). To achieve a stable octet (8 electrons), it needs to gain 1 electron.\nValency = 8 - 7 = 1. (It has a valency of 1).'),(7759,'2b33fe4d',3420,'Draw a neat, labeled diagram of a typical Plant Cell. List three key features that distinguish a plant cell from an animal cell.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','Diagram: (A typical plant cell diagram must be drawn showing the cell wall, plasma membrane, large central vacuole, nucleus, mitochondria, chloroplasts, and cytoplasm).\n\nDistinguishing Features:\n1. Cell Wall: Plant cells possess a rigid outer cell wall made of cellulose; animal cells lack a cell wall.\n2. Plastids (Chloroplasts): Plant cells generally contain chloroplasts for photosynthesis; animal cells do not.\n3. Vacuole: Plant cells usually have a large central vacuole occupying 50% to 90% of the cell volume; animal cells have much smaller or absent vacuoles.\n(Alternative: Plant cells lack centrioles found in animal cells).'),(7760,'2b33fe4d',3421,'State Newton’s Universal Law of Gravitation. If the distance between two objects is tripled, how does the force of gravitation between them change? Derive the relationship between force (F), masses (M and m), and distance (d).','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Newton’s Universal Law of Gravitation states that every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force which is directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.\n\nDerivation:\n1. F ∝ M × m (Force is proportional to the product of masses)\n2. F ∝ 1/d² (Force is inversely proportional to the square of the distance)\nCombining (1) and (2):\nF ∝ (M × m) / d²\nF = G (M × m) / d²\nWhere G is the Universal Gravitational Constant.\n\nEffect of Tripling Distance:\nIf the new distance d\' = 3d, the new force F\' will be:\nF\' = G (M × m) / (3d)²\nF\' = G (M × m) / 9d²\nF\' = (1/9) × [G (M × m) / d²]\nF\' = F / 9\nConclusion: If the distance is tripled, the gravitational force reduces to one-ninth (1/9th) of the original force.'),(7761,'2b33fe4d',3422,'Define Kinetic Energy and Potential Energy. A body of mass 10 kg is lifted to a height of 5 m. Calculate the potential energy gained by the body. (Take g = 9.8 m/s²).','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','1. Kinetic Energy (KE): The energy possessed by an object due to its motion. Formula: KE = ½mv².\n2. Potential Energy (PE): The energy possessed by an object due to its position or change in shape. Gravitational Potential Energy Formula: PE = mgh.\n\nCalculation:\nGiven: Mass (m) = 10 kg\nHeight (h) = 5 m\nAcceleration due to gravity (g) = 9.8 m/s²\n\nPotential Energy (PE) = m × g × h\nPE = 10 kg × 9.8 m/s² × 5 m\nPE = 490 J\n\nAnswer: The potential energy gained by the body is 490 Joules.'),(7762,'2b33fe4d',3423,'State the Law of Conservation of Momentum. Explain this law by deriving the final velocity of a bullet fired from a gun (recoil velocity).','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Law of Conservation of Momentum: When two or more bodies act upon one another, their total momentum remains constant, provided no external force is acting on them.\n\nDerivation (Recoil of Gun):\nConsider a gun (mass Mᵧ, initial velocity uᵧ=0) and a bullet (mass Mᵦ, initial velocity uᵦ=0).\nTotal momentum before firing (Pᵢ) = Mᵧuᵧ + Mᵦuᵦ = Mᵧ(0) + Mᵦ(0) = 0.\n\nAfter firing, the gun moves backward with velocity Vᵧ (recoil velocity), and the bullet moves forward with velocity Vᵦ.\nTotal momentum after firing (Pᶠ) = MᵧVᵧ + MᵦVᵦ.\n\nBy the Law of Conservation of Momentum:\nPᵢ = Pᶠ\n0 = MᵧVᵧ + MᵦVᵦ\n\nRearranging to find the recoil velocity of the gun (Vᵧ):\nMᵧVᵧ = - MᵦVᵦ\nVᵧ = - (MᵦVᵦ) / Mᵧ\n\nThe negative sign indicates that the recoil velocity (Vᵧ) is in the opposite direction to the bullet’s velocity (Vᵦ). The gun recoils because the momentum gained by the bullet must be equal and opposite to the momentum gained by the gun, ensuring total momentum remains zero.'),(7763,'2b33fe4d',3424,'a) Define the Mole concept. \nb) Calculate the number of molecules present in 11.2 L of Carbon Dioxide (CO₂) gas at STP. \nc) What is the mass of 0.5 mole of water (H₂O)? (Atomic masses: C=12 u, O=16 u, H=1 u).','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','a) Mole Concept: A mole is defined as the amount of substance that contains the same number of particles (atoms, molecules, or ions) as there are atoms in exactly 12 grams of the carbon-12 isotope. This number is Avogadro’s number (N₀), approximately 6.022 × 10²³.\n\nb) Calculation of Molecules in 11.2 L CO₂ at STP:\nWe know that 1 mole of any gas at STP occupies 22.4 L and contains N₀ molecules.\nGiven Volume = 11.2 L.\nNumber of moles = 11.2 L / 22.4 L/mol = 0.5 moles.\nNumber of molecules = Moles × Avogadro’s number\nNumber of molecules = 0.5 × 6.022 × 10²³ = 3.011 × 10²³ molecules.\n\nc) Mass of 0.5 mole of water (H₂O):\nMolar mass of H₂O = (2 × Molar mass of H) + (1 × Molar mass of O)\nMolar mass of H₂O = (2 × 1 u) + (1 × 16 u) = 18 g/mol.\nMass = Number of moles × Molar mass\nMass = 0.5 mol × 18 g/mol = 9.0 g.\nAnswer: The mass of 0.5 mole of water is 9.0 grams.'),(7764,'2b33fe4d',3425,'Explain the major causes and resulting effects of Acid Rain and Ozone layer depletion. How do these environmental issues threaten biodiversity and natural resources?','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','A) Acid Rain:\nCauses: Release of Sulphur Dioxide (SO₂) and Nitrogen Oxides (NOₓ) into the atmosphere, primarily from burning fossil fuels in power plants and vehicles. These gases react with water vapor to form sulfuric acid and nitric acid.\nEffects:\n1. Damage to Infrastructure: Corrosion of buildings, statues (especially marble).\n2. Aquatic Life: Lowers the pH of lakes and rivers, making them unsuitable for aquatic organisms.\n3. Soil and Vegetation: Leaches essential nutrients from the soil, damaging forests and crops.\n\nB) Ozone Layer Depletion:\nCauses: Release of synthetic chemicals, mainly Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) used in refrigerators, air conditioners, and fire extinguishers, which rise to the stratosphere and break down ozone (O₃) molecules.\nEffects:\n1. Health Risks: Increased incidence of skin cancer, cataracts, and immune system damage in humans due to higher UV-B radiation exposure.\n2. Ecosystem Damage: Harm to phytoplankton (base of the marine food chain) and reduced crop yields.\n\nThreat to Biodiversity and Natural Resources: Both phenomena lead to the destruction of habitats (due to acidification or increased UV radiation), altering ecological balances, leading to the extinction of sensitive species, and contaminating water resources.'),(7765,'5a10a3a0',3426,'Which of the following processes requires heat energy to be released?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Sublimation\", \"Fusion\", \"Condensation\", \"Vaporization\"]','C'),(7766,'5a10a3a0',3427,'If an element has atomic number 12 and mass number 24, how many neutrons does it possess?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"12\", \"24\", \"6\", \"36\"]','A'),(7767,'5a10a3a0',3428,'The cell organelle responsible for detoxifying poisons and drugs in liver cells is the:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum (RER)\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum (SER)\", \"Golgi Apparatus\"]','C'),(7768,'5a10a3a0',3429,'Which quantity remains constant when a body is falling freely under gravity?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Velocity\", \"Acceleration\", \"Potential Energy\", \"Kinetic Energy\"]','B'),(7769,'5a10a3a0',3430,'Which phylum is characterized by having jointed appendages and segmented bodies?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"Mollusca\", \"Annelida\", \"Arthropoda\", \"Platyhelminthes\"]','C'),(7770,'5a10a3a0',3431,'The intensity of sound is measured in units of:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Hertz (Hz)\", \"Metres per second (m/s)\", \"Decibel (dB)\", \"Joule (J)\"]','C'),(7771,'5a10a3a0',3432,'The movement of water molecules through a selectively permeable membrane is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Osmosis'),(7772,'5a10a3a0',3433,'A substance that contains only one type of particle (atoms or molecules) is known as a _______________ substance.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Pure'),(7773,'5a10a3a0',3434,'The tendency of an object to resist changes in its state of motion or rest is called _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Inertia'),(7774,'5a10a3a0',3435,'The formula unit mass of $NaCl$ is calculated using the atomic masses of $Na$ (23 u) and $Cl$ (35.5 u), resulting in _______________ u.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','58.5'),(7775,'5a10a3a0',3436,'The permanent tissue responsible for providing flexibility to plant parts, like leaf stalks, is _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Collenchyma'),(7776,'5a10a3a0',3437,'The Earth is divided into major spheres: the atmosphere, the hydrosphere, and the _______________.','Fill in the Blanks','Hard',1,'null','Lithosphere'),(7777,'5a10a3a0',3438,'Why is the nucleus called the functional center of the cell? List two main functions of the nucleus.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','The nucleus is called the functional center of the cell because it houses the genetic material (chromosomes) which directs and controls all cellular activities, including protein synthesis and cell division.\nFunctions:\n1. Controlling all metabolic activities of the cell.\n2. Storing and transmitting hereditary information (DNA) to the next generation of cells.'),(7778,'5a10a3a0',3439,'Define potential energy and derive the expression for the potential energy of an object of mass \'m\' raised to a height \'h\'.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Potential energy is the energy possessed by an object due to its position or change in shape. \nDerivation:\nWork done (W) in lifting the object = Force (F) × displacement (h).\nSince the object is lifted against gravity, the force required F = mg.\nTherefore, W = mgh.\nThis work done is stored in the object as Gravitational Potential Energy (PE). Hence, PE = mgh.'),(7779,'5a10a3a0',3440,'State the key differences between Parenchyma and Sclerenchyma tissues in plants.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','1. Nature of Cells: Parenchyma cells are generally living; Sclerenchyma cells are dead.\n2. Cell Walls: Parenchyma cell walls are thin and uniformly thickened; Sclerenchyma cell walls are thick due to lignin deposition.\n3. Function: Parenchyma primarily functions in storage and photosynthesis; Sclerenchyma provides mechanical strength and hardness.'),(7780,'5a10a3a0',3441,'A solution contains 30g of sugar dissolved in 370g of water. Calculate the concentration of the solution in terms of mass percentage.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Mass of solute (sugar) = 30 g.\nMass of solvent (water) = 370 g.\nTotal mass of solution = 30 g + 370 g = 400 g.\nConcentration (Mass %) = (Mass of Solute / Mass of Solution) × 100\nConcentration = (30 g / 400 g) × 100\nConcentration = 0.075 × 100 = 7.5%'),(7781,'5a10a3a0',3442,'Derive the first equation of motion ($v = u + at$) using the graphical method.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Consider a velocity-time graph for an object moving with uniform acceleration \'a\'. The initial velocity is \'u\' (point A) and the final velocity is \'v\' after time \'t\' (point B).\nAcceleration (a) is defined as the slope of the v-t graph.\n$a = \\text{Change in velocity} / \\text{Time taken}$\n$a = (BD - CD) / AD$\n$a = (v - u) / t$\nRearranging the equation: $at = v - u$\nTherefore, $v = u + at$.'),(7782,'5a10a3a0',3443,'Define isotopes and isobars. Give one example of each.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','1. Isotopes: Atoms of the same element that have the same atomic number but different mass numbers (due to different numbers of neutrons).\nExample: Carbon-12 and Carbon-14.\n2. Isobars: Atoms of different elements that have the same mass number but different atomic numbers.\nExample: Argon-40 and Calcium-40.'),(7783,'5a10a3a0',3444,'Explain the three states of matter (Solid, Liquid, Gas) based on their particle arrangement, kinetic energy, and intermolecular forces of attraction.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','1. Solids: \n	Particle Arrangement: Particles are closely packed in fixed positions.\n	Intermolecular Forces: Very strong, holding particles tightly.\n	Kinetic Energy: Minimum. Particles only vibrate about their mean positions.\n2. Liquids: \n	Particle Arrangement: Particles are close together but are not in fixed positions and can slide past each other.\n	Intermolecular Forces: Moderate, weaker than solids but strong enough to keep the volume fixed.\n	Kinetic Energy: Moderate. Particles move randomly.\n3. Gases: \n	Particle Arrangement: Particles are far apart from each other.\n	Intermolecular Forces: Negligible/Very weak.\n	Kinetic Energy: Maximum. Particles move randomly and rapidly.'),(7784,'5a10a3a0',3445,'Describe the structure and function of the Plasma Membrane. Why is it called a selectively permeable membrane?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Structure: The plasma membrane is the outer covering of the cell. It is made up primarily of organic molecules like lipids and proteins. It is typically a fluid mosaic structure, consisting of a lipid bilayer in which protein molecules are embedded.\nFunction:\n1. Separates the cell contents from the external environment.\n2. Protects the cell and gives it shape.\n3. Regulates the movement of substances (entry and exit) into and out of the cell.\nSelectively Permeable: It is called selectively permeable (or semi-permeable) because it allows only certain molecules to pass through it, while preventing the passage of others. It controls which materials enter and leave the cell, maintaining the cell’s internal environment.'),(7785,'5a10a3a0',3446,'State Newton’s Law of Universal Gravitation. Based on this law, explain why the value of acceleration due to gravity (g) is greater at the poles than at the equator.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Newton’s Law of Universal Gravitation states that every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force that is directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between their centers.\n$F = G \\times (M_1 M_2) / R^2$.\n\nVariation of \'g\' due to Earth\'s Shape:\nThe acceleration due to gravity (g) is related to the radius (R) of the Earth by the formula $g = GM/R^2$. Since $G$ and $M$ (mass of Earth) are constant, $g$ is inversely proportional to $R^2$. \n1. The Earth is not a perfect sphere; it is slightly flattened at the poles and bulges at the equator (oblate spheroid).\n2. Consequently, the radius of the Earth ($R_e$) at the equator is greater than the radius of the Earth ($R_p$) at the poles ($R_e > R_p$).\n3. Since $g$ is inversely related to $R^2$, where the radius is smaller (at the poles), the acceleration due to gravity ($g$) is greater, and vice versa. Thus, $g_{poles} > g_{equator}$.'),(7786,'5a10a3a0',3447,'Calculate:\n(i) The formula unit mass of Sodium Carbonate ($Na_2CO_3$).\n(ii) The mass of 0.2 moles of oxygen gas ($O_2$).\n[Given Atomic Masses: Na=23 u; C=12 u; O=16 u]','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','(i) Formula Unit Mass of $Na_2CO_3$:\nMass = (2 × Mass of Na) + (1 × Mass of C) + (3 × Mass of O)\nMass = (2 × 23 u) + (1 × 12 u) + (3 × 16 u)\nMass = 46 u + 12 u + 48 u\nFormula Unit Mass = 106 u.\n\n(ii) Mass of 0.2 moles of oxygen gas ($O_2$):\nMolar mass of $O_2$ = 2 × 16 g/mol = 32 g/mol.\nMass = Moles × Molar Mass\nMass = 0.2 mol × 32 g/mol\nMass = 6.4 g.'),(7787,'5a10a3a0',3448,'Describe the water cycle and explain the role of condensation and precipitation in it.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','The Water Cycle (Hydrologic Cycle) is the continuous movement of water on, above, and below the surface of the Earth. It involves several processes:\n1. Evaporation/Transpiration: Water turns into vapor and rises into the atmosphere.\n2. Condensation: Water vapor rises and cools down, forming tiny water droplets that aggregate to form clouds.\n3. Precipitation: The water droplets become too heavy and fall back to the Earth\'s surface as rain, snow, or hail.\n4. Runoff/Infiltration: Water flows across the land or seeps into the ground.\n\nRole of Condensation: Condensation is essential because it converts the gaseous water vapor back into liquid form (droplets) in the upper atmosphere, forming clouds. Without condensation, rain formation would not occur.\nRole of Precipitation: Precipitation returns the water stored in the atmosphere back to the lithosphere and hydrosphere, recharging groundwater, rivers, and oceans, thereby completing the cycle.'),(7788,'5a10a3a0',3449,'State Newton\'s Second Law of Motion. Derive the mathematical formulation of the Second Law (F=ma).','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','Newton’s Second Law of Motion states that the rate of change of momentum of an object is proportional to the applied unbalanced force in the direction of the force.\n\nDerivation of F = ma:\n1. Consider an object of mass $m$ with initial velocity $u$. A force $F$ is applied for time $t$, resulting in final velocity $v$.\n2. Initial Momentum ($P_1$) = $mu$.\n3. Final Momentum ($P_2$) = $mv$.\n4. Change in Momentum ($\\Delta P$) = $P_2 - P_1 = mv - mu = m(v - u)$.\n5. Rate of change of momentum = $\\Delta P / t = m(v - u) / t$.\n6. According to the Second Law, $F \\propto m(v - u) / t$.\n7. Since acceleration $a = (v - u) / t$, we substitute this into the proportion:\n$F \\propto ma$.\n8. By introducing a constant of proportionality $k$ (where $k=1$ in SI units), we get:\n$F = kma$\n$F = ma$.'),(7789,'5a10a3a0',3450,'Read the following passage and answer the questions:\n\nOrganisms are grouped based on evolutionary relationship and organization complexity. The Kingdom Monera includes prokaryotic organisms (lacking a defined nucleus) like bacteria, which show tremendous diversity in nutrition (autotrophic or heterotrophic). Protista, however, includes single-celled eukaryotic organisms. These may have structures like cilia or flagella for movement. Fungi are multicellular eukaryotes but are heterotrophic and have cell walls made of chitin, distinguishing them significantly from the Kingdom Plantae.','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','A. Prokaryotic organisms. B. Presence of a well-defined nucleus and membrane-bound organelles. C. Fungi are heterotrophic and lack chloroplasts, while Plantae are autotrophic and perform photosynthesis. Fungi cell walls are made of chitin, while Plantae cell walls are made of cellulose. D. Protista.'),(7790,'5a10a3a0',3451,'Read the following scenario and answer the questions:\n\nDriver X applies brakes suddenly upon seeing a stationary obstacle ahead. Due to the sudden application of brakes, the passengers in the bus lurch forward sharply. Furthermore, when the bus speeds up again, the bus driver observes that the necessary force required to accelerate the bus is much higher when the bus is fully loaded compared to when it is empty.','Case Study','Hard',4,'null','A. The passengers lurch forward due to inertia of motion (Newton\'s First Law). The passengers\' bodies tend to remain in the state of motion (moving forward) even when the bus (the external frame) stops. B. Mass is the measure of inertia. A heavier bus (fully loaded) has greater mass, hence greater inertia. C. According to Newton\'s Second Law (F=ma), if acceleration \'a\' is kept constant, a greater mass \'m\' requires a proportionally greater force \'F\'. D. Momentum is the product of mass and velocity ($p=mv$).'),(7791,'195f5708',3452,'Which state of matter has definite volume but no definite shape?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Solid\", \"Liquid\", \"Gas\", \"Plasma\"]','B'),(7792,'195f5708',3453,'The mass of one mole of Nitrogen atoms is:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"14 u\", \"28 g\", \"14 g\", \"14 kg\"]','C'),(7793,'195f5708',3454,'If a moving object suddenly stops, a person sitting inside tends to fall forward. This is due to:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Centripetal force\", \"Inertia of rest\", \"Inertia of motion\", \"Newton\'s Third Law\"]','C'),(7794,'195f5708',3455,'The powerhouse of the cell is:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Endoplasmic Reticulum\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Lysosome\", \"Nucleus\"]','B'),(7795,'195f5708',3456,'Which group of organisms possesses an open circulatory system and jointed appendages?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"Mollusca\", \"Annelida\", \"Arthropoda\", \"Nematoda\"]','C'),(7796,'195f5708',3457,'When a force of 1 N is applied to a body of 1 kg mass, the resulting acceleration is:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"1 m/s²\", \"10 m/s²\", \"9.8 m/s²\", \"0.1 m/s²\"]','A'),(7797,'195f5708',3458,'The cell wall of plants is primarily composed of  	.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Cellulose'),(7798,'195f5708',3459,'A heterogeneous mixture in which the solute particles do not settle down and are large enough to scatter light is called a 	.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Colloid'),(7799,'195f5708',3460,'The frequency of sound is measured in the unit 	.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Hertz (Hz)'),(7800,'195f5708',3461,'The amount of energy required to change 1 kg of a liquid to gas at atmospheric pressure at its boiling point is called the Latent heat of 	.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Vaporization'),(7801,'195f5708',3462,'Plant tissues responsible for increase in girth and primary growth are collectively known as 	 tissues.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Meristematic'),(7802,'195f5708',3463,'The maximum number of electrons that can be accommodated in the K shell of an atom is 	.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','2'),(7803,'195f5708',3464,'Calculate the number of moles for 52 g of Helium (He). (Atomic mass of He = 4 u).','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Molar mass of He = 4 g/mol.\nNumber of moles = Given mass / Molar mass\nNumber of moles = 52 g / 4 g/mol = 13 moles.'),(7804,'195f5708',3465,'Define Kinetic Energy. A body of mass 10 kg is moving with a velocity of 2 m/s. Calculate its Kinetic Energy.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Kinetic Energy (KE) is the energy possessed by a body due to its motion.\nFormula: KE = 1/2 * mv²\nGiven: m = 10 kg, v = 2 m/s\nKE = 1/2 * (10 kg) * (2 m/s)² = 1/2 * 10 * 4 = 20 J.\nThe Kinetic Energy is 20 Joules.'),(7805,'195f5708',3466,'State three differences between Tendon and Ligament.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','1. Tendons connect muscle to bone, while Ligaments connect bone to bone.\n2. Tendons are tough, fibrous, and possess great strength but limited flexibility.\n3. Ligaments are elastic and possess considerable flexibility to allow movement at joints.\n4. Tendons have closely packed parallel bundles of collagen fibres; Ligaments have less matrix and are primarily yellow elastic tissue.'),(7806,'195f5708',3467,'Explain Rutherford’s observation regarding the scattering of alpha particles in his experiment.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Rutherford observed three main points:\n1. Most alpha particles passed straight through the gold foil undeflected, indicating that most of the space inside the atom is empty.\n2. Some alpha particles were deflected by small angles, suggesting the presence of a positively charged body (nucleus).\n3. Very few (about 1 in 12,000) alpha particles rebounded, indicating that the positive charge and mass of the atom are concentrated in a very small volume.'),(7807,'195f5708',3468,'What is latent heat of fusion? Explain why the temperature of ice-water mixture remains constant at 0°C until all the ice melts.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Latent heat of fusion is the heat energy required to change 1 kg of a solid into liquid at atmospheric pressure at its melting point without any change in temperature.\nDuring melting, the heat supplied is used up in overcoming the forces of attraction between the particles of the solid (ice) instead of increasing the kinetic energy of the particles. Since the kinetic energy does not increase, the temperature remains constant.'),(7808,'195f5708',3469,'If the acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the Earth is 9.8 m/s², what will be the acceleration due to gravity (g) at a height equal to the radius of the Earth (R)?','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','The formula for acceleration due to gravity at height h is g\' = g [R / (R + h)]².\nGiven h = R (height is equal to the radius of the Earth).\ng\' = g [R / (R + R)]² = g [R / 2R]² = g (1/2)² = g/4.\nIf g = 9.8 m/s², then g\' = 9.8 / 4 = 2.45 m/s².'),(7809,'195f5708',3470,'Differentiate between Crystalline solids, Amorphous solids, and Colloids based on particle size, stability, and filtration method. Give one example of each.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Comparison Table:\n\n| Feature | True Solution (Crystalline/Homogeneous) | Colloids | Suspension (Amorphous/Heterogeneous) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Particle Size** | < 1 nm (Cannot be seen) | 1 nm to 100 nm (Invisible to naked eye) | > 100 nm (Visible to naked eye) |\n| **Nature/Stability** | Homogeneous and Stable | Heterogeneous, but appears homogeneous. Stable. | Heterogeneous and Unstable (particles settle) |\n| **Filtration** | Cannot be separated by filtration or ultrafiltration. | Pass through filter paper but can be separated by ultrafiltration. | Can be separated by simple filtration. |\n| **Appearance** | Transparent | Translucent | Opaque |\n| **Example** | Salt solution, Sugar in water | Milk, Starch solution, Blood | Muddy water, Chalk-water mixture |'),(7810,'195f5708',3471,'State the Law of Conservation of Energy. A machine does 1000 J of work in 10 seconds. Calculate the Power consumed. If the same machine performs 2000 J of work in 5 seconds, how does its power output change?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Law of Conservation of Energy: Energy can neither be created nor destroyed; it can only be transformed from one form to another. The total energy before and after transformation remains constant.\n\nCase 1:\nWork (W₁) = 1000 J\nTime (t₁) = 10 s\nPower (P₁) = W₁ / t₁ = 1000 J / 10 s = 100 W.\n\nCase 2:\nWork (W₂) = 2000 J\nTime (t₂) = 5 s\nPower (P₂) = W₂ / t₂ = 2000 J / 5 s = 400 W.\n\nChange in Power: The power output increases from 100 W to 400 W, representing a fourfold increase.'),(7811,'195f5708',3472,'Draw a neat, labeled diagram of a typical Plant Cell. List three cellular components present in a plant cell but absent in an animal cell.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','Diagram:\n[Self-Correction: Cannot generate image, but the answer requires a detailed drawing of a plant cell showing cell wall, large central vacuole, nucleus, mitochondria, chloroplasts, etc.]\n\nCellular components present in Plant Cells but absent in Animal Cells:\n1. Cell Wall (provides structural support)\n2. Chloroplasts (site of photosynthesis)\n3. Large Central Vacuole (stores water, maintains turgidity)'),(7812,'195f5708',3473,'What is relative molecular mass? Calculate the formula unit mass of Calcium Chloride (CaCl₂). (Given atomic masses: Ca = 40 u, Cl = 35.5 u). If you have 0.2 mole of water (H₂O), calculate the mass in grams. (H=1 u, O=16 u).','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Relative Molecular Mass (or Formula Unit Mass for ionic compounds) is the sum of the atomic masses of all atoms present in a molecule or a formula unit, expressed in atomic mass units (u).\n\n1. Formula Unit Mass of CaCl₂:\nMass of Ca = 1 x 40 u = 40 u\nMass of Cl = 2 x 35.5 u = 71 u\nTotal Formula Unit Mass = 40 u + 71 u = 111 u.\n\n2. Mass of 0.2 mole of water (H₂O):\nMolar mass of H₂O = (2 x 1) + 16 = 18 g/mol.\nMass = Number of moles × Molar mass\nMass = 0.2 mol × 18 g/mol = 3.6 g.\n\nThe mass of 0.2 mole of water is 3.6 grams.'),(7813,'195f5708',3474,'What are the characteristics of the Phylum Pisces (Fishes)? Classify five classes of Vertebrata, giving one example for each class.','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','Characteristics of Pisces (Fishes):\n1. They are cold-blooded (poikilotherms).\n2. Their skin is covered with scales/plates.\n3. They respire using gills.\n4. Their body is streamlined for movement in water.\n5. They have a two-chambered heart.\n\nClassification of Vertebrata (Five Classes):\n1. **Pisces:** Example: Shark, Tuna.\n2. **Amphibia:** Example: Frog, Salamander. (Adaptable to land and water, three-chambered heart).\n3. **Reptilia:** Example: Lizard, Snake. (Cold-blooded, lay eggs with tough coverings, usually crawl).\n4. **Aves:** Example: Pigeon, Sparrow. (Warm-blooded, four-chambered heart, possess feathers, forelimbs modified for flight).\n5. **Mammalia:** Example: Human, Whale. (Warm-blooded, four-chambered heart, possess mammary glands for milk production, generally give birth to live young).'),(7814,'195f5708',3475,'State Newton’s Universal Law of Gravitation. How does the value of \'G\' (Universal Gravitational Constant) differ from \'g\' (Acceleration due to gravity)? List any three applications or consequences of the Universal Law of Gravitation.','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','Newton’s Universal Law of Gravitation states that every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force that is directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between their centers.\n\nDifference between G and g:\n1. **Nature:** G is a universal constant; g is a variable vector quantity.\n2. **Value:** G has a constant value everywhere (6.673 x 10⁻¹¹ Nm²/kg²); g varies with height, depth, and location on Earth (approx. 9.8 m/s² on the surface).\n3. **Unit:** Unit of G is Nm²/kg²; Unit of g is m/s².\n\nApplications/Consequences:\n1. The force that binds us to the Earth.\n2. The motion of the Moon around the Earth.\n3. The motion of planets around the Sun.\n4. The cause of tides due to the Moon and the Sun.'),(7815,'195f5708',3476,'A student, Rahul, was observing the speed of a car driven by his father. The father drove the car for 40 minutes and covered a distance of 60 km. For the first 15 minutes, the car covered 20 km, and for the remaining time, it covered 40 km.\n\n(i) What was the total distance covered in meters?\n(ii) Calculate the average speed of the car in km/h.\n(iii) Was the car moving with uniform motion throughout the journey? Justify your answer.','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','(i) Total distance = 60 km. 60 km * 1000 m/km = 60,000 meters.\n(ii) Total time = 40 minutes = 40/60 hours = 2/3 hours (approx 0.67 h).\nAverage Speed = Total Distance / Total Time = 60 km / (2/3 h) = 60 * 3 / 2 = 90 km/h.\n(iii) No, the car was not moving with uniform motion. Uniform motion requires equal distances to be covered in equal intervals of time. In the first 15 minutes, speed = 20 km / 0.25 h = 80 km/h. In the next 25 minutes (40-15=25 min or 25/60 h), speed = 40 km / (25/60 h) = 96 km/h. Since the speed was changing, the motion was non-uniform.'),(7816,'195f5708',3477,'A biology teacher showed students two types of specialized cells: Cell A, which was elongated, multinucleated, and striated, and Cell B, which was highly elongated, with finger-like processes (dendrites) and a long tail (axon).\n\n(i) Identify Cell A and state its primary location.\n(ii) Identify Cell B and mention the specific function performed by its axon.\n(iii) What is the fundamental difference in the function of these two cells, related to movement and transmission?','Case Study','Easy',4,'null','(i) Cell A is a Skeletal Muscle Fibre (Striated Muscle). Primary location: Attached to bones, responsible for voluntary body movements.\n(ii) Cell B is a Neuron (Nerve Cell). The axon’s function is to transmit the nerve impulse away from the cell body towards the next neuron or muscle.\n(iii) Cell A (Muscle cell) is responsible for generating force and causing mechanical movement/contraction, while Cell B (Nerve cell) is responsible for rapid communication and transmission of electrical signals (impulses).'),(7817,'e0a73210',3478,'इलेक्ट्रॉन की खोज किसने की थी?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"जेम्स चैडविक\", \"ई. गोल्डस्टीन\", \"जे.जे. थॉमसन\", \"अर्नेस्ट रदरफोर्ड\"]','C'),(7818,'e0a73210',3479,'किसी वस्तु का चंद्रमा पर भार, पृथ्वी पर उसके भार का लगभग कितना गुना होता है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"1/2\", \"1/4\", \"1/6\", \"2 गुना\"]','C'),(7819,'e0a73210',3480,'शुष्क बर्फ क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"ठोस जल\", \"ठोस कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड\", \"ठोस नाइट्रोजन\", \"ठोस सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड\"]','B'),(7820,'e0a73210',3481,'पौधों में लचीलेपन (Flexibility) के लिए कौन सा ऊतक जिम्मेदार है?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"स्क्लेरेन्काइमा (Sclerenchyma)\", \"पैरेन्काइमा (Parenchyma)\", \"कोलेनकाइमा (Collenchyma)\", \"जाइलम (Xylem)\"]','C'),(7821,'e0a73210',3482,'जल (H₂O) का मोलर द्रव्यमान क्या है? (H=1 u, O=16 u)','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"16 ग्राम/मोल\", \"18 ग्राम/मोल\", \"17 ग्राम/मोल\", \"32 ग्राम/मोल\"]','B'),(7822,'e0a73210',3483,'विस्थापन का SI मात्रक क्या है?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"सेकंड\", \"मीटर प्रति सेकंड\", \"मीटर\", \"किलोग्राम\"]','C'),(7823,'e0a73210',3484,'कोशिका का \'पावर हाउस\' ___________ कहलाता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','माइटोकॉन्ड्रिया'),(7824,'e0a73210',3485,'दो या दो से अधिक पदार्थों का समांगी मिश्रण ___________ कहलाता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','विलयन (Solution)'),(7825,'e0a73210',3486,'ध्वनि तरंगें ___________ तरंगें होती हैं।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','यांत्रिक/अनुदैर्ध्य'),(7826,'e0a73210',3487,'गति के कारण किसी वस्तु में निहित ऊर्जा ___________ ऊर्जा कहलाती है।','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','गतिज'),(7827,'e0a73210',3488,'सरीसृप वर्ग के जंतुओं में हृदय सामान्यतः ___________ कक्षीय होता है।','Fill in the Blanks','Hard',1,'null','तीन (अपवाद: मगरमच्छ में चार)'),(7828,'e0a73210',3489,'वायुमंडल में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड की मात्रा लगभग ___________ प्रतिशत है।','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','0.03 से 0.04'),(7829,'e0a73210',3490,'वाष्पीकरण (Evaporation) को प्रभावित करने वाले किन्हीं तीन कारकों का उल्लेख कीजिए।','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','वाष्पीकरण को प्रभावित करने वाले तीन कारक:\n1. सतह का क्षेत्रफल: सतह का क्षेत्रफल बढ़ने पर वाष्पीकरण की दर बढ़ती है।\n2. तापमान: तापमान बढ़ने पर वाष्पीकरण की दर बढ़ती है।\n3. आर्द्रता: आर्द्रता (हवा में जल वाष्प की मात्रा) कम होने पर वाष्पीकरण की दर बढ़ती है।\n(अन्य कारक: वायु की गति)'),(7830,'e0a73210',3491,'निम्न यौगिकों के रासायनिक सूत्र लिखिए:\n(क) मैग्नीशियम क्लोराइड\n(ख) कैल्शियम ऑक्साइड\n(ग) अमोनियम सल्फेट','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','(क) मैग्नीशियम क्लोराइड: MgCl₂\n(ख) कैल्शियम ऑक्साइड: CaO\n(ग) अमोनियम सल्फेट: (NH₄)₂SO₄'),(7831,'e0a73210',3492,'जड़त्व (Inertia) को परिभाषित कीजिए और गति के प्रथम नियम से इसका संबंध स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','जड़त्व की परिभाषा: किसी वस्तु का वह गुण जिसके कारण वह अपनी विराम अवस्था या एकसमान गति की अवस्था में परिवर्तन का विरोध करती है, जड़त्व कहलाता है।\nसंबंध: न्यूटन की गति का प्रथम नियम (First Law of Motion) सीधे तौर पर जड़त्व की अवधारणा को व्यक्त करता है। यह नियम बताता है कि जब तक कोई बाहरी असंतुलित बल कार्य नहीं करता, वस्तु अपनी जड़त्व की स्थिति बनाए रखती है। इसलिए, गति के प्रथम नियम को जड़त्व का नियम भी कहा जाता है।'),(7832,'e0a73210',3493,'पादप कोशिका और जंतु कोशिका में कोई तीन अंतर लिखिए।','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','पादप कोशिका और जंतु कोशिका में तीन अंतर:\n| विशेषता | पादप कोशिका | जंतु कोशिका |\n|---|---|---|\n| कोशिका भित्ति | उपस्थित | अनुपस्थित |\n| प्लास्टिड (जैसे हरित लवक) | उपस्थित | अनुपस्थित |\n| रिक्तिका (Vacuole) | बड़ी, केंद्र में | छोटी या अनुपस्थित |\n| सेंट्रोसोम | अनुपस्थित | उपस्थित |'),(7833,'e0a73210',3494,'पैरेन्काइमा, कोलेनकाइमा और स्क्लेरेन्काइमा में उनके कार्य के आधार पर विभेद कीजिए।','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','1. पैरेन्काइमा: मुख्य कार्य भोजन का भंडारण और प्रकाश संश्लेषण करना। कोशिका भित्ति पतली होती है।\n2. कोलेनकाइमा: मुख्य कार्य पौधों को यांत्रिक सहायता और लचीलापन प्रदान करना। कोनों पर कोशिका भित्ति मोटी होती है।\n3. स्क्लेरेन्काइमा: मुख्य कार्य कठोरता और यांत्रिक शक्ति प्रदान करना (सुरक्षात्मक कार्य)। कोशिका भित्ति लिग्निन के कारण बहुत मोटी होती है, और कोशिकाएँ प्रायः मृत होती हैं।'),(7834,'e0a73210',3495,'निलंबन (Suspension) के कोई तीन गुणधर्म लिखिए।','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','निलंबन के तीन गुणधर्म:\n1. यह एक विषमांगी मिश्रण है।\n2. इसके कण आँखों से देखे जा सकते हैं।\n3. इसके कणों का आकार बड़ा (100 nm से अधिक) होता है।\n4. यह टिंडल प्रभाव (प्रकाश के पथ को फैलाना) दिखाता है।\n5. इसके कणों को छानने की विधि द्वारा मिश्रण से पृथक किया जा सकता है।'),(7835,'e0a73210',3496,'रदरफोर्ड के अल्फा कण प्रकीर्णन प्रयोग का वर्णन कीजिए। इस प्रयोग के प्रेक्षण और निष्कर्ष क्या थे?','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','रदरफोर्ड का अल्फा कण प्रकीर्णन प्रयोग:\nवर्णन: रदरफोर्ड ने रेडियोधर्मी स्रोत से निकलने वाले तीव्र गति के अल्फा कणों (धनावेशित कण) को एक बहुत पतली सोने की पन्नी (Gold Foil) पर टकराया। पन्नी के चारों ओर एक फ्लोरोसेंट स्क्रीन लगाई गई ताकि अल्फा कणों के विक्षेपण को देखा जा सके।\n\nप्रेक्षण (Observations):\n1. अधिकतर अल्फा कण सीधे पन्नी से होकर निकल गए।\n2. कुछ अल्फा कण छोटे कोणों से विक्षेपित हुए।\n3. बहुत कम कण (लगभग 12,000 में से 1) वापस 180 डिग्री के कोण पर लौट आए।\n\nनिष्कर्ष (Conclusions):\n1. परमाणु का अधिकांश भाग खोखला (रिक्त) होता है (क्योंकि अधिकांश कण सीधे निकल गए)।\n2. परमाणु का समस्त धनावेश और द्रव्यमान एक बहुत छोटे आयतन में केंद्रित होता है, जिसे नाभिक (Nucleus) कहते हैं (क्योंकि कुछ कण वापस लौट आए)।\n3. नाभिक का आयतन परमाणु के कुल आयतन की तुलना में बहुत कम होता है।'),(7836,'e0a73210',3497,'जंतु जगत के पाँच वर्गों (Classes) के नाम लिखिए और प्रत्येक का एक-एक उदाहरण देते हुए उनकी मुख्य विशेषताएँ बताइए।','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','जंतु जगत के प्रमुख पाँच वर्ग (कशेरुकी उप-संघ से):\n\n1. मत्स्य वर्ग (Pisces):\n   - मुख्य विशेषताएँ: त्वचा शल्कों (Scales) से ढकी होती है। श्वसन गलफड़ों (Gills) द्वारा होता है। ये असमतापी (शीतरक्त वाले) होते हैं।\n   - उदाहरण: रोहू, शार्क।\n\n2. उभयचर वर्ग (Amphibia):\n   - मुख्य विशेषताएँ: जल और थल दोनों जगह रह सकते हैं। हृदय तीन कक्षीय होता है। त्वचा चिकनी और नम होती है।\n   - उदाहरण: मेंढक, सैलामेंडर।\n\n3. सरीसृप वर्ग (Reptilia):\n   - मुख्य विशेषताएँ: ये रेंगकर चलते हैं। त्वचा सूखी और शल्कों वाली होती है। अंडे कठोर कवच वाले होते हैं। ये असमतापी होते हैं।\n   - उदाहरण: छिपकली, साँप, मगरमच्छ।\n\n4. पक्षी वर्ग (Aves):\n   - मुख्य विशेषताएँ: शरीर पर पंख होते हैं। दो पैर और उड़ने के लिए दो पंख होते हैं। हड्डियाँ खोखली (वायुकोश) होती हैं। ये समतापी (गरमरक्त वाले) होते हैं।\n   - उदाहरण: कबूतर, मोर।\n\n5. स्तनधारी वर्ग (Mammalia):\n   - मुख्य विशेषताएँ: त्वचा पर बाल होते हैं। दुग्ध ग्रंथियाँ (स्तन ग्रंथियाँ) उपस्थित होती हैं। ये अपने बच्चों को दूध पिलाते हैं। हृदय चार कक्षीय होता है और ये समतापी होते हैं।\n   - उदाहरण: मनुष्य, व्हेल, चमगादड़।'),(7837,'e0a73210',3498,'एक वस्तु विराम अवस्था से चलना शुरू करती है और 5 सेकंड में 20 m/s की गति प्राप्त करती है। वस्तु का त्वरण और 5 सेकंड में तय की गई दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','दिया गया है:\nप्रारंभिक वेग (u) = 0 m/s (विराम अवस्था)\nअंतिम वेग (v) = 20 m/s\nसमय (t) = 5 s\n\nI. त्वरण (a) ज्ञात करना:\nगति के प्रथम समीकरण से: v = u + at\n20 = 0 + a × 5\n5a = 20\nत्वरण (a) = 4 m/s²\n\nII. तय की गई दूरी (s) ज्ञात करना:\nगति के द्वितीय समीकरण से: s = ut + (1/2)at²\ns = (0 × 5) + (1/2) × 4 × (5)²\ns = 0 + (1/2) × 4 × 25\ns = 2 × 25\nतय की गई दूरी (s) = 50 मीटर।'),(7838,'e0a73210',3499,'मुक्त पतन (Free Fall) क्या है? \'g\' (गुरुत्वीय त्वरण) और \'G\' (सार्वत्रिक गुरुत्वाकर्षण स्थिरांक) में अंतर स्पष्ट कीजिए।','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','मुक्त पतन (Free Fall):\nजब कोई वस्तु केवल पृथ्वी के गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल के प्रभाव में गिरती है (हवा प्रतिरोध को नगण्य मानते हुए), तो उसकी गति को मुक्त पतन कहते हैं। मुक्त पतन के दौरान वस्तु में उत्पन्न त्वरण को गुरुत्वीय त्वरण \'g\' कहते हैं।\n\n\'g\' और \'G\' में अंतर:\n| विशेषता | गुरुत्वीय त्वरण (g) | सार्वत्रिक गुरुत्वाकर्षण स्थिरांक (G) |\n|---|---|---|\n| परिभाषा | यह वह त्वरण है जो किसी वस्तु में पृथ्वी के गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल के कारण उत्पन्न होता है। | यह दो इकाई द्रव्यमानों के बीच इकाई दूरी पर लगने वाला गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल है। |\n| मान | स्थान और ऊँचाई के अनुसार बदलता है। पृथ्वी की सतह पर इसका औसत मान 9.8 m/s² होता है। | इसका मान ब्रह्मांड में हर जगह स्थिर (Constant) रहता है। G ≈ 6.674 × 10⁻¹¹ Nm²/kg² |\n| मात्रक | मीटर प्रति सेकंड वर्ग (m/s²) | न्यूटन मीटर वर्ग प्रति किलोग्राम वर्ग (Nm²/kg²) |\n| प्रकृति | सदिश राशि (दिशा नीचे की ओर) | अदिश राशि |\n| निर्भरता | पृथ्वी के द्रव्यमान और त्रिज्या पर निर्भर करता है। | यह पिंडों के द्रव्यमान या दूरी पर निर्भर नहीं करता। |'),(7839,'e0a73210',3500,'जल चक्र (Water Cycle) का सचित्र वर्णन कीजिए और इसके प्रमुख चरणों को समझाइए।','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','जल चक्र वह प्रक्रिया है जिसके द्वारा पृथ्वी पर जल लगातार अपनी अवस्था बदलता रहता है और एक रूप से दूसरे रूप में संचरित होता रहता है। यह पृथ्वी पर जीवन के लिए आवश्यक है।\n\nप्रमुख चरण (चित्र आवश्यक):\n1. वाष्पीकरण (Evaporation): सूर्य की ऊर्जा के कारण जल निकायों (नदियों, समुद्रों) से जल वाष्प बनकर वायुमंडल में जाता है।\n2. संघनन (Condensation): जैसे-जैसे जलवाष्प ऊपर उठती है, वह ठंडी होकर छोटे जल कणों या बर्फ के क्रिस्टल में बदल जाती है, जिससे बादल बनते हैं।\n3. वर्षण (Precipitation): जब बादल में जल कण भारी हो जाते हैं और हवा उन्हें रोक नहीं पाती, तो वे वर्षा, बर्फ, ओले आदि के रूप में पृथ्वी की सतह पर गिरते हैं।\n4. संग्रह/अपवाह (Collection/Runoff): वर्षा का जल नदियों, झीलों और अंततः समुद्र में बह जाता है (अपवाह)। कुछ जल भूमि में रिसकर भूजल बन जाता है।\n\n(टिप्पणी: विद्यार्थी द्वारा जल चक्र का सरल आरेख बनाना अपेक्षित है।)'),(7840,'e0a73210',3501,'ऊर्जा संरक्षण के नियम (Law of Conservation of Energy) को लिखिए। उदाहरण देकर स्पष्ट कीजिए कि जब कोई वस्तु किसी ऊँचाई से स्वतंत्र रूप से गिरती है तो उसकी यांत्रिक ऊर्जा संरक्षित रहती है।','Long Answer','Easy',5,'null','ऊर्जा संरक्षण का नियम:\nइस नियम के अनुसार, ऊर्जा को न तो उत्पन्न किया जा सकता है और न ही नष्ट किया जा सकता है। इसे केवल एक रूप से दूसरे रूप में रूपांतरित किया जा सकता है। ब्रह्मांड की कुल ऊर्जा हमेशा स्थिर रहती है।\n\nऊँचाई से गिरती वस्तु में ऊर्जा संरक्षण का स्पष्टीकरण:\nमान लीजिए कि \'m\' द्रव्यमान की एक वस्तु को ऊँचाई \'h\' से स्वतंत्र रूप से गिराया जाता है। यांत्रिक ऊर्जा = गतिज ऊर्जा (K.E.) + स्थितिज ऊर्जा (P.E.)।\n\n1. प्रारंभिक बिंदु (शीर्ष पर, ऊँचाई h पर):\n   - वस्तु विराम में है, इसलिए गतिज ऊर्जा (K.E.) = 0।\n   - स्थितिज ऊर्जा (P.E.) = mgh (अधिकतम)।\n   - कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा = mgh।\n\n2. मध्य बिंदु (ऊँचाई x पर):\n   - वस्तु गति में है। P.E. कम (mgx) हो जाती है।\n   - स्थितिज ऊर्जा में कमी (mg(h-x)) गतिज ऊर्जा (K.E.) के रूप में परिवर्तित हो जाती है।\n   - कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा = K.E. + P.E. = mgh (अभी भी संरक्षित)।\n\n3. अंतिम बिंदु (जमीन को छूने से ठीक पहले):\n   - ऊँचाई (h) = 0, इसलिए P.E. = 0 (न्यूनतम)।\n   - गतिज ऊर्जा (K.E.) अधिकतम होती है। यह पूरी तरह से प्रारंभिक स्थितिज ऊर्जा (mgh) के बराबर होती है।\n   - कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा = K.E. + P.E. = mgh।\n\nनिष्कर्ष: वस्तु के गिरने के दौरान, स्थितिज ऊर्जा लगातार गतिज ऊर्जा में परिवर्तित होती रहती है, लेकिन किसी भी बिंदु पर कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा (स्थितिज + गतिज) समान रहती है। इस प्रकार, ऊर्जा संरक्षित रहती है।'),(7841,'75a7abf5',1,'The process in which a gas changes directly into liquid state without passing through the solid state is called:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Melting\", \"Sublimation\", \"Evaporation\", \"Condensation\"]','D'),(7842,'75a7abf5',2,'Which cell organelle is known as the \'Powerhouse of the cell\' because it produces ATP?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Nucleus\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Chloroplast\", \"Endoplasmic Reticulum\"]','B'),(7843,'75a7abf5',3,'If an object is taken from the Earth to the Moon, which of the following physical quantities will change?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Mass\", \"Density\", \"Volume\", \"Weight\"]','D'),(7844,'75a7abf5',4,'An atom of an element contains 6 protons and 6 neutrons. What is the mass number of this atom?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"6\", \"0\", \"12\", \"18\"]','C'),(7845,'75a7abf5',5,'The primary function of Xylem tissue in plants is the transport of:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Sugars and manufactured food\", \"Water and dissolved minerals from the roots\", \"Hormones synthesized in the shoot tip\", \"Amino acids only\"]','B'),(7846,'75a7abf5',6,'A body continues to be in its state of rest or uniform motion unless acted upon by an external force. This principle defines:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Law of conservation of energy\", \"Newton\'s First Law of Motion (Law of Inertia)\", \"Newton\'s Second Law of Motion\", \"Newton\'s Third Law of Motion\"]','B'),(7847,'75a7abf5',7,'Define acceleration and state its SI unit. If a bus starting from rest attains a speed of 30 m/s in 10 seconds, calculate its acceleration.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Acceleration is defined as the rate of change of velocity. Its SI unit is meter per second squared (m/s²).\nCalculation: Initial velocity (u) = 0 m/s. Final velocity (v) = 30 m/s. Time (t) = 10 s.\nAcceleration (a) = (v - u) / t = (30 - 0) / 10 = 3 m/s².'),(7848,'75a7abf5',8,'Briefly state the primary functions of two important cell organelles: (i) Ribosomes and (ii) Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum (SER).','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','(i) Ribosomes: They are the sites of protein synthesis (translation) in the cell.\n(ii) Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum (SER): It is crucial for the synthesis of lipids and steroids, and also plays a role in the detoxification of poisons and drugs in liver cells.'),(7849,'75a7abf5',9,'Differentiate between a True Solution and a Suspension based on (i) particle size and (ii) stability.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','True Solution vs. Suspension:\n(i) Particle Size: True solutions have particle sizes less than 1 nm, whereas Suspensions have particle sizes greater than 100 nm.\n(ii) Stability: True solutions are highly stable; the particles do not settle down. Suspensions are unstable; the particles settle down under gravity upon standing.'),(7850,'75a7abf5',10,'State Newton\'s Second Law of Motion. Give the mathematical relation derived from this law, and define the resulting unit of force.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Newton\'s Second Law states that the rate of change of momentum of an object is proportional to the applied unbalanced force in the direction of the force.\nMathematical relation: F = ma (Force = mass × acceleration).\nUnit of Force: The SI unit of force is the Newton (N). One Newton is defined as the force required to produce an acceleration of 1 m/s² in an object of mass 1 kg.'),(7851,'75a7abf5',11,'Explain why organisms like Viruses are often considered controversial or are excluded from R.H. Whittaker\'s Five Kingdom Classification system. Give two reasons.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Viruses are excluded because they do not display the characteristics of life until they enter a living cell, making them borderline between living and non-living.\n1. Non-cellular Structure: Viruses lack cellular machinery (like ribosomes or cytoplasm) and are essentially nucleic acid coated by protein, hence they do not fit into any kingdom based on cell structure.\n2. Obligate Parasitism: They can only reproduce by hijacking the metabolic machinery of a host cell. Outside a host, they are inert particles.'),(7852,'75a7abf5',12,'Describe the two major limitations of Rutherford\'s model of the atom concerning atomic stability. How did Niels Bohr attempt to overcome these limitations?','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Limitations:\n1. Stability of the Atom: According to classical electromagnetic theory, an electron revolving in a circular orbit should accelerate and radiate energy. This would cause the electron to spiral into the nucleus, leading to the collapse of the atom, which contradicts observations.\n2. Spectral Explanation: Rutherford’s model could not explain the characteristic line spectra observed for elements.\nBohr\'s Resolution: Bohr proposed that electrons revolve only in specific, fixed orbits (discrete energy levels) and that they do not radiate energy while orbiting in these fixed shells, thus ensuring atomic stability.'),(7853,'75a7abf5',13,'List any three general principles that are essential for the prevention of infectious diseases in a community.','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Three general principles of prevention:\n1. Providing public hygiene and clean surroundings (e.g., safe drinking water, proper waste disposal).\n2. Preventing exposure (e.g., maintaining social distancing, vector control).\n3. Strengthening the immune system through specific measures like vaccination (immunization).'),(7854,'75a7abf5',14,'Describe the critical role played by the bacterium Rhizobium in the Nitrogen Cycle and how this contributes to crop improvement.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Role of Rhizobium:\nRhizobium bacteria live symbiotically in the root nodules of leguminous plants (like peas and beans).\nCritical Role: They perform Nitrogen Fixation, the process of converting atmospheric nitrogen gas (N₂) into usable forms like nitrates and nitrites. Atmospheric N₂ cannot be directly utilized by plants.\nContribution to Crop Improvement: By fixing nitrogen, Rhizobium makes the soil naturally rich in nitrogen compounds, reducing the need for artificial fertilizers and enhancing crop productivity in leguminous crops.'),(7855,'52bc02a4',15,'Which of the following processes is responsible for the cooling effect when liquid evaporates?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Condensation\", \"Sublimation\", \"Latent heat of fusion\", \"Latent heat of vaporisation\"]','D'),(7856,'52bc02a4',16,'The powerhouse of the cell is:','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Ribosome\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Endoplasmic Reticulum\", \"Nucleus\"]','B'),(7857,'52bc02a4',17,'A body starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 2 m/s². What will be its velocity after 5 seconds?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"5 m/s\", \"10 m/s\", \"2 m/s\", \"20 m/s\"]','B'),(7858,'52bc02a4',18,'Calculate the molar mass of water (H₂O). (Given: Atomic masses H=1 u, O=16 u)','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"17 g/mol\", \"18 g/mol\", \"16 g/mol\", \"20 g/mol\"]','B'),(7859,'52bc02a4',19,'Which kingdom includes organisms that are eukaryotic, multicellular, and possess cell walls but cannot perform photosynthesis?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Monera\", \"Protista\", \"Fungi\", \"Plantae\"]','C'),(7860,'52bc02a4',20,'The maximum number of electrons that can be accommodated in the M shell (n=3) of an atom is:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"2\", \"8\", \"18\", \"32\"]','C'),(7861,'52bc02a4',21,'The value of acceleration due to gravity (g) is maximum at the _________ of the Earth.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Poles'),(7862,'52bc02a4',22,'The process of getting rid of unwanted plants (weeds) in the field is called _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Easy',1,'null','Weeding'),(7863,'52bc02a4',23,'Tissues that are responsible for the movement in our body are the _________ tissues.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Muscular'),(7864,'52bc02a4',24,'A substance is said to be a compound if it is composed of two or more elements chemically combined in a fixed _________.','Fill in the Blanks','Medium',1,'null','Ratio'),(7865,'52bc02a4',25,'Why does a person tending to jump out of a moving bus fall forward?','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','This is due to the Law of Inertia (Newton\'s First Law of Motion). When the person jumps, their entire body is initially moving forward with the velocity of the bus (Inertia of Motion). As their feet hit the ground, the feet stop, but the upper body continues to move forward due to inertia, causing the person to fall forward.'),(7866,'52bc02a4',26,'Define work done. Under what condition is the work done on an object zero?','Short Answer','Easy',3,'null','Work done is defined as the product of the force applied on an object and the displacement of the object in the direction of the force (W = F × d).\nWork done is zero under two main conditions:\n1. If the displacement (d) is zero (e.g., pushing a solid wall).\n2. If the force (F) is applied perpendicular (90°) to the direction of displacement (e.g., carrying a load horizontally).'),(7867,'52bc02a4',27,'Differentiate between tendon and ligament based on their structure and function.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Tendon:\n1. Connects muscle to bone.\n2. Made of white fibrous tissue; great strength but limited flexibility.\nLigament:\n1. Connects bone to bone.\n2. Made of yellow fibrous tissue; very elastic and flexible.'),(7868,'52bc02a4',28,'State the Law of Conservation of Mass. If 10g of Calcium Carbonate decomposes completely to give 4.4g of Carbon Dioxide, what mass of Calcium Oxide will be formed?','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Law of Conservation of Mass states that mass can neither be created nor destroyed in a chemical reaction. The total mass of reactants must equal the total mass of products.\nCalculation:\nReactants: Mass of CaCO₃ = 10 g\nProducts: Mass of CO₂ + Mass of CaO\nAccording to the law: 10 g = 4.4 g + Mass of CaO\nMass of CaO = 10 g - 4.4 g = 5.6 g.'),(7869,'52bc02a4',29,'Explain Rutherford’s major flaw in his nuclear model of the atom and how Niels Bohr addressed this flaw.','Short Answer','Hard',3,'null','Rutherford\'s flaw: His model predicted that electrons, revolving in circular orbits, would accelerate and, according to classical electromagnetic theory, should continuously emit energy. This energy loss would cause the electron to spiral into the nucleus, making the atom highly unstable. However, atoms are observed to be stable.\nBohr’s correction: Bohr proposed that electrons occupy specific, discrete orbits (stationary states) and, as long as they remain in these orbits, they do not radiate energy. They only absorb or emit energy when they jump between these fixed energy levels.'),(7870,'52bc02a4',30,'a) State the Universal Law of Gravitation. b) Derive the mathematical expression for this law. c) How is the value of \'G\' determined, and why is it known as the Universal Constant?','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','a) The Universal Law of Gravitation states that every object in the universe attracts every other object with a force which is directly proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.\nb) Derivation: Let M and m be the masses of two objects and r be the distance between their centres. According to the law:\n1. F ∝ M × m\n2. F ∝ 1 / r²\nCombining (1) and (2): F ∝ (M × m) / r²\nIntroducing the constant of proportionality G (Universal Gravitational Constant): F = G (M × m) / r².\nc) The value of G was experimentally determined by Henry Cavendish using a sensitive torsion balance apparatus. G is known as the Universal Constant because its value remains constant throughout the universe, regardless of the nature or size of the interacting bodies or the surrounding environment.'),(7871,'52bc02a4',31,'Draw a well-labelled diagram of an animal cell. Explain the structure and primary function of the Plasma Membrane and the Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER).','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','Diagram: Must show nucleus, plasma membrane, mitochondria, ER (rough and smooth), Golgi apparatus, cytoplasm, etc., clearly labelled.\nPlasma Membrane (Cell Membrane):\nStructure: Composed of a lipid bilayer in which proteins are embedded (fluid mosaic model). It is flexible and selectively permeable.\nFunction: It regulates the movement of substances into and out of the cell (selective permeability). It maintains the cell’s shape and provides protection.\nEndoplasmic Reticulum (ER):\nStructure: A large network of membrane-bound tubules and sheets. It exists as Rough ER (RER, having ribosomes) and Smooth ER (SER, lacking ribosomes).\nFunction: RER is the site for protein synthesis (due to ribosomes) and transport. SER is responsible for the synthesis of lipids, steroids, and detoxification of drugs/poisons.'),(7872,'52bc02a4',32,'a) Define the mole concept. b) Calculate the number of moles in 52 g of Helium gas (He). c) Calculate the mass of 0.5 mole of Nitrogen gas (N₂). (Atomic mass He = 4 u, N = 14 u; Avogadro Constant = 6.022 x 10²³ particles/mol).','Long Answer','Medium',5,'null','a) The mole is defined as the amount of substance that contains exactly 6.022 × 10²³ elementary entities (atoms, molecules, or ions). This number is the Avogadro constant.\nb) Calculation for Moles in 52 g He:\nMolar mass of He = 4 g/mol.\nNumber of moles = Given Mass / Molar Mass = 52 g / 4 g/mol = 13 moles.\nc) Calculation for Mass of 0.5 mole N₂:\nMolar mass of N₂ = 2 × 14 u = 28 g/mol.\nMass = Number of moles × Molar Mass = 0.5 mol × 28 g/mol = 14 g.'),(7873,'52bc02a4',33,'Describe the main steps involved in the Nitrogen Cycle. Explain the crucial role played by bacteria in this cycle.','Long Answer','Hard',5,'null','The Nitrogen Cycle involves four main steps:\n1. Nitrogen Fixation: Conversion of atmospheric nitrogen (N₂) into usable compounds like ammonia (NH₃) or nitrates. This is done primarily by certain bacteria (e.g., Rhizobium in root nodules or free-living blue-green algae).\n2. Ammonification: Conversion of complex organic nitrogen compounds (from dead plants/animals and waste) back into ammonia by decaying bacteria and fungi.\n3. Nitrification: Conversion of ammonia into nitrites by Nitrosomonas bacteria, and then nitrites are converted into nitrates by Nitrobacter bacteria. Plants absorb nitrogen mainly in the form of nitrates.\n4. Denitrification: Conversion of nitrates back into atmospheric nitrogen (N₂) by denitrifying bacteria (e.g., Pseudomonas), completing the cycle.\nCrucial Role of Bacteria: Bacteria are indispensable as they are the only organisms capable of performing nitrogen fixation (breaking the strong N₂ triple bond) and denitrification, thus controlling the flow of nitrogen between the atmosphere and the soil/living matter.'),(7874,'52bc02a4',34,'Match the items in Column A with the appropriate description/function in Column B.','Matching','Medium',3,'[{\"A\": \"Plastids\", \"B\": \"Protective tissue in plants\"}, {\"A\": \"Causative agent of AIDS\", \"B\": \"Gravity of the moon\"}, {\"A\": \"Sclerenchyma\", \"B\": \"Storage or photosynthesis in plant cells\"}]','Plastids - Storage or photosynthesis in plant cells; Causative agent of AIDS - Virus (HIV); Sclerenchyma - Protective tissue in plants (provides structural support and rigidity).'),(7875,'52bc02a4',35,'A sound wave emitted by a boat is detected by a microphone at the bottom of a lake. The time interval between the emission of the signal and its reception is 0.4 seconds. If the speed of sound in water is 1500 m/s, answer the following questions:\na) Name the phenomenon responsible for the signal returning to the detector. \nb) Calculate the depth of the lake at that point. \nc) What characteristic of the wave determines its loudness? \nd) If the frequency of the sound wave increases, how does it affect the pitch?','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','a) The phenomenon is Echo or Reflection of Sound.\nb) Calculation: Since the time given (0.4 s) is the round trip time (down and back up).\nDistance = Speed × Time = 1500 m/s × 0.4 s = 600 m.\nDepth of the lake (one way distance) = Total Distance / 2 = 600 m / 2 = 300 m.\nc) The loudness (or intensity) of a sound wave is determined by its Amplitude.\nd) If the frequency of the sound wave increases, the pitch increases (becomes sharper or shriller).'),(7876,'52bc02a4',36,'A farmer decides to diversify his income by starting practices that rely on both land and water resources. He plans to start integrated farming involving rearing fish in ponds and keeping beehives near his crops.\na) What is the scientific term for rearing fish on a large scale? \nb) State two differences between Composite Fish Culture and Capture Fishing. \nc) What advantage does the presence of beehives provide to the farmer’s crop production? \nd) Why is proper resource management crucial in integrated farming practices?','Case Study','Medium',4,'null','a) Pisciculture (or Aquaculture).\nb) Composite Fish Culture (CFC) involves culturing 5 or 6 species in a single pond, utilizing all food zones, and aims for high yield in closed systems. Capture fishing involves catching fish from natural water bodies (seas, rivers) where yields are unpredictable.\nc) Bees act as excellent pollinators. Their presence increases the efficiency of pollination of the crops, leading to better seed setting and higher overall yields.\nd) Proper resource management (e.g., managing nutrient runoff from fish waste to fertilize crops, or using agricultural waste as fish food) minimizes waste, optimizes resource utilization, and reduces environmental impact, making the system economically viable and sustainable.'),(7877,'343304e9',37,'When solid calcium oxide reacts vigorously with water, it produces calcium hydroxide and releases a large amount of heat. What type of chemical reaction is this?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Decomposition reaction\", \"Combination reaction\", \"Displacement reaction\", \"Double displacement reaction\"]','B'),(7878,'343304e9',38,'Which of the following is the energy currency for most cellular processes?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"DNA\", \"RNA\", \"ATP\", \"Glucose\"]','C'),(7879,'343304e9',39,'If two resistors, R1 and R2, are connected in parallel, how does their equivalent resistance (Req) compare to the individual resistances?','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"Req is always greater than both R1 and R2.\", \"Req is equal to R1 + R2.\", \"Req is always smaller than the smallest individual resistance.\", \"Req is equal to the average of R1 and R2.\"]','C'),(7880,'343304e9',40,'A solution turns red litmus paper blue. Its pH value is likely to be:','MCQ','Medium',1,'[\"2\", \"5\", \"7\", \"10\"]','D'),(7881,'343304e9',41,'A student uses a concave mirror to project the image of a candle flame on a screen. If the screen is moved closer to the mirror, the image size decreases. Where must the candle (object) currently be placed?','MCQ','Hard',1,'[\"At the focus (F)\", \"Between the pole (P) and focus (F)\", \"Between the center of curvature (C) and focus (F)\", \"Beyond the center of curvature (C)\"]','C'),(7882,'343304e9',42,'Which mode of reproduction is generally favored by organisms living in a stable environment?','MCQ','Easy',1,'[\"Sexual reproduction\", \"Fragmentation\", \"Budding\", \"Fission\"]','D'),(7883,'343304e9',43,'What are amphoteric oxides? Give one example of a metal oxide that exhibits this property.','Short Answer','Easy',2,'null','Amphoteric oxides are metal oxides that react with both acids and bases to produce salts and water. Example: Aluminium oxide (Al2O3) or Zinc oxide (ZnO).'),(7884,'343304e9',44,'State the role of the receptor and effector organs in the process of a reflex action.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','Receptors are structures (like specialized cells or sense organs) that detect the stimulus (change in environment) and convert it into a nerve impulse. Effectors are muscles or glands that receive the instruction from the central nervous system (via motor nerves) and carry out the appropriate response.'),(7885,'343304e9',45,'A current-carrying straight conductor experiences a force when placed in a uniform magnetic field. State the rule used to determine the direction of this force and list the three quantities related by this rule.','Short Answer','Medium',2,'null','The rule used to determine the direction of the force is Fleming\'s Left-Hand Rule. The three quantities related by this rule are: 1. Force (Thumb), 2. Magnetic Field Direction (Forefinger), 3. Direction of Current (Middle finger).'),(7886,'343304e9',46,'Explain why only about 10% of the energy is transferred to the next trophic level in a food chain.','Short Answer','Hard',2,'null','The energy transfer is limited to 10% because the remaining 90% of the energy is lost to the environment. This loss occurs primarily through metabolic processes of the organism at that level, such as respiration, digestion, movement, and heat loss to maintain body temperature. This makes food chains typically short (3-4 steps).'),(7887,'343304e9',47,'Draw the electron dot structure for Methane (CH4). Explain the type of bonding present in this molecule.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Electron Dot Structure: (The structure must show Carbon sharing 4 electrons with 4 Hydrogen atoms, resulting in 4 covalent bonds.) \nType of Bonding: Methane exhibits Covalent Bonding. This type of bonding is formed by the mutual sharing of valence electrons between the atoms (Carbon and Hydrogen) so that both achieve the stable noble gas configuration.'),(7888,'343304e9',48,'What is Myopia? State the two possible causes of this defect and suggest the type of lens required for its correction.','Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Myopia (Nearsightedness) is the eye defect where a person can see nearby objects clearly but cannot see distant objects distinctly. \nPossible Causes: 1. Excessive curvature of the eye lens. 2. Elongation of the eyeball. \nCorrection: It is corrected by using a concave lens (or diverging lens) of appropriate power. The concave lens diverges the incoming light rays slightly before they reach the eye lens, ensuring the image is formed correctly on the retina.'),(7889,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7890,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7891,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7892,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7893,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7894,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7895,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7896,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7897,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7898,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7899,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7900,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7901,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7902,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Short Answer','Medium',3,'null','Answer would depend on the specific topic.'),(7903,'b63e0773',NULL,NULL,'Shor